#: src/introduction.md:3
msgid "TinyBrains is a competition for small neural networks that play strategy games. Your goal is to **build the smallest brain that plays well**: choose what it sees, train it to make useful decisions, and find out how it performs against other competitors' models."
msgstr "TinyBrains 是一场让小型神经网络玩策略游戏的竞赛。你的目标是**构建一个尽可能小、又能打得好的大脑**：决定它看到什么，训练它做出有用的决策，再看看它与其他参赛者的模型对战时表现如何。"

#: src/introduction.md:7
msgid "You train and test your entry, then submit it to the arena. TinyBrains runs the matches and keeps the rankings, and you read the results and replays to decide what your next version should improve."
msgstr "你训练并测试自己的参赛模型，然后把它提交到竞技场。TinyBrains 负责进行对局并维护排名，你则通过结果和回放来决定下一个版本该改进什么。"

#: src/introduction.md:10
msgid "The first game: Ants"
msgstr "第一款游戏：Ants"

#: src/introduction.md:12
msgid "In **Ants**, your model commands a colony on a grid that wraps in both directions. Your ants explore, gather food to grow the colony, defend your hills and attack enemy hills. You see only the area around your living ants, and all players choose their moves at the same time."
msgstr "在 **Ants** 中，你的模型指挥一个蚁群，地图是一张在两个方向上都环绕的网格。你的蚂蚁要探索、采集食物以壮大蚁群、守卫自己的蚁丘并进攻敌方蚁丘。你只能看到存活蚂蚁周围的区域，而所有玩家同时选择各自的移动。"

#: src/introduction.md:16
msgid "Hills decide the score: you earn points for razing an enemy hill and lose one for each of your own hills you lose. Food and combat score nothing; they are how you get to the hills. A strong model balances exploration, growth, coordination and defence while it sees only part of what its opponents do."
msgstr "得分由蚁丘决定：摧毁一座敌方蚁丘可以得分，自己每失去一座蚁丘则扣一分。食物和战斗本身不计分，它们只是通往蚁丘的手段。强大的模型会在只能看到对手部分行动的情况下，兼顾探索、发展、协调和防御。"

#: src/introduction.md:21
msgid "Start with [Ants](games/ants.md) for the game overview, then read [the world](games/ants/world.md), [a turn](games/ants/turn.md) and [ending and scoring](games/ants/scoring.md)."
msgstr "先从 [Ants](games/ants.md) 了解游戏概览，再阅读[世界](games/ants/world.md)、[回合](games/ants/turn.md)和[结束与计分](games/ants/scoring.md)。"

#: src/introduction.md:26
msgid "A finished ladder match, replayed from its recorded actions by the cartridge that refereed it. The platform records one of these for every match on the ladder."
msgstr "一场已结束的天梯对局，由裁判它的那个卡带根据记录下来的动作重新回放。天梯上的每一场对局，平台都会记录这样一份回放。"

#: src/introduction.md:33
msgid "What you build"
msgstr "你要构建什么"

#: src/introduction.md:35
msgid "A version has two parts, which you submit together:"
msgstr "一个版本由两部分组成，二者一起提交："

#: src/introduction.md:37
msgid "**`model.onnx`**: your trained neural network, exported as ONNX."
msgstr "**`model.onnx`**：你训练好的神经网络，导出为 ONNX 格式。"

#: src/introduction.md:38
msgid "**`manifest.json`**: your graph's inputs and outputs, and one declarative **adapter** per input that turns the game's observation into that tensor."
msgstr "**`manifest.json`**：你的计算图的输入和输出，以及每个输入对应的一个声明式**适配器**，它把游戏的观测转换成对应的张量。"

#: src/introduction.md:41
msgid "The game defines [what your model can see](models/observation.md) and [the actions it can take](models/actions.md). You choose the tensor representation and the network architecture, and the [manifest](models/adapters.md) connects those choices to the game. You write it in JSONLogic with tensor operators, the expression engine the platform runs its own logic on. The referee owns the action side: it reads your policy head, so the channel order is a rule of the game and you write no program for it."
msgstr "游戏定义了[你的模型能看到什么](models/observation.md)和[它能采取哪些动作](models/actions.md)。张量表示和网络架构由你选择，而[清单](models/adapters.md)把这些选择和游戏连接起来。清单用带张量操作符的 JSONLogic 编写，这正是平台运行自身逻辑所用的表达式引擎。动作这一端归裁判负责：它直接读取你的策略头，所以通道顺序是游戏规则的一部分，你不需要为此编写任何程序。"

#: src/introduction.md:48
msgid "Size counts both files. **Your weight class is the two files' bytes, added together.** The platform compresses nothing, so no way of packing your weights into the file understates the total. An operation budget and a turn deadline also apply, and an entry has to fit its class and play within both. [Model format](models/format.md), [weight classes](models/weight-classes.md) and [limits and budgets](reference/limits.md) give the requirements."
msgstr "大小同时计入两个文件。**你的重量级由两个文件的字节数相加决定**。平台不做任何压缩，所以无论怎样把权重打包进文件，都无法少报总量。此外还有算子预算和回合时限，参赛模型既要符合自己的重量级，也要在这两项限制内完成对局。[模型格式](models/format.md)、[重量级](models/weight-classes.md)和[限制与预算](reference/limits.md)给出了具体要求。"

#: src/introduction.md:54
msgid "How to participate"
msgstr "如何参赛"

#: src/introduction.md:56
msgid "**Choose a season.** Read the game's season rules, eligibility requirements and submission window. Each version you submit belongs to one season."
msgstr "**选择一个赛季**。阅读该游戏赛季的规则、参赛资格要求和提交窗口。你提交的每个版本都属于一个赛季。"

#: src/introduction.md:58
msgid "**Learn the game and build your entry.** Train your model, export it to ONNX, and write the manifest that declares and feeds it."
msgstr "**学习游戏，构建参赛模型**。训练模型，导出为 ONNX，并编写清单来声明它的输入输出并为它提供数据。"

#: src/introduction.md:60
msgid "**Test before submitting.** The `tinybrains` CLI links the two libraries a node links, so it takes admission's measurements on your machine: the tensors your adapters build, what they charge, whether the graph accepts them, and a whole match through the real engine. See [testing before you submit](models/testing.md)."
msgstr "**提交前先测试**。`tinybrains` CLI 链接的正是节点所链接的那两个库，所以它能在你的机器上做出与审核相同的测量：你的适配器构建出的张量、它们的开销、计算图是否接受这些张量，以及用真实引擎完整地打一场对局。参见[提交前的测试](models/testing.md)。"

#: src/introduction.md:64
msgid "**Submit and upload.** Name your entry once, submit both hashes against it, and `PUT` `model.onnx` and `manifest.json` to the one-shot URLs the submission returns. See [submitting a version](competing/submitting.md)."
msgstr "**提交并上传**。先为参赛模型命名（只需一次），针对它提交两个文件的哈希，再把 `model.onnx` 和 `manifest.json` 用 `PUT` 上传到提交返回的一次性 URL。参见[提交版本](competing/submitting.md)。"

#: src/introduction.md:67
msgid "**Complete admission and the trial.** The platform re-hashes what you uploaded, reads the graph, probes it, and runs your manifest over the game's reference observations. A verified version then plays an unrated trial, and a version that passes becomes active and enters ranked matches."
msgstr "**通过审核和试赛**。平台会对你上传的文件重新计算哈希，读取计算图，对它进行探测，并在游戏的参考观测上运行你的清单。通过验证的版本随后会打一场不计评分的试赛，通过试赛的版本进入参赛中状态，开始参加排位对局。"

#: src/introduction.md:70
msgid "**Review and improve.** Find weaknesses in your match results, replays and rankings, and submit a new version while the season's submission window is open."
msgstr "**复盘并改进**。从对局结果、回放和排名中找出弱点，并在赛季的提交窗口开放期间提交新版本。"

#: src/introduction.md:73
msgid "The [trial](competing/trial.md) checks that your entry can play, and **you do not have to win it**: a completed trial passes if your version stays below the forfeit strike limit. If admission or the trial rejects your entry, read the reported reason and fix the problem before you submit again."
msgstr "[试赛](competing/trial.md)检查你的参赛模型能否正常比赛，而且**你不需要赢**：只要你的版本的判罚次数没有达到判负上限，打完的试赛就算通过。如果审核或试赛拒绝了你的作品，请阅读报告的原因，解决问题后再重新提交。"

#: src/introduction.md:77
msgid "How competition works"
msgstr "竞赛如何进行"

#: src/introduction.md:79
msgid "The matchmaker pairs active versions without any action from you. Each of your models has one rating, on the **Open ladder**, where models of every size compete. Your class ranking is your place on Open among models of your own size, so it shows how well you play within a size budget. Ratings come from match results, and the matchmaker picks opponents and maps to measure how strong each version is."
msgstr "配对器会自动为参赛中的版本配对，无需你做任何操作。你的每个模型都有一个评分，位于**无差别级天梯**上，各种大小的模型都在那里同场竞技。你的重量级排名就是你在无差别级天梯上、在同等大小的模型中的名次，因此它反映的是你在给定的大小预算内打得有多好。评分来自对局结果，配对器会挑选对手和地图来衡量每个版本的强弱。"

#: src/introduction.md:84
msgid "A new version that passes its trial replaces that model's previous active version in the same season, and the previous version can keep competing while the platform checks the candidate. [The life of a version](competing/version-life.md) covers promotion and withdrawal, and [ranking](competing/ranking.md) covers how ratings carry forward between versions."
msgstr "新版本通过试赛后，会替换该模型在同一赛季中原先参赛的版本；在平台检查候选版本期间，原版本可以继续参赛。[版本的生命周期](competing/version-life.md)介绍晋级和撤回，[排名](competing/ranking.md)介绍评分如何在版本之间延续。"

#: src/introduction.md:89
msgid "Play can continue past a season's submission deadline. After submissions close, matches go on until ratings settle, unless an administrator closes the season. Final standings stay available, and you enter a later season by submitting to it or re-entering a model as it stood. A game can run several seasons at once, some of them restricted to a class or a cohort. [Seasons](competing/seasons.md) has the full lifecycle."
msgstr "对局可以在赛季的提交截止后继续进行。提交截止后，对局会一直进行到评分稳定为止，除非管理员结束赛季。最终排名会一直保留；要参加之后的赛季，可以向它提交新版本，或者让模型按原样再次参赛。一款游戏可以同时运行多个赛季，其中一些只对某个重量级或某个团体开放。[赛季](competing/seasons.md)有完整的生命周期说明。"

#: src/introduction.md:94
msgid "Start here"
msgstr "从这里开始"

#: src/introduction.md:96
msgid "This book is for competitors who build and enter models. Follow the [quickstart](quickstart.md) for the entry sequence, or begin with [Ants](games/ants.md) for the decisions your model has to make. As you iterate, [matches](competing/matches.md) and [replays](competing/replays.md) show how your versions play, and the reference chapters give exact requirements and rejection reasons."
msgstr "本指南面向构建并提交模型的参赛者。按照[快速上手](quickstart.md)走一遍参赛流程，或者先从 [Ants](games/ants.md) 了解你的模型需要做出哪些决策。在迭代过程中，[对局](competing/matches.md)和[回放](competing/replays.md)展示你的各个版本如何比赛，参考章节则给出精确的要求和拒绝原因。"

#: src/quickstart.md:3
msgid "Your first target is a version that completes a trial and enters the ladder. Start with a simple model whose inputs and outputs you understand, then use match results to improve its decisions."
msgstr "你的第一个目标是做出一个能完成试赛并登上天梯的版本。先从一个你清楚其输入和输出的简单模型开始，再用对局结果来改进它的决策。"

#: src/quickstart.md:6 src/platform/running-locally.md:8
msgid "What you need"
msgstr "你需要准备什么"

#: src/quickstart.md:8
msgid "You need an account with one of the site's sign-in providers (the sign-in page lists them), a way to train and export an ONNX model, and a manifest for Ants. The platform uses the provider for signing you in and nothing else. Your public handle is taken from your login there the first time you sign in, and stays the same if you later rename yourself at the provider. Check the game's [seasons](competing/seasons.md) before you prepare an entry: a submission has to arrive inside a season's open window, and a restricted season admits only its participants."
msgstr "你需要一个本站登录服务商的账户（登录页面列出了所有服务商）、一种训练并导出 ONNX 模型的方法，以及一份 Ants 的清单。平台只用服务商来让你登录，别无他用。你的公开用户名取自你第一次登录时在服务商那里的登录名，之后即使你在服务商那里改名，它也保持不变。准备参赛模型之前，先查看该游戏的[赛季](competing/seasons.md)：提交必须落在某个赛季的开放窗口之内，而受限赛季只允许它的参与者参赛。"

#: src/quickstart.md:15
msgid "The `tinybrains` command-line tool plays matches, runs admission's checks, and exposes the real cartridge as a [training environment](models/testing.md#train-against-the-real-engine), so your training loop drives the same engine the ladder plays. [Installing it](models/testing.md#the-tinybrains-cli) takes one `brew install` or a release download. You do not need to run the platform to enter a hosted competition."
msgstr "`tinybrains` 命令行工具可以进行对局、运行审核的各项检查，并把真实卡带暴露为一个[训练环境](models/testing.md#train-against-the-real-engine)，这样你的训练循环驱动的就是天梯所用的同一个引擎。[安装它](models/testing.md#the-tinybrains-cli)只需一条 `brew install`，或者下载一个发布版本。参加托管的竞赛不需要你自己运行平台。"

#: src/quickstart.md:21
msgid "The short way: start from a working entry"
msgstr "捷径：从一份可用的参赛模型开始"

#: src/quickstart.md:23
msgid "[**`Tiny-Brains/ants-starter`**](https://github.com/Tiny-Brains/ants-starter) is a trained **nano** entry that admission accepts unchanged. It comes with its generated manifest, the `metrics.json` and `card.md` the platform measures, two match files, and a CI workflow that re-checks it on every push."
msgstr "[**`Tiny-Brains/ants-starter`**](https://github.com/Tiny-Brains/ants-starter) 是一份训练好的 **nano** 参赛模型，原样提交就能通过审核。它附带生成好的清单、平台会测量的 `metrics.json` 和 `card.md`、两个对局文件，以及一个在每次推送时重新检查它的 CI 工作流。"

#: src/quickstart.md:29 src/quickstart.md:30
msgid "# once\n"
msgstr "# 只需一次\n"

#: src/quickstart.md:33
msgid "# what admission will say\n"
msgstr "# 审核会给出的结论\n"

#: src/quickstart.md:34
msgid "# play it against itself, through the real engine\n"
msgstr "# 用真实引擎让它和自己对战\n"

#: src/quickstart.md:35
msgid "# the training code, from the ants repository\n"
msgstr "# 训练代码，来自 ants 仓库\n"

#: src/quickstart.md:36
msgid "# retrain it: about an hour\n"
msgstr "# 重新训练它：大约一小时\n"

#: src/quickstart.md:39
msgid "Submit it as it is to watch the whole loop end to end, then change something and retrain. It was trained with its own seed, so the ladder takes it as a new entry, and `models/` beside it holds three trained opponents to play it against."
msgstr "先原样提交它，完整地看一遍整个流程，然后改点什么再重新训练。它是用自己的种子训练的，所以天梯会把它当作一份新的参赛模型；旁边的 `models/` 目录里有三个训练好的对手可以陪它练习。"

#: src/quickstart.md:43
msgid "The long way"
msgstr "完整流程"

#: src/quickstart.md:45
msgid "1. Train something small"
msgstr "1. 训练一个小模型"

#: src/quickstart.md:47
msgid "Read [Ants](games/ants.md), then decide how to represent the [observation](models/observation.md). For example, a spatial model can take planes for your ants, visible enemies, food and known water, and produce five move scores per ant or per board square."
msgstr "先阅读 [Ants](games/ants.md)，再决定如何表示[观测](models/observation.md)。例如，一个空间模型可以用几个平面分别表示你的蚂蚁、可见的敌人、食物和已知的水域，然后为每只蚂蚁或每个地图格子输出五个移动得分。"

#: src/quickstart.md:51
msgid "Train on the information the arena supplies, and against the same engine if you can: [`tinybrains env`](models/testing.md#train-against-the-real-engine) drives it from Python, so you never write the rules a second time. Export to `model.onnx` with named tensor inputs and outputs for your manifest to name. Check the [model requirements](models/format.md) and [size classes](models/weight-classes.md) before you commit to an architecture; a graph that exports can still fail admission."
msgstr "用竞技场提供的信息来训练，条件允许的话就直接对着同一个引擎训练：[`tinybrains env`](models/testing.md#train-against-the-real-engine) 可以从 Python 驱动它，这样你永远不用把规则再写一遍。导出为 `model.onnx` 时，给输入和输出张量命名，以便在清单中引用。在确定架构之前，先查看[模型要求](models/format.md)和[重量级](models/weight-classes.md)；能导出的计算图仍然可能通不过审核。"

#: src/quickstart.md:58
msgid "2. Write the manifest"
msgstr "2. 编写清单"

#: src/quickstart.md:60
msgid "Create `manifest.json`. It declares each of your graph's inputs and outputs by name, dtype and shape, and carries one **adapter** per input: a small program that turns the observation into that tensor. A dimension may be a _name_, so one entry plays every board size."
msgstr "创建 `manifest.json`。它按名称、dtype 和形状声明你的计算图的每个输入和输出，并为每个输入附带一个**适配器**：一个把观测转换成对应张量的小程序。维度可以是一个<em>名称</em>，这样同一份参赛模型就能在任何地图尺寸上比赛。"

#: src/quickstart.md:64
msgid "The referee reads your policy head, in a channel order the game publishes ([why](models/adapters.md#why-you-do-not-write-the-head)), so the output side needs no program of yours. [The manifest](models/adapters.md) has a complete small example, and [a real manifest, piece by piece](models/adapters/walkthrough.md) walks through one that plays."
msgstr "裁判按游戏公布的通道顺序读取你的策略头（[为什么](models/adapters.md#why-you-do-not-write-the-head)），所以输出端不需要你编写任何程序。[清单](models/adapters.md)一章有一个完整的小例子，[逐段解读一份真实清单](models/adapters/walkthrough.md)则逐段讲解一份真正能比赛的清单。"

#: src/quickstart.md:69
msgid "Run the pair through [local checks](models/testing.md). Exercise every basic board (two seats to eight, 24 to 124 a side), empty lists, large colonies and fragmented known-water masks. Check that execution returns, and check the operation counts and the actions it produced as well."
msgstr "用[本地检查](models/testing.md)跑一遍这两个文件。把每张基础地图（2 到 8 个席位，每边 24 到 124 格）、空列表、大蚁群和支离破碎的已知水域掩码都试一遍。确认执行能够返回，并检查运算次数和它产生的动作。"

#: src/quickstart.md:73
msgid "3. Hash the two files, or let the site do it"
msgstr "3. 计算两个文件的哈希，或者交给网站"

#: src/quickstart.md:75
msgid "Keep the exact names `model.onnx` and `manifest.json`: the platform mints the upload URLs for those names. **If you submit through the site, skip this step**: `/submit` hashes both files in your browser. To hash them yourself, compute SHA-256 over those exact bytes:"
msgstr "文件名必须严格是 `model.onnx` 和 `manifest.json`：平台会为这两个名字签发上传 URL。**如果你通过网站提交，可以跳过这一步**：`/submit` 页面会在浏览器中计算两个文件的哈希。要自己计算，就对这些字节原样计算 SHA-256："

#: src/quickstart.md:80
msgid "# Linux\n"
msgstr "# Linux\n"

#: src/quickstart.md:82
msgid "# macOS\n"
msgstr "# macOS\n"

#: src/quickstart.md:87
msgid "Do not change the files after you hash them. The submission carries `sha256:` followed by each file's 64 hexadecimal digits."
msgstr "计算哈希之后不要再改动文件。提交时写的是 `sha256:` 后接每个文件的 64 位十六进制哈希值。"

#: src/quickstart.md:90
msgid "4. Create the model, then submit to it"
msgstr "4. 创建模型，再向它提交"

#: src/quickstart.md:92
msgid "Sign in, make the model with the New model form on your profile, and **the site's `/submit` form does the rest for you**: pick the model, pick the two files, press the button. The form hashes the files in your browser and uploads them straight to the object store, so it does step 3 for you."
msgstr "登录后，在个人主页上用“新建模型”表单创建模型，**剩下的交给网站的 `/submit` 表单**：选择模型，选择两个文件，按下按钮。表单会在你的浏览器中计算文件哈希，并把它们直接上传到对象存储，也就是替你完成了第 3 步。"

#: src/quickstart.md:96
msgid "Through the API it takes two calls. A model is your entry: a name, and every version you enter under it. Create it once:"
msgstr "通过 API 则需要两次调用。模型就是你的参赛模型：一个名字，加上你在它名下提交的每个版本。创建它只需一次："

#: src/quickstart.md:101 src/models/adapters.md:39 src/models/adapters.md:43 src/models/adapters.md:44 src/models/adapters.md:133 src/models/adapters.md:136 src/models/adapters.md:149 src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:33 src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:34 src/models/memory.md:24 src/models/memory.md:25 src/models/memory.md:58 src/models/memory.md:81
msgid "\"name\""
msgstr "\"name\""

#: src/quickstart.md:101
msgid "\"First try\""
msgstr "\"First try\""

#: src/quickstart.md:104
msgid "The response carries a `model_id`. Submit the version against it:"
msgstr "响应中带有 `model_id`。针对它提交版本："

#: src/quickstart.md:109 src/models/testing.md:165 src/reference/api.md:210 src/platform/adding-a-game.md:153
msgid "\"game\""
msgstr "\"game\""

#: src/quickstart.md:109 src/models/testing.md:165 src/reference/api.md:210 src/platform/adding-a-game.md:153
msgid "\"ants\""
msgstr "\"ants\""

#: src/quickstart.md:110 src/reference/api.md:211
msgid "\"season\""
msgstr "\"season\""

#: src/quickstart.md:110
msgid "\"<the season's slug; left out, the featured season>\""
msgstr "\"<赛季的 slug；省略则为精选赛季>\""

#: src/quickstart.md:111 src/reference/api.md:212
msgid "\"model\""
msgstr "\"model\""

#: src/quickstart.md:111
msgid "\"<the model_id from above>\""
msgstr "\"<上面返回的 model_id>\""

#: src/quickstart.md:112 src/reference/api.md:213
msgid "\"weights_hash\""
msgstr "\"weights_hash\""

#: src/quickstart.md:112
msgid "\"sha256:<64 hex digits for model.onnx>\""
msgstr "\"sha256:<64 位十六进制哈希，对应 model.onnx>\""

#: src/quickstart.md:113 src/reference/api.md:214
msgid "\"manifest_hash\""
msgstr "\"manifest_hash\""

#: src/quickstart.md:113
msgid "\"sha256:<64 hex digits for manifest.json>\""
msgstr "\"sha256:<64 位十六进制哈希，对应 manifest.json>\""

#: src/quickstart.md:117
msgid "Replace the placeholder hashes with your own. Save the returned `version_id`. The platform assigns the version number, and this first one is v1."
msgstr "把占位的哈希替换成你自己的。保存返回的 `version_id`。版本号由平台分配，第一个版本是 v1。"

#: src/quickstart.md:120
msgid "**The `201` response carries two one-shot upload URLs**, and nothing happens until you use them:"
msgstr "**`201` 响应中带有两个一次性上传 URL**，在你使用它们之前什么都不会发生："

#: src/quickstart.md:123
msgid "\"$MODEL_URL\"       # upload.model_onnx\n"
msgstr "\"$MODEL_URL\"       # 对应 upload.model_onnx\n"

#: src/quickstart.md:124
msgid "\"$MANIFEST_URL\"    # upload.manifest_json\n"
msgstr "\"$MANIFEST_URL\"    # 对应 upload.manifest_json\n"

#: src/quickstart.md:127
msgid "The platform stores no bytes of its own and downloads nothing from you, so it rejects a version whose bucket is empty with `ARTIFACT_MISSING`. It re-hashes what arrives and compares it with what you declared. [Submitting](competing/submitting.md) covers session usage and error handling, and [Models and versions](competing/models.md) explains the two separate calls."
msgstr "平台自己不保存任何字节，也不从你那里下载任何东西，所以存储桶为空的版本会以 `ARTIFACT_MISSING` 被拒绝。它会对收到的文件重新计算哈希，并与你声明的值比较。[提交版本](competing/submitting.md)介绍会话的使用和错误处理，[模型与版本](competing/models.md)解释为什么是两次独立的调用。"

#: src/quickstart.md:132
msgid "5. Watch the trial"
msgstr "5. 观看试赛"

#: src/quickstart.md:134
msgid "Watch it on the version's page, or read `GET /v1/me/versions/{version_id}`, which shows you your own version in any state. Its `phase` tells waiting for verification apart from waiting for a trial. A version that passes admission becomes `verified`, then `active` after a successful trial. **You can lose the trial and still pass**, and a forfeit fails it. The trial checks that your version can play, and it never changes ratings."
msgstr "在版本页面上观看，或者读取 `GET /v1/me/versions/{version_id}`，它会显示你自己的版本，无论处于什么状态。它的 `phase` 区分“等待验证”和“等待试赛”。通过审核的版本变为 `verified`，试赛成功后变为 `active`**。试赛输了也能通过**，但被判负则不通过。试赛只检查你的版本能否正常比赛，它从不改变评分。"

#: src/quickstart.md:140
msgid "A rejection carries `reject_reason`. Fix the named issue, validate again, and submit the corrected files as the next version. If the version is still waiting, check its phase and trial status before you submit to the same model again: each model can have one candidate in flight. You can submit to another of your models in the meantime."
msgstr "被拒绝时会附带 `reject_reason`。修复指出的问题，重新验证，再把修正后的文件作为下一个版本提交。如果版本仍在等待，再次向同一个模型提交之前，先查看它的阶段和试赛状态：每个模型同一时间只能有一个候选版本在进行中。在此期间你可以向自己的其他模型提交。"

#: src/quickstart.md:145
msgid "If you get stuck"
msgstr "遇到问题"

#: src/quickstart.md:147
msgid "Ask on [Discord](https://discord.gg/xr9Z2mSkxr), where competitors and the people who run the platform talk. Bring the version's id and its `reject_reason`, or the match's id: those are what anyone helping you will look up first. The source of every part is on [GitHub](https://github.com/Tiny-Brains)."
msgstr "到 [Discord](https://discord.gg/xr9Z2mSkxr) 提问，参赛者和平台的运营者都在那里交流。带上版本的 id 和它的 `reject_reason`，或者对局的 id：帮你的人首先要查的就是这些。每个部分的源代码都在 [GitHub](https://github.com/Tiny-Brains) 上。"

#: src/quickstart.md:152
msgid "Where to go next"
msgstr "接下来读什么"

#: src/quickstart.md:154
msgid "[Matches](competing/matches.md), [replays](competing/replays.md) and [ranking](competing/ranking.md) explain your first results. Improve one behavior at a time, and enter another version while the submission window is open. A model's active version keeps competing while the platform tests its replacement, and your other models keep playing the whole time."
msgstr "[对局](competing/matches.md)、[回放](competing/replays.md)和[排名](competing/ranking.md)解释你的最初几场结果。每次只改进一种行为，并趁提交窗口开放再提交一个版本。平台测试替代版本期间，模型当前参赛的版本会继续比赛，你的其他模型也始终在比赛。"

#: src/quickstart.md:159
msgid "**Replay visualiser (planned):** one admitted entry's trial, marking its first food collection, a fight and the final result, with the candidate's view beside the full replay."
msgstr "**回放可视化（计划中**）：一份通过审核的参赛模型的试赛，标出它第一次采集食物、一次战斗和最终结果，并在完整回放旁边显示候选版本的视角。"

#: src/games/ants.md:3
msgid "Ants is a simultaneous-turn strategy game between colonies on a wrapping grid. You control every ant in your colony through one model call each turn. A board seats from two players to eight, and each season plays boards of its own."
msgstr "Ants 是一款同时行动的回合制策略游戏，多个蚁群在一张环绕的网格上对抗。每个回合，你通过一次模型调用控制蚁群中的每一只蚂蚁。一张地图可容纳 2 到 8 名玩家，每个赛季使用自己的地图。"

#: src/games/ants.md:7
msgid "The idea"
msgstr "基本思路"

#: src/games/ants.md:9
msgid "Grow a colony, find the opponent, and raze its hills while protecting yours. Razing an enemy hill scores **+2**; losing a hill costs **−1**. Gathering food, killing ants and controlling territory score nothing on their own."
msgstr "壮大蚁群，找到对手，摧毁它的蚁丘，同时守住自己的。摧毁一座敌方蚁丘得 **+2** 分；失去一座蚁丘扣 **−1** 分。采集食物、击杀蚂蚁和控制领土本身都不计分。"

#: src/games/ants.md:13
msgid "Growth matters for what it lets you do at the hills. A large army can defend and scout, and you can still lose a match on an unguarded hill before that army reaches the opponent."
msgstr "发展之所以重要，在于它让你在蚁丘上能做的事。一支大军既能防守也能侦察，但在这支大军抵达对手之前，你仍可能因为一座无人防守的蚁丘而输掉对局。"

#: src/games/ants.md:16
msgid "What you command"
msgstr "你指挥什么"

#: src/games/ants.md:18
msgid "Each living ant can move one square north, east, south or west, or stay where it is. All players choose before any move resolves. Your adapters turn each [observation](../models/observation.md) into your graph's inputs, and the referee reads your graph's policy head to build the [action](../models/actions.md): one order per ant, in the observation's order."
msgstr "每只存活的蚂蚁可以向北、东、南或西移动一格，或者留在原地。所有玩家先做出选择，然后移动才一起结算。你的适配器把每份[观测](../models/observation.md)转换成计算图的输入，裁判则读取计算图的策略头来构建[动作](../models/actions.md)：每只蚂蚁一条指令，顺序与观测中的顺序一致。"

#: src/games/ants.md:23
msgid "Ants that end their move on the same square die, friendly ants included. Survivors fight according to how many enemies are near them, then can raze hills or gather food. Gathered food goes into a shared hive, and the engine turns it into new ants on free hills on a later turn. Read [A turn](ants/turn.md) before you design movement and combat."
msgstr "移动后停在同一格的蚂蚁会死亡，友军也不例外。幸存者根据周围敌人的数量进行战斗，然后可以摧毁蚁丘或采集食物。采集到的食物进入共享的蚁巢，引擎会在之后的回合把它变成空闲蚁丘上的新蚂蚁。在设计移动和战斗之前，先阅读[回合](ants/turn.md)。"

#: src/games/ants.md:28
msgid "What you can see"
msgstr "你能看到什么"

#: src/games/ants.md:30
msgid "Your living ants give you vision, and you see enemies, food and standing hills only inside it. Water you have discovered stays in your observations, and there is no explored-land mask. Anything else your model wants to remember goes in its [memory](../models/memory.md), when the season's class allows one. [The world](ants/world.md) explains wrapping and fog."
msgstr "视野来自你存活的蚂蚁，敌人、食物和尚存的蚁丘只有在视野之内你才能看到。你已发现的水域会一直留在观测中，但没有“已探索陆地”掩码。模型想记住的其他任何东西都要放进它的[记忆](../models/memory.md)，前提是赛季的重量级允许记忆。[世界](ants/world.md)解释环绕和迷雾。"

#: src/games/ants.md:35 src/games/ants/scoring.md:40
msgid "How a match ends"
msgstr "对局如何结束"

#: src/games/ants.md:37
msgid "A match ends at its turn limit, when one colony or none has ants left, when the ranking is decided, or at a stalemate cutoff. The highest hill score wins, and equal scores tie. A colony left as the lone survivor also scores the enemy hills still standing. [Ending and scoring](ants/scoring.md) covers these rules and forfeits, which the platform handles apart from the game score."
msgstr "对局在以下情况结束：达到回合上限、只剩一个蚁群或没有蚁群还有蚂蚁、名次已经确定，或者触发僵局截止。蚁丘得分最高者获胜，得分相同则平局。作为唯一幸存者的蚁群，还能把仍然矗立的敌方蚁丘计入得分。[结束与计分](ants/scoring.md)介绍这些规则以及判负，判负由平台处理，与游戏得分无关。"

#: src/games/ants.md:45
msgid "**Each season has its own boards**, and no release carries them. An admin uploads them to the season, where they are public as soon as they arrive, and can put a board into play or take one out while the season runs. Every board fits the game's limits (two to eight seats, 24 to 124 squares a side, at most 14,880 squares) and uses the same movement, vision, combat and scoring rules. The release ships five **basic boards**, one of each size, which span those limits; you test against them on your machine. [The maps](ants/maps.md) shows them, lists what every board guarantees, and says where to find a season's boards."
msgstr "**每个赛季都有自己的地图**，发布版本中不包含它们。管理员把地图上传到赛季，上传后立即公开，并且可以在赛季进行期间随时启用或停用某张地图。每张地图都符合游戏的限制（2 到 8 个席位，每边 24 到 124 格，最多 14,880 格），并使用相同的移动、视野、战斗和计分规则。发布版本附带五张**基础地图**，每种尺寸一张，覆盖了这些限制的范围；你在自己的机器上用它们测试。[地图](ants/maps.md)展示这些地图，列出每张地图都保证的条件，并说明去哪里找赛季的地图。"

#: src/games/ants.md:53
msgid "Where the rules are exact"
msgstr "规则的精确出处"

#: src/games/ants.md:55
msgid "The chapters that follow describe the current Ants cartridge. Its source and rule tests are in the Ants repository listed under [repositories](../platform/repositories.md). Each match record names the engine that played it, and the viewer has to reconstruct a replay with that engine version."
msgstr "接下来的几章描述当前的 Ants 卡带。它的源代码和规则测试在[仓库](../platform/repositories.md)一章列出的 Ants 仓库中。每条对局记录都标明了运行它的引擎，查看器必须用该引擎版本来重建回放。"

#: src/games/ants.md:62
msgid "A real ladder match on <code>small-basic-3p-1h</code>, the release's basic small three-player board: three seats, one hill each, 36 by 36. Seat 2 loses its last ant on turn 20, and seat 1 razes its hill on turn 48 to lead on score, three to one. Seat 0 grows the larger colony instead, and by turn 240 it holds fourteen ants to seat 1's six. On the last turn, 375, seat 0 razes seat 1's hill and takes the match three to two, <code>rank_stabilized</code>. No seat was struck: once seat 2 had no ants, the platform stopped asking it for moves."
msgstr "一场真实的天梯对局，地图是 <code>small-basic-3p-1h</code>，即发布版本中的基础小型三人地图：三个席位，各有一座蚁丘，36 × 36。席位 2 在第 20 回合失去最后一只蚂蚁，席位 1 在第 48 回合摧毁了它的蚁丘，以 3 比 1 领先。席位 0 则专注于壮大蚁群，到第 240 回合，它有 14 只蚂蚁，而席位 1 只有 6 只。在最后一回合，即第 375 回合，席位 0 摧毁了席位 1 的蚁丘，以 3 比 2 赢下对局，结束原因为 <code>rank_stabilized</code>。没有席位被判罚：席位 2 没有蚂蚁之后，平台就不再向它索取移动。"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:3
msgid "The Ants world is a rectangular grid of land and water. Coordinates are `[row, column]`, both starting at zero. The observation's `size` gives `[rows, columns]`; do not assume a square board."
msgstr "Ants 的世界是一张由陆地和水域组成的矩形网格。坐标写作 `[row, column]`，两者都从零开始。观测中的 `size` 给出 `[rows, columns]`；不要假定地图是正方形的。"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:6
msgid "The grid, and why it wraps"
msgstr "网格，以及它为什么环绕"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:8
msgid "Both axes wrap. On a 64 × 96 board, a move north from `[0, 10]` reaches `[63, 10]`, and a move east from `[20, 95]` reaches `[20, 0]`. Borders block nothing: an enemy can attack a hill near one from across the board boundary."
msgstr "两个轴都环绕。在 64 × 96 的地图上，从 `[0, 10]` 向北移动会到达 `[63, 10]`，从 `[20, 95]` 向东移动会到达 `[20, 0]`。边界不会阻挡任何东西：敌人可以从地图边界的另一侧攻击靠近边界的蚁丘。"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:12
msgid "Ranges use the shorter wrapped displacement on each axis. With row difference `dr` and column difference `dc`, use:"
msgstr "距离在每个轴上都取环绕后较短的那段位移。设行差为 `dr`、列差为 `dc`，则："

#: src/games/ants/world.md:21
msgid "Vision, fighting and food collection all use this geometry."
msgstr "视野、战斗和食物采集都使用这套几何。"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:23
msgid "Two steps show it. An ant ordered north off the top row arrives on the bottom one, and an ant ordered west off the left column arrives on the right. Nothing stops the ant or marks the crossing; its row or column jumps to the other end."
msgstr "两步就能看明白。一只蚂蚁从最上面一行被命令向北移动，会出现在最下面一行；从最左边一列被命令向西移动，会出现在最右边一列。没有任何东西阻拦蚂蚁，也没有任何标记提示它跨越了边界；它的行号或列号直接跳到另一端。"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:29
msgid "Red's hill is in the top-left corner. Press the right arrow once: the order north takes the ant off the top row and it appears on the bottom one. Press again: the order west takes it off the left column and it appears on the right. Two steps from home, it stands in the far corner of the picture. The board has no corner to defend and no edge an enemy can pin you against."
msgstr "红方的蚁丘在左上角。按一下右方向键：向北的指令让蚂蚁离开最上面一行，出现在最下面一行。再按一下：向西的指令让它离开最左边一列，出现在最右边一列。离家才两步，它就站在了画面的对角。地图上没有可以据守的角落，也没有能让敌人把你逼到死角的边缘。"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:40
msgid "Terrain and water"
msgstr "地形与水域"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:42
msgid "Water is impassable and permanent. A move into water leaves the ant where it was, and that ant can still collide with another ant arriving on its square. **Food refuses a move the same way**: an ant cannot step onto a food square, so it gathers from beside it. A land square can hold a hill and an ant together, and the engine places new food on empty land only. No two ants remain on one square after movement resolves."
msgstr "水域不可通行且永久存在。试图移入水域的蚂蚁会留在原地，而且仍然可能与另一只到达它所在格子的蚂蚁相撞。**食物同样会拒绝移动**：蚂蚁不能踏上有食物的格子，所以只能从旁边采集。一个陆地格可以同时容纳一座蚁丘和一只蚂蚁，而引擎只在空的陆地上放置新食物。移动结算之后，不会有两只蚂蚁留在同一格。"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:48
msgid "Your observation keeps the water you have discovered. A zero in its water mask means land or an undiscovered square, so a route of zeros can still run into water. [The observation format](../../models/observation.md) gives the encoding."
msgstr "你的观测会保留你已发现的水域。水域掩码中的 0 表示陆地或尚未发现的格子，所以一条全是 0 的路线仍然可能撞上水域。[观测格式](../../models/observation.md)给出了编码方式。"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:52
msgid "Hills"
msgstr "蚁丘"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:54
msgid "New ants spawn on hills and nowhere else. An enemy ant standing on a hill after combat razes it, and a razed hill is gone for good. An ant on your own hill blocks spawning there, even with food in your hive."
msgstr "新蚂蚁只会在蚁丘上出生，别处不会。战斗结束后仍站在蚁丘上的敌方蚂蚁会摧毁它，被摧毁的蚁丘永远消失。站在自己蚁丘上的蚂蚁会阻止那里出生新蚂蚁，即使蚁巢里有食物也一样。"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:58
msgid "A colony that loses all its hills stays in the match while its ants live. They keep moving and attacking, and without a standing hill the colony cannot replace them."
msgstr "失去所有蚁丘的蚁群，只要还有蚂蚁存活，就仍留在对局中。它们可以继续移动和攻击，但没有尚存的蚁丘，蚁群就无法补充它们。"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:61 src/games/ants/maps.md:197 src/games/ants/maps.md:202
msgid "Food"
msgstr "食物"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:63
msgid "An ant can gather food on its own square or on one of the four squares beside it, after spawning resolves. The food goes into the colony's hive, a shared store with no place on the map. One unit of stored food can create one ant on a free hill."
msgstr "出生结算之后，蚂蚁可以采集自己所在格或相邻四格中的食物。食物进入蚁群的蚁巢，这是一个共享的储备，在地图上没有位置。一单位储备的食物可以在一座空闲的蚁丘上生成一只蚂蚁。"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:67
msgid "Each board puts food near the starting hills so colonies can start growing. After turn zero, food arrives at a **hidden rate** the engine draws from the match's seed, between five and eleven units per colony every nineteen to thirty-seven turns. It lands in symmetric sets, so no colony is fed while its opponents starve, and a unit owed to an occupied square waits until the square is free. The rate is the one thing about a board you cannot read from its file."
msgstr "每张地图都会在起始蚁丘附近放置食物，让蚁群能够开始发展。第零回合之后，食物按一个**隐藏的速率**出现，这个速率由引擎根据对局的种子抽取：每 19 到 37 个回合，每个蚁群得到 5 到 11 单位。食物以对称的组合落下，所以不会出现一个蚁群吃饱而对手挨饿的情况；应该落在已被占据格子上的那一单位会等到格子空出来。这个速率是地图上唯一无法从地图文件中读出的东西。"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:73
msgid "Vision and fog"
msgstr "视野与迷雾"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:75
msgid "You see a square if its wrapped squared distance from any of your living ants is at most **77**. Water does not block vision. Enemies, food and hills outside that radius are missing from the current observation, so losing an ant can hide an area you saw a turn earlier."
msgstr "如果一个格子到你任意一只存活蚂蚁的环绕距离平方不超过 **77**，你就能看到它。水域不会遮挡视野。半径之外的敌人、食物和蚁丘不会出现在当前观测中，所以失去一只蚂蚁可能让你上一回合还看得到的区域消失。"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:79
msgid "The engine remembers discovered water for you and nothing else out of sight: enemies, food and hills drop out of the observation once you lose sight of them. The observation carries no turn number, score or hive count. It does carry `vis`, the mask of what you can see this turn, so your model can tell an empty square from one it cannot see. Anything else your model carries between calls is its own [memory](../../models/memory.md), and only when its class allows one."
msgstr "引擎只替你记住已发现的水域，视野之外的其他一切都不记：敌人、食物和蚁丘一旦离开视野，就从观测中消失。观测不包含回合数、得分或蚁巢中的食物数。它确实包含 `vis`，即本回合你能看到哪些格子的掩码，这样你的模型就能区分空格子和看不到的格子。模型在两次调用之间携带的其他任何东西都属于它自己的[记忆](../../models/memory.md)，而且只有在它的重量级允许记忆时才行。"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:85
msgid "**The viewer cannot show this yet.** A replay frame carries the board as the _referee_ sees it (every ant, all the water), because re-simulating an action stream rebuilds that view. `replay-decode` cannot yet say what a seat _knew_ on a given turn, and until it can, a replay here would teach you the opposite of this section."
msgstr "**查看器目前还无法展示这一点**。回放帧携带的是<em>裁判</em>看到的地图（每一只蚂蚁、全部水域），因为重新模拟动作流重建的正是这个视图。`replay-decode` 目前还说不出某个席位在某一回合<em>知道</em>什么；在它能做到之前，放在这里的回放只会教给你与本节相反的东西。"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:97
msgid "Symmetry and boards"
msgstr "对称性与地图"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:99
msgid "Every seat starts on the same board: seat `k`'s terrain, hills and turn-zero food are seat 0's, moved `k` times by the board's shift, which the map file names `symmetry`. The colonies choose different moves, so play can break that symmetry from the first turn."
msgstr "每个席位的起点都是同一张地图：席位 `k` 的地形、蚁丘和第零回合的食物，就是席位 0 的那些按地图的平移量移动 `k` 次得到的，地图文件把这个平移量称为 `symmetry`。各个蚁群选择不同的移动，所以从第一回合起，对局就可能打破这种对称。"

#: src/games/ants/world.md:103
msgid "The [board](maps.md) sets the dimensions, the terrain, the hills a seat and the seat count. Boards seat from two players to eight, a season's boards are its own, and two boards of one size can seat different counts, so read the seat count from the board and never infer it from the size."
msgstr "[地图](maps.md)决定尺寸、地形、每个席位的蚁丘数和席位数。地图可容纳 2 到 8 名玩家，每个赛季的地图都是它自己的，同一尺寸的两张地图可以容纳不同的人数，所以席位数要从地图中读取，绝不要根据尺寸推断。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:3
msgid "Every player chooses its actions from its own observation before the turn resolves. You see an opponent's move, and can react to it, only in the next observation."
msgstr "每位玩家都在回合结算之前，根据自己的观测选择动作。你只有在下一次观测中才能看到对手的行动，并作出反应。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:6
msgid "The replays on this page are short scripted matches on a six-by-eight board, played through the cartridge the ladder runs. Each opens one turn before the moment it shows, so one press of the right arrow plays it. The viewer draws a death as a hollow ring on the square the ant died on with a line from every enemy that killed it (two ants that kill each other draw two lines that meet halfway), and a razed hill as a dashed square."
msgstr "本页的回放都是在 6 × 8 地图上进行的简短脚本对局，由天梯所用的卡带运行。每段回放都从它要展示的时刻的前一回合打开，所以按一下右方向键就能播放。查看器把死亡画成蚂蚁死亡格子上的空心圆环，并从每个击杀它的敌方蚂蚁引出一条线（两只互相击杀的蚂蚁会画出两条在中点相接的线）；被摧毁的蚁丘画成虚线方框。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:12
msgid "The six steps, in order"
msgstr "六个步骤，按顺序"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:14 src/models/memory.md:47
msgid "Step"
msgstr "步骤"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:14
msgid "Resolution"
msgstr "结算"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:14
msgid "Consequence"
msgstr "后果"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:16
msgid "1. Move"
msgstr "1. 移动"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:16
msgid "Apply moves, then remove collisions"
msgstr "执行移动，然后移除碰撞的蚂蚁"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:16
msgid "Friendly ants can kill each other"
msgstr "己方蚂蚁之间也会互相撞死"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:17
msgid "2. Battle"
msgstr "2. 战斗"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:17
msgid "Evaluate combat among survivors"
msgstr "在幸存者之间结算战斗"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:17
msgid "An ant that dies on a hill razes nothing"
msgstr "死在蚁丘上的蚂蚁摧毁不了蚁丘"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:18
msgid "3. Raze"
msgstr "3. 摧毁"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:18
msgid "Surviving enemies destroy occupied hills"
msgstr "幸存的敌方蚂蚁摧毁它们所站的蚁丘"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:18
msgid "A destroyed hill cannot spawn"
msgstr "被摧毁的蚁丘不再出生蚂蚁"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:19
msgid "4. Spawn"
msgstr "4. 出生"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:19
msgid "Stored food creates ants on free hills"
msgstr "储存的食物在空闲的蚁丘上变成蚂蚁"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:19
msgid "An occupied hill blocks growth"
msgstr "被占据的蚁丘阻碍扩张"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:20
msgid "5. Gather"
msgstr "5. 采集"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:20
msgid "Nearby food enters the hive"
msgstr "附近的食物进入蚁巢"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:20
msgid "This food cannot spawn until a later turn"
msgstr "这些食物要到之后的回合才能出生蚂蚁"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:21
msgid "6. New food"
msgstr "6. 新食物"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:21
msgid "Place fresh food"
msgstr "放置新的食物"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:21
msgid "Ants can gather it on later turns"
msgstr "蚂蚁可以在之后的回合采集"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:23
msgid "After these steps the engine folds each colony's vision into what it knows, advances the turn count and checks the [ending conditions](scoring.md)."
msgstr "这些步骤之后，引擎把每个蚁群的视野并入其已知信息，推进回合计数，并检查[结束条件](scoring.md)。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:26
msgid "Moving and collisions"
msgstr "移动与碰撞"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:28
msgid "An ant moves one square north, east, south or west, or stays. The engine treats a move into water **or onto food** as staying: both refuse the destination and leave the ant where it was. An ant with no order also stays. Movement wraps at both edges; see [The world](world.md)."
msgstr "蚂蚁每回合向北、东、南、西移动一格，或者原地不动。引擎把走进水域**或走上食物**的移动视为原地不动：两者都拒绝该目的地，蚂蚁留在原处。没有指令的蚂蚁同样原地不动。移动在两个方向的边缘都会环绕；见[世界](world.md)。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:32
msgid "The engine checks collisions at each ant's final destination. If two or more ants arrive on one square, **all of them die**, whoever owns them. Moving onto a friendly ant that stays is a collision. Two adjacent ants that swap places do not collide, since their destinations differ; combat still follows at their new positions."
msgstr "引擎在每只蚂蚁的最终目的地检查碰撞。如果两只或更多蚂蚁到达同一格，**它们全部死亡**，不论属于谁。走上一只原地不动的己方蚂蚁也算碰撞。两只相邻的蚂蚁互换位置不算碰撞，因为它们的目的地不同；战斗仍会在它们的新位置上进行。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:37
msgid "A collision is between your own ants. Two enemies that could arrive on one square stood at most two squares apart the turn before, squared distance 4 at the furthest, so they were already in each other's attack range, and two enemies in range can never both survive a battle. The one exception is an ant that appeared after that battle, since spawning runs later in the turn than the fighting."
msgstr "碰撞只会发生在你自己的蚂蚁之间。两只有可能到达同一格的敌对蚂蚁，上一回合最多相隔两格，距离平方最远为 4，所以它们早已在彼此的攻击范围内，而两只互在范围内的敌对蚂蚁绝不可能都在战斗中幸存。唯一的例外是在那场战斗之后出生的蚂蚁，因为出生在回合中晚于战斗。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:42
msgid "The order array is positional, in `mine` order: row-major by square, whatever order your ants appeared in. Entry 0 is the ant in your topmost occupied row, leftmost of any tie, and that can be a different ant each turn."
msgstr "指令数组按位置对应，顺序与 `mine` 相同：按格子行优先排列，与你的蚂蚁出生的先后无关。第 0 项是你占据的最上面一行里的蚂蚁，同一行取最左边的，而这每回合都可能是不同的蚂蚁。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:48
msgid "Red gathers the food below its hill, steps east, and a new ant appears on the hill behind it, so on turn 2 red's two ants stand side by side with the hill ant as entry 0. Press the right arrow: turn 3 sends entry 0 east onto the square the other ant holds. Both ants die there, two rings on one square, and neither death has a killer. Blue never moves. With no red ant left, the engine credits blue with red's hill and ends the match."
msgstr "红方采集蚁丘下方的食物，向东走一步，一只新蚂蚁出现在它身后的蚁丘上，所以在第 2 回合红方的两只蚂蚁并排站立，蚁丘上的那只是第 0 项。按右方向键：第 3 回合把第 0 项向东送到另一只蚂蚁所在的格子。两只蚂蚁都死在那里，同一格上有两个圆环，而两次死亡都没有击杀者。蓝方始终不动。红方没有蚂蚁了，引擎把红方的蚁丘算作被蓝方摧毁，并结束对局。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:62
msgid "Combat"
msgstr "战斗"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:64
msgid "An enemy is in attack range when the wrapped squared distance is at most **5**. After collisions, the engine counts the enemies in range of each ant; that count is the ant's **focus**. Friendly ants add nothing to it."
msgstr "环绕后的距离平方不超过 **5** 的敌方蚂蚁就在攻击范围内。碰撞处理之后，引擎数出每只蚂蚁攻击范围内的敌方蚂蚁数量；这个数就是该蚂蚁的**集火值**。己方蚂蚁不计入。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:68
msgid "An ant dies if any enemy in range has focus less than or equal to its own. An ant survives only if every enemy it faces has a higher focus, and an ant with no enemy in range survives combat."
msgstr "只要范围内有任何一只敌方蚂蚁的集火值小于或等于自己的，蚂蚁就会死亡。只有当它面对的每只敌方蚂蚁集火值都比它高，它才能幸存；范围内没有敌方蚂蚁的蚂蚁则安然度过战斗。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:71
msgid "The engine computes every focus before it removes any ant, so a dying ant still counts in that turn's comparisons and deaths do not cascade."
msgstr "引擎先算出所有集火值，再移除任何蚂蚁，所以将死的蚂蚁仍然计入本回合的比较，死亡不会连锁。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:74
msgid "Position after movement"
msgstr "移动后的位置"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:74
msgid "Focus values"
msgstr "集火值"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:74 src/models/adapters/operators.md:14 src/models/adapters/operators.md:45 src/models/adapters/operators.md:65 src/models/adapters/operators.md:79 src/reference/api.md:23 src/reference/api.md:42 src/reference/api.md:245
msgid "Result"
msgstr "结果"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:76
msgid "One ant against one, in range"
msgstr "一对一，互在范围内"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:76
msgid "Both 1"
msgstr "都是 1"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:76
msgid "Both die"
msgstr "都死亡"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:77
msgid "Two allies each in range of one enemy, no other enemies"
msgstr "两只己方蚂蚁各自在同一敌方蚂蚁的范围内，没有其他敌人"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:77
msgid "Allies 1 each; enemy 2"
msgstr "己方各 1；敌方 2"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:77
msgid "Allies survive; enemy dies"
msgstr "己方幸存；敌方死亡"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:78
msgid "Two against two, all in mutual range"
msgstr "二对二，全部互在范围内"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:78
msgid "All 2"
msgstr "都是 2"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:78
msgid "All die"
msgstr "全部死亡"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:79
msgid "Four adjacent cells in a row: A A B B"
msgstr "一行四个相邻格子：A A B B"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:79
msgid "Outer ants 1; inner ants 2"
msgstr "外侧 1；内侧 2"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:79
msgid "Inner ants die; outer ants survive"
msgstr "内侧死亡；外侧幸存"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:81
msgid "The last two cases have the same number of ants and different outcomes. Your model has to weigh position and support as well as the size of each army."
msgstr "最后两种情况蚂蚁数量相同，结果却不同。你的模型除了衡量双方兵力，还要衡量位置和支援。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:84
msgid "Two ants that close to within attack range with no support on either side have equal focus, and both die. You never see one ant facing another in range, because the fight resolves on the turn the gap closes."
msgstr "两只蚂蚁进入彼此的攻击范围，而双方都没有支援，那么集火值相等，两只都死亡。你永远看不到一只蚂蚁与范围内的另一只对峙，因为距离拉近的那一回合，战斗就已结算。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:90
msgid "Turn 1 has each ant one step off its hill and the two four columns apart, squared distance 17, outside the range of 5. Press the right arrow: on turn 2 red steps east and blue steps west, the distance becomes 5, and each ant kills the other: a line in each colour runs from its ring and the two meet halfway. The match ends there with no ants on the board."
msgstr "第 1 回合，两只蚂蚁各自离开蚁丘一步，相隔四列，距离平方为 17，在 5 的范围之外。按右方向键：第 2 回合红方向东一步，蓝方向西一步，距离平方变为 5，两只蚂蚁互相击杀：每种颜色各有一条线从它的圆环引出，两条线在中点相接。对局就此结束，地图上没有蚂蚁了。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:101
msgid "Support changes the outcome, and you can see it. Two ants that come into range of a lone enemy **on the same turn** each face one enemy while it faces two: its focus is 2 and theirs is 1, so it dies and both of them live. Arriving a turn apart would be the case above, twice."
msgstr "支援会改变结果，而且你能看到。两只蚂蚁**在同一回合**进入一只落单敌方蚂蚁的范围，它们各自面对一个敌人，而它面对两个：它的集火值是 2，它们的是 1，所以它死亡，它们两只都活下来。如果相隔一回合到达，就是上面的情况重演两次。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:107
msgid "Red gathers the food beside its hill and spawns a second ant, while blue walks west from its own hill. Turn 2 has red's two ants in a column and blue two squares from the nearer one. Press the right arrow: on turn 3 red steps south and blue steps west, which puts blue in range of both red ants at once. Two lines run into blue's ring and none into red's: blue faced two and died, each red ant faced one and lived. Blue has no ant left, so the engine credits red with blue's hill (the dashed square) and ends the match 3–0."
msgstr "红方采集蚁丘旁的食物并出生第二只蚂蚁，蓝方则从自己的蚁丘向西走。第 2 回合，红方两只蚂蚁排成一列，蓝方距离较近的那只两格。按右方向键：第 3 回合红方向南一步，蓝方向西一步，这让蓝方同时进入两只红方蚂蚁的范围。两条线通向蓝方的圆环，没有一条通向红方的：蓝方面对两个敌人而死，每只红方蚂蚁面对一个而活。蓝方没有蚂蚁了，引擎把蓝方的蚁丘（虚线方框）算作被红方摧毁，并以 3–0 结束对局。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:120
msgid "Razing a hill"
msgstr "摧毁蚁丘"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:122
msgid "A surviving enemy on a standing hill destroys it, earning +2 and costing its owner 1 point. An attacker killed during collisions or battle razes nothing. Your own ant cannot raze your hill."
msgstr "幸存的敌方蚂蚁站在尚存的蚁丘上就会摧毁它，获得 +2 分，蚁丘的主人失去 1 分。在碰撞或战斗中死亡的进攻者摧毁不了任何东西。你自己的蚂蚁不能摧毁你的蚁丘。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:125
msgid "That last rule is what makes hills hard to take. An ant on its own hill covers every square within squared distance 5 of it, two squares out in a line, so a lone attacker stepping into that ring dies with the defender and razes nothing. To take a defended hill you need support, or a defender that has left. The replay below shows the second case: the script walks blue's ant away from its hill first, so red razes the hill without a fight."
msgstr "最后这条规则正是蚁丘难以攻下的原因。站在自己蚁丘上的蚂蚁覆盖距离平方 5 以内的每一格，直线上可达两格之外，所以单独一只进攻者踏入这个圈子就会与防守者同归于尽，摧毁不了任何东西。要攻下有防守的蚁丘，你需要支援，或者等防守者离开。下面的回放展示第二种情况：脚本先让蓝方的蚂蚁走离蚁丘，于是红方未经战斗就摧毁了蚁丘。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:133
msgid "Blue's ant walked three squares north on the first three turns and holds there, out of range of its own hill. Red walked three south and is walking east along blue's row. Turn 6 has it one square from the hill. Press the right arrow: on turn 7 red stands on the hill, the hill is drawn as a dashed square because it is gone, and the score goes from 1–1 to 3–0, +2 to the razer and −1 to the owner. With no enemy hill left standing, the finishing order can no longer change, so the engine ends the match <code>rank_stabilized</code>. Red's own hill is untouched and can still spawn."
msgstr "蓝方的蚂蚁在前三回合向北走了三格并停在那里，离开了自己蚁丘的范围。红方向南走了三格，正沿着蓝方所在的行向东走。第 6 回合它离蚁丘只有一格。按右方向键：第 7 回合红方站上蚁丘，蚁丘因为已经不复存在而画成虚线方框，比分从 1–1 变为 3–0，摧毁者 +2，主人 −1。没有敌方蚁丘尚存，最终名次再也不会改变，所以引擎以 <code>rank_stabilized</code> 结束对局。红方自己的蚁丘毫发无损，仍然可以出生蚂蚁。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:147
msgid "Food and new ants"
msgstr "食物与新蚂蚁"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:149
msgid "Each stored food unit spawns one ant on an unoccupied friendly hill. With several hills free, the one that has gone longest without being touched goes first, where a hill is touched when it spawns and when one of its own ants stands on it. A tie goes to the hill listed first in the map file, and the map file lists hills so that every seat's first hill is the same hill of the board, moved by its shift. Each hill can spawn at most one ant per turn, because the new ant then occupies it. Food waits in the hive while no hill is free."
msgstr "每单位储存的食物在一个无蚂蚁占据的己方蚁丘上出生一只蚂蚁。有多个蚁丘空闲时，最久没有被“触碰”的那个先出生；蚁丘在出生蚂蚁时，以及有自己的蚂蚁站在上面时，算作被触碰。若相同，则取地图文件中先列出的蚁丘；地图文件列出蚁丘的方式，保证每个席位的第一个蚁丘都是地图上同一个蚁丘按偏移量移动后的位置。每个蚁丘每回合最多出生一只蚂蚁，因为新蚂蚁随即占据了它。没有蚁丘空闲时，食物在蚁巢里等待。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:156
msgid "Gathering uses squared radius **1**: the food square and its four orthogonal neighbours. If one colony alone has surviving ants in range, it collects the food; with none in range, the food stays. The engine also destroys food that several colonies contest. That case cannot arise under the current attack and gathering radii, because opposing ants cannot both survive in gathering range of the same food."
msgstr "采集使用的半径平方为 **1**：食物所在的格子和它正交相邻的四格。如果只有一个蚁群有幸存的蚂蚁在范围内，它就收下这份食物；范围内没有蚂蚁，食物就留在原地。多个蚁群争夺的食物，引擎会将其销毁。但在当前的攻击半径和采集半径下，这种情况不可能出现，因为敌对的蚂蚁不可能都在同一份食物的采集范围内幸存。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:162
msgid "Food gathered this turn can spawn **next turn at the earliest**, so a useful growth pattern is to step off a hill while another ant gathers nearby."
msgstr "本回合采集的食物**最早要到下一回合**才能出生蚂蚁，所以一种有效的扩张方式是：一只蚂蚁走下蚁丘，同时另一只在附近采集。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:165
msgid "Spawning also runs _after_ the fighting, which works for the defender: a colony whose defender dies on its own hill can replace it in the same turn from food already in the hive. A hill stops producing defenders once the hive behind it is empty."
msgstr "出生还在战斗<em>之后</em>进行，这对防守方有利：防守者死在自己蚁丘上的蚁群，可以在同一回合用蚁巢里已有的食物补上一只。蚁巢空了之后，蚁丘就不再产出防守者。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:171
msgid "On turn 1 red gathers the food beside its hill: the food is gone from that frame and no ant has appeared. Press the right arrow: turn 2 steps the gatherer off the hill, and the new ant stands on it. Food gathered on one turn becomes an ant on the next, and never sooner. Blue shows the other half of the rule. It gathered the food beside its hill on turn 1 as well and never spawns, because its own ant stands on the only square where its new ant could appear."
msgstr "第 1 回合红方采集蚁丘旁的食物：那一帧里食物消失了，但没有蚂蚁出现。按右方向键：第 2 回合采集者走下蚁丘，新蚂蚁站在蚁丘上。某一回合采集的食物在下一回合变成蚂蚁，绝不会更早。蓝方展示规则的另一半。它同样在第 1 回合采集了蚁丘旁的食物，却始终没有出生新蚂蚁，因为它自己的蚂蚁一直站在新蚂蚁唯一能出现的格子上。"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:186
msgid "Sending nothing"
msgstr "不发指令"

#: src/games/ants/turn.md:188
msgid "The game leaves an ant with no order where it is. A failed model call is a different matter: the platform counts a missing or failed answer as a strike, substitutes no movement, and forfeits the seat at the strike limit. Make the call succeed every turn: your adapters must evaluate, and your graph must return its declared head, inside the deadline. A policy that holds every ant still answers, by scoring `-` highest for each one. See [actions](../../models/actions.md)."
msgstr "游戏让没有指令的蚂蚁留在原地。模型调用失败则是另一回事：平台把缺失或失败的回答记为一次判罚，以不移动代替，并在达到判罚上限时将该席位判负。要让每一回合的调用都成功：你的适配器必须能求值，你的计算图必须在时限内返回它声明的策略头。让每只蚂蚁都原地不动的策略同样是一种回答，只需给每只蚂蚁的 `-` 打最高分。见[动作](../../models/actions.md)。"

#: src/games/ants/scoring.md:3
msgid "Ants ranks colonies by hill score. Army size, food collection and survival count only as far as they help you score."
msgstr "Ants 按蚁丘得分给蚁群排名。兵力、采集的食物和存活本身都不计分，只有在帮助你得分时才有意义。"

#: src/games/ants/scoring.md:6
msgid "How score is computed"
msgstr "得分如何计算"

#: src/games/ants/scoring.md:8
msgid "Event"
msgstr "事件"

#: src/games/ants/scoring.md:8
msgid "Score change"
msgstr "得分变化"

#: src/games/ants/scoring.md:10
msgid "Raze an enemy hill"
msgstr "摧毁一个敌方蚁丘"

#: src/games/ants/scoring.md:10
msgid "+2"
msgstr "+2"

#: src/games/ants/scoring.md:11
msgid "Lose one of your hills"
msgstr "失去一个自己的蚁丘"

#: src/games/ants/scoring.md:11
msgid "−1"
msgstr "−1"

#: src/games/ants/scoring.md:12
msgid "Kill an ant, gather food, or hold territory"
msgstr "击杀蚂蚁、采集食物或占据领土"

#: src/games/ants/scoring.md:12 src/models/weight-classes.md:20 src/models/weight-classes.md:21 src/models/weight-classes.md:22 src/models/weight-classes.md:23 src/models/weight-classes.md:24 src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:108
msgid "0"
msgstr "0"

#: src/games/ants/scoring.md:14
msgid "**A colony starts with one point per hill it owns**, so a two-player match on one hill a seat opens at 1–1. A colony loses at most one point for each hill it owns, so a colony that loses every hill and razes nothing ends on **0** instead of below it. The floor comes from the scoring and holds on every board, including those with two hills a seat."
msgstr "**蚁群开局时每拥有一个蚁丘得 1 分**，所以每方一个蚁丘的双人对局以 1–1 开局。蚁群每个蚁丘最多失去 1 分，所以失去全部蚁丘而没有摧毁任何敌方蚁丘的蚁群最终得 **0** 分，不会更低。这个下限来自计分规则本身，在每张地图上都成立，包括每方两个蚁丘的地图。"

#: src/games/ants/scoring.md:19
msgid "If one colony is the last with living ants, the engine treats every enemy hill still standing as razed: the survivor gets +2 per hill and each owner loses 1 per hill."
msgstr "如果只剩一个蚁群还有存活的蚂蚁，引擎把所有尚存的敌方蚁丘都视为已被摧毁：幸存者每个蚁丘得 +2 分，每个主人每个蚁丘失去 1 分。"

#: src/games/ants/scoring.md:22
msgid "In a two-player match with one hill each, both colonies open on 1, and a successful raze finishes **3–0**: the attacker's own point plus 2, against the defender's point less 1. Ant count breaks no tie."
msgstr "在每方一个蚁丘的双人对局中，两个蚁群都以 1 分开局，一次成功的摧毁以 **3–0** 收场：进攻方自己的 1 分加 2，对阵防守方的 1 分减 1。蚂蚁数量不能用来打破平局。"

#: src/games/ants/scoring.md:28
msgid "The defender walked away from its hill on the first three turns and the attacker is one square from it on turn 6. Press the right arrow: the attacker stands on the hill, the hill is drawn as a dashed square, and the 1–1 opening becomes 3–0, +2 to the razer and −1 to the owner. The engine played it from a written script, so the rule plays out as stated."
msgstr "防守者在前三回合走离了自己的蚁丘，第 6 回合进攻者离蚁丘只有一格。按右方向键：进攻者站上蚁丘，蚁丘画成虚线方框，开局的 1–1 变成 3–0，摧毁者 +2，主人 −1。这场对局由引擎按写好的脚本进行，所以规则正如所述地展现出来。"

#: src/games/ants/scoring.md:42
msgid "After resolving a turn, the current engine checks these conditions in this order. The turn limit comes **last**, so a match that reaches the limit on a turn that also meets another condition carries the other reason:"
msgstr "结算完一回合后，当前引擎按以下顺序检查这些条件。回合上限排在**最后**，所以一场对局若在达到上限的同一回合也满足了另一个条件，记录的就是另一个原因："

#: src/games/ants/scoring.md:46
msgid "Condition"
msgstr "条件"

#: src/games/ants/scoring.md:46 src/models/observation.md:9 src/competing/version-life.md:8 src/competing/matches.md:41 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:11 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:44 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:55 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:72 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:91 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:100 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:145 src/reference/glossary.md:3
