#: src/models/observation.md:18
msgid "`vis.rle`"
msgstr "`vis.rle`"

#: src/models/observation.md:18
msgid "Row-major mask of what you can see **this turn**"
msgstr "行优先掩码，标出你**本回合**能看到的范围"

#: src/models/observation.md:20
msgid "Coordinates are zero-based and wrap as [The world](../games/ants/world.md) describes. Any list can be empty. A list index is no ant's identity: the engine sorts `mine` afresh for each observation, and births, deaths and movement change its order. `ids` is the identity."
msgstr "坐标从 0 开始，并按[世界](../games/ants/world.md)所述环绕。任何列表都可以为空。列表下标不是蚂蚁的身份：引擎为每次观测重新排序 `mine`，出生、死亡和移动都会改变它的顺序。身份由 `ids` 给出。"

#: src/models/observation.md:24
msgid "Ant ids"
msgstr "蚂蚁 id"

#: src/models/observation.md:26
msgid "`ids[i]` is the id of the ant at `mine[i]`. `mine` keeps its row-major order, so your actions and your policy head stay aligned with `mine`, exactly as [What your model answers](actions.md) says."
msgstr "`ids[i]` 是位于 `mine[i]` 的那只蚂蚁的 id。`mine` 保持行优先顺序，所以你的动作和策略头始终与 `mine` 对齐，正如[模型回答什么](actions.md)所述。"

#: src/models/observation.md:29
msgid "**An id belongs to one ant for its whole life, and is never reused.** The ant keeps it through every move, a blocked one included, and when it dies its id goes with it."
msgstr "**一个 id 终生只属于一只蚂蚁，永不重复使用**。蚂蚁在每一次移动中都保留它，被阻挡的移动也不例外；蚂蚁死亡时，它的 id 也随之消失。"

#: src/models/observation.md:31
msgid "**Ids are per seat**, counted from 0: your starting ants first, in the order of your hills, then each new ant in the order it spawns. Every seat counts the same way, so the seats stay symmetric."
msgstr "**id 按席位各自计数**，从 0 开始：先是你的初始蚂蚁，按你蚁丘的顺序，然后是每只新蚂蚁，按出生顺序。每个席位都以同样方式计数，所以各席位保持对称。"

#: src/models/observation.md:33
msgid "**Only your own ants carry ids.** `foes` carries none: an enemy ant's id would say how many ants that colony has ever spawned, which is what fog hides."
msgstr "**只有你自己的蚂蚁带有 id**。`foes` 不带：敌方蚂蚁的 id 会泄露那个蚁群总共出生过多少只蚂蚁，而这正是迷雾要隐藏的信息。"

#: src/models/observation.md:35
msgid "An id stays far below 2<sup>24</sup>, so it survives a cast to `f32` exactly."
msgstr "id 远小于 2<sup>24</sup>，所以转换为 `f32` 后仍然精确无损。"

#: src/models/observation.md:37
msgid "A model with no [memory](memory.md) has no use for `ids`. One with a memory per ant uses them to find each ant's row from last turn ([how](memory.md#a-memory-per-ant)). An adapter reads only the keys it names, so a manifest that never names `ids` plays unchanged."
msgstr "没有[记忆](memory.md)的模型用不到 `ids`。每只蚂蚁各带一份记忆的模型则用它们找到每只蚂蚁上一回合对应的那一行（[怎么做](memory.md#a-memory-per-ant)）。适配器只读取它点名的键，所以从不提到 `ids` 的清单照常运行，不受影响。"

#: src/models/observation.md:41
msgid "Keys the runner adds"
msgstr "运行器添加的键"

#: src/models/observation.md:43
msgid "The game never sends `memory` or `ant_memory`. **They are the runner's**: when your manifest declares an output of that name, the runner hands its last value back on your seat's next observation under the same key, and it is absent on turn 0. [Memory](memory.md#the-carry) has the whole rule. A model that declares neither output never sees either key."
msgstr "游戏从不发送 `memory` 或 `ant_memory`**。它们属于运行器**：当你的清单声明了同名输出时，运行器会在你席位的下一次观测中以同一个键把上次的值交还给你，而在第 0 回合它不存在。完整规则见[记忆](memory.md#the-carry)。两个输出都不声明的模型永远不会看到这两个键。"

#: src/models/observation.md:48
msgid "Ownership labels"
msgstr "归属标签"

#: src/models/observation.md:50
msgid "Owners are **relative to you**. In `hills`, owner `0` is yours and `1` upward is an opponent's. In `foes`, the owner runs from `1` upward and is never `0`, since a foe is never you. On a two-seat board the label is constant: your hills are `0`, and every enemy hill and ant is `1`."
msgstr "归属是**相对于你的**。在 `hills` 中，归属 `0` 是你的，`1` 及以上是对手的。在 `foes` 中，归属从 `1` 起，永远不会是 `0`，因为敌人不可能是你自己。在双席位地图上这个标签是固定的：你的蚁丘是 `0`，所有敌方蚁丘和蚂蚁都是 `1`。"

#: src/models/observation.md:54
msgid "The observation has no self-seat field, and you need none: as far as the observation says, you always sit in seat `0`. Relabel every seat in the world and the same player receives identical bytes. That property makes the two seats of one match two samples of one distribution, and a self-play trainer depends on it."
msgstr "观测里没有自己席位的字段，你也不需要：在观测看来，你永远坐在席位 `0`。把世界里的所有席位重新编号，同一位玩家收到的字节完全相同。这一性质让一场对局的两个席位成为同一分布的两个样本，自博弈训练正依赖于此。"

#: src/models/observation.md:59
msgid "Known water"
msgstr "已知水域"

#: src/models/observation.md:61
msgid "Read RLE as `(value, count)` pairs. Values are 0 or 1, and the counts cover `rows × columns` cells in row-major order. A 1 means discovered water. A 0 can be known land **or an unexplored square**. Water you discovered on an earlier turn stays in the mask after your ants lose sight of it."
msgstr "RLE 按 `(value, count)` 成对读取。值为 0 或 1，计数按行优先顺序覆盖 `rows × columns` 个格子。1 表示已发现的水域。0 可能是已知的陆地，**也可能是尚未探索的格子**。你在之前回合发现的水域，在蚂蚁失去视野后仍保留在掩码中。"

#: src/models/observation.md:65
msgid "As an example of the encoding, `size: [2, 3]` and `rle: [0, 2, 1, 1, 0, 3]` expand to `[[0, 0, 1], [0, 0, 0]]`; no season could play a board that small. Use `rle_expand` to build the tensor without a JSON loop over cells."
msgstr "举个编码的例子：`size: [2, 3]` 和 `rle: [0, 2, 1, 1, 0, 3]` 展开为 `[[0, 0, 1], [0, 0, 0]]`；当然没有哪个赛季会用这么小的地图。用 `rle_expand` 来构建张量，不必在 JSON 里逐格循环。"

#: src/models/observation.md:69
msgid "What you can see this turn"
msgstr "本回合的视野"

#: src/models/observation.md:71
msgid "`vis` is the mask the engine filtered this observation through: a 1 at every cell within squared radius 77 of one of your ants, with wrapping, and a 0 everywhere else. It uses the same RLE encoding as `water`, so `rle_expand` builds the plane."
msgstr "`vis` 是引擎过滤这次观测所用的掩码：与你任意一只蚂蚁的距离平方不超过 77 的每个格子（含环绕）为 1，其余为 0。它使用与 `water` 相同的 RLE 编码，所以 `rle_expand` 就能构建这个平面。"

#: src/models/observation.md:75
msgid "**`vis` separates \"there is nothing here\" from \"I cannot see here\".** A 0 in the enemy plane where `vis` is 1 means the square is empty; a 0 where `vis` is 0 means you do not know. Your encoder needs that distinction: without it, a network learns \"no enemy\" from cells it could not have seen."
msgstr "**`vis` 把“这里什么都没有”和“这里我看不见”区分开**。敌方平面上的 0，在 `vis` 为 1 处表示该格为空；而 `vis` 为 0 处的 0 表示你不知道。你的编码器需要这一区分：没有它，网络就会从它本不可能看见的格子里学到“没有敌人”。"

#: src/models/observation.md:79
msgid "A trainer can derive `vis` from `mine` and the radius in four lines of numpy. **An adapter cannot**: its expression language cannot address an enclosing iterator's element, so it cannot union a disk per ant, and the engine sends the mask for that reason. If your trainer derives this plane itself, check that the two agree."
msgstr "训练器可以用四行 numpy 从 `mine` 和半径推出 `vis`**。适配器做不到**：它的表达式语言无法引用外层迭代器的元素，所以无法把每只蚂蚁周围的圆盘取并集，引擎正因此才发送这个掩码。如果你的训练器自己推导这个平面，请检查两者是否一致。"

#: src/models/observation.md:84
msgid "What is hidden"
msgstr "被隐藏的信息"

#: src/models/observation.md:86
msgid "The engine filters enemies, food and hills to this turn's vision; only known water carries over from one turn to the next. The payload has no scores, turn number, hive count or explored mask."
msgstr "引擎把敌人、食物和蚁丘过滤到本回合的视野内；只有已知水域会从一个回合延续到下一个。数据中没有得分、回合数、蚁巢存粮数，也没有已探索掩码。"

#: src/models/observation.md:89
msgid "A model call sees one observation and, when its class allows [memory](memory.md), what the model wrote on its previous turn. Nothing else carries over, so anything else a model wants to remember, it has to write into that memory. Train with the same missing information you will face in competition."
msgstr "一次模型调用只看到一份观测，以及在重量级允许[记忆](memory.md)时，模型在上一回合写下的内容。其他什么都不会延续，所以模型想记住的任何别的东西，都必须写进那份记忆。训练时就要面对与比赛中相同的信息缺失。"

