#: src/models/observation.md:111
msgid "The second ant is `mine[1]`, so the second action must address `[13, 30]`. `ids` says that ant is ant 0, the colony's first, and the one on the hill is ant 2, spawned later; ant 1 has died. The water field says this view holds no discovered water; the rest of the board may still hold some. The enemy and food coordinates lie within this turn's vision."
msgstr "第二只蚂蚁是 `mine[1]`，所以第二个动作必须指向 `[13, 30]`。`ids` 说明那只蚂蚁是 0 号蚂蚁，蚁群的第一只；蚁丘上的那只是后来出生的 2 号蚂蚁；1 号蚂蚁已经死亡。水域字段表明这个视图里没有已发现的水域；地图的其余部分可能仍有。敌人和食物的坐标都在本回合的视野之内。"

#: src/models/observation.md:117
msgid "**The viewer cannot show this yet.** A replay frame carries the board as the _referee_ sees it (every ant, all the water), because re-simulating an action stream reconstructs that view. `replay-decode` cannot yet say what a seat _knew_ at a turn, and until it can, a replay here would teach the opposite of this page's point."
msgstr "**查看器目前还无法展示这一点**。回放帧携带的是<em>裁判</em>所见的地图（每一只蚂蚁、全部水域），因为重新模拟动作流重建的就是那个视图。`replay-decode` 还无法说出一个席位在某回合<em>知道</em>什么，在它能做到之前，这里放一段回放反而会教给你与本页要点相反的东西。"

#: src/models/actions.md:3
msgid "The Ants action is a JSON array with one string per ant in the observation's `mine` list. **The referee produces it** by reading your graph's policy head, so this page is the contract your _output tensor_ has to meet."
msgstr "Ants 的动作是一个 JSON 数组，观测的 `mine` 列表中每只蚂蚁对应一个字符串。**它由裁判生成**：裁判读取你计算图的策略头来得到它，所以本页是你的<em>输出张量</em>必须满足的契约。"

#: src/models/actions.md:7
msgid "String"
msgstr "字符串"

#: src/models/actions.md:7
msgid "Move"
msgstr "移动"

#: src/models/actions.md:9
msgid "`N`"
msgstr "`N`"

#: src/models/actions.md:9
msgid "Row −1"
msgstr "行 −1"

#: src/models/actions.md:10
msgid "`E`"
msgstr "`E`"

#: src/models/actions.md:10
msgid "Column +1"
msgstr "列 +1"

#: src/models/actions.md:11
msgid "`S`"
msgstr "`S`"

#: src/models/actions.md:11
msgid "Row +1"
msgstr "行 +1"

#: src/models/actions.md:12
msgid "`W`"
msgstr "`W`"

#: src/models/actions.md:12
msgid "Column −1"
msgstr "列 −1"

#: src/models/actions.md:13
msgid "`-`"
msgstr "`-`"

#: src/models/actions.md:13
msgid "Stay"
msgstr "原地不动"

#: src/models/actions.md:15
msgid "Every move wraps at the map boundary. The contract has no diagonal moves, destinations, ant identifiers or action objects."
msgstr "每一步移动在地图边界处环绕。契约中没有斜向移动、目的地、蚂蚁标识符或动作对象。"

#: src/models/actions.md:18
msgid "One order per ant"
msgstr "每只蚂蚁一条指令"

#: src/models/actions.md:20
msgid "For `mine: [[12, 30], [13, 30]]`, the action `[\"N\", \"E\"]` moves the first ant toward `[11, 30]` and the second toward `[13, 31]`. The action holds one order per ant in `mine`, in `mine`'s order, and zero ants means `[]`."
msgstr "对于 `mine: [[12, 30], [13, 30]]`，动作 `[\"N\", \"E\"]` 让第一只蚂蚁走向 `[11, 30]`，第二只走向 `[13, 31]`。动作为 `mine` 中的每只蚂蚁各含一条指令，按 `mine` 的顺序排列；没有蚂蚁时就是 `[]`。"

#: src/models/actions.md:24
msgid "The two head shapes"
msgstr "两种策略头形状"

#: src/models/actions.md:26
msgid "Your manifest declares one output, in one of these two shapes. **Both carry five channels, in the order `N, E, S, W, -`**, and the referee takes the argmax."
msgstr "你的清单声明一个输出，形状为下面两种之一。**两者都带五个通道，顺序为 `N, E, S, W, -`**，裁判取 argmax。"

#: src/models/actions.md:29
msgid "Declared shape"
msgstr "声明的形状"

#: src/models/actions.md:29
msgid "What it means"
msgstr "含义"

#: src/models/actions.md:31
msgid "`[1, 5, \"H\", \"W\"]`"
msgstr "`[1, 5, \"H\", \"W\"]`"

#: src/models/actions.md:31
msgid "**A per-cell policy.** A score for every move at every square of the board. The referee gathers the five channels at each of your ants' cells, in `mine` order, and takes the argmax of each. A fully convolutional network produces this shape with no extra work"
msgstr "**逐格策略**。地图上每个格子的每种移动各有一个分数。裁判按 `mine` 顺序在你每只蚂蚁所在的格子上收集五个通道，再对每只取 argmax。全卷积网络无需额外工作就能产出这种形状"

#: src/models/actions.md:32
msgid "`[N, 5]`"
msgstr "`[N, 5]`"

#: src/models/actions.md:32
msgid "**One row per ant, already in `mine` order.** The referee takes the argmax of each row. `N` is a named dimension that binds to your ant count, so the same manifest serves every turn"
msgstr "**每只蚂蚁一行，已按 `mine` 顺序排列**。裁判对每一行取 argmax。`N` 是一个命名维度，绑定到你的蚂蚁数量，所以同一份清单每个回合都适用"

#: src/models/actions.md:34
msgid "The referee decodes both the same way from there, so pick the one that suits your architecture; the rules treat them alike. The per-cell head costs a gather that the platform pays for. The per-ant head is cheaper on large boards, but your graph has to do the indexing, which limits the axes you can name ([why](adapters.md#a-dimension-may-be-a-name))."
msgstr "从那一步起，裁判对两者的解码方式相同，所以选适合你架构的那种即可；规则对两者一视同仁。逐格策略头需要一次收集操作，开销由平台承担。逐蚁策略头在大地图上更便宜，但索引工作得由你的计算图自己完成，这会限制你能命名的轴（[原因](adapters.md#a-dimension-may-be-a-name)）。"

#: src/models/actions.md:39
msgid "**Keep training labels, output channels and this table in the same order.** With the channel order off by one, your model plays a rotation of what it learned, scores low, and nothing reports an error."
msgstr "**让训练标签、输出通道和这张表保持同一顺序**。通道顺序若错位一格，你的模型就会把学到的走法旋转后执行，得分很低，而且不会有任何报错。"

#: src/models/actions.md:43
msgid "Illegal and missing orders"
msgstr "非法与缺失的指令"

#: src/models/actions.md:45
msgid "An ant ordered into water stays where it is. The engine also treats an unrecognised direction string as staying, and ignores surplus positional orders. Your model cannot cause either of those two: the referee produces only the five strings, so those fallbacks guard against a cartridge change."
msgstr "被命令走进水域的蚂蚁会留在原地。引擎也把无法识别的方向字符串当作原地不动，并忽略多余的位置指令。这两种情况你的模型都不可能引起：裁判只会生成那五个字符串，这些兜底是为了防范卡带的变更。"

#: src/models/actions.md:50
msgid "**Admission checks legality.** It confirms that each adapter produces a tensor of the dtype and shape the manifest declares, that the graph runs, and that the head decodes to a valid action on every reference observation. It does not judge whether the action is any _good_. A model that answers `[\"-\", \"-\", …]` every turn is a legal entry that never moves, and an untrained graph does that. Check the distribution of your own actions during [testing](testing.md)."
msgstr "**审核检查的是合法性**。它确认每个适配器都产出清单声明的 dtype 和形状的张量，计算图能运行，并且在每份参考观测上策略头都能解码为合法动作。它不评判动作<em>好不好</em>。每回合都回答 `[\"-\", \"-\", …]` 的模型是一个合法但从不移动的参赛模型，未经训练的计算图就是这样。在[测试](testing.md)时检查一下你自己动作的分布。"

#: src/models/actions.md:56
msgid "The turn clock"
msgstr "回合时钟"

#: src/models/actions.md:58
msgid "The standard turn deadline is **1,000 ms** for your adapters and your inference together, and it is **yours alone**: each seat is its own call with its own deadline, so a slow opponent cannot spend your clock. A failed or timed-out call adds a strike, and none of the seat's ants move that turn. At five cumulative strikes the seat forfeits, and successful calls between failures do not reset the count."
msgstr "标准回合时限是 **1,000 ms**，适配器和推理共用，而且**只属于你**：每个席位是各自独立的调用，各有自己的时限，所以对手再慢也耗不掉你的时间。一次失败或超时的调用会记一次判罚，该席位的蚂蚁这一回合都不移动。累计五次判罚，席位就判负；失败之间的成功调用不会重置计数。"

#: src/models/actions.md:64
msgid "A deliberate hold array such as `[\"-\", \"-\"]` is a normal answer, and the referee treats it apart from a call that returns no action. The Ants contract has no resign action; see [scoring and forfeits](../games/ants/scoring.md)."
msgstr "像 `[\"-\", \"-\"]` 这样有意让全体原地不动的数组是正常回答，裁判把它与没有返回动作的调用区别对待。Ants 的契约中没有认输动作；见[计分与判负](../games/ants/scoring.md)。"

#: src/models/actions.md:68
msgid "A move is an intention"
msgstr "移动只是意图"

#: src/models/actions.md:70
msgid "An accepted action does not guarantee that the ant survives or reaches a useful position. Opponents move at the same time, friendly ants can collide, and battle runs before hill razing. Judge your model by the outcomes the [turn rules](../games/ants/turn.md) produce, beyond whether its direction strings are valid."
msgstr "动作被接受并不保证蚂蚁能存活或到达有用的位置。对手同时移动，友方蚂蚁可能碰撞，战斗在摧毁蚁丘之前结算。评判你的模型要看[回合规则](../games/ants/turn.md)产生的结果，而不只是方向字符串是否合法。"

#: src/models/actions.md:78
msgid "Every order in this match is valid, and the board still does things the orders do not say. Turn 1 sent the ant east onto the food beside its hill: food refuses a move, so the ant stayed on the hill, and it gathered the food from where it stood. Turn 2 moved that ant one square south, and a second ant nobody ordered appeared on the hill it left. Now press the right arrow. Turn 3 gives both ants the same order, east. The ant on the hill walks onto the square the food left empty; the ant below it is refused by water and stays. One order, two outcomes, and the engine received one order per ant, which is what your model has to answer."
msgstr "这场对局里的每条指令都合法，地图却仍然发生了指令没有说的事。第 1 回合命令蚂蚁向东走上蚁丘旁的食物：食物会拒绝移动，所以蚂蚁留在蚁丘上，并就地收集了那份食物。第 2 回合那只蚂蚁向南走了一格，一只谁也没有下令的新蚂蚁出现在它离开的蚁丘上。现在按一下右方向键。第 3 回合给两只蚂蚁同样的指令：向东。蚁丘上的蚂蚁走上食物消失后空出的格子；它下方的蚂蚁被水域拒绝，留在原地。一条指令，两种结果，而引擎收到的是每只蚂蚁一条指令，这正是你的模型要回答的。"

#: src/models/format.md:3
msgid "Submit a self-contained ONNX file named `model.onnx`, alongside `manifest.json`. A node reads the graph from the protobuf, builds a plan for it under **tract**, and runs it against the tensors your adapters produce. You choose the training code and framework; the exported file has to work within the deployed runtime and admission policy."
msgstr "提交一个名为 `model.onnx` 的自包含 ONNX 文件，连同 `manifest.json`。节点从 protobuf 中读取计算图，在 **tract** 下为它构建执行计划，再用你的适配器产出的张量运行它。训练代码和框架由你选择；导出的文件必须能在部署的运行时和审核策略之内工作。"

#: src/models/format.md:8
msgid "ONNX compatibility"
msgstr "ONNX 兼容性"

#: src/models/format.md:10
msgid "The deployment accepts ONNX opsets **13 through 19**, inclusive, and applies an operator allowlist. A graph that loads on your development machine can still break these rules. Keep your weights inside the graph: the contract is one model file and one manifest file, so a graph that points at weight files beside it finds nothing there."
msgstr "部署接受 ONNX opset **13 到 19**（含两端），并应用一份算子允许列表。能在你开发机上加载的计算图仍可能违反这些规则。把权重放在计算图内部：契约是一个模型文件加一个清单文件，所以指向旁边权重文件的计算图在那里什么也找不到。"

#: src/models/format.md:15
msgid "The allowlist names these operators:"
msgstr "允许列表包含以下算子："

#: src/models/format.md:29
msgid "The list is a snapshot of the deployment's policy, and it does not promise that every operator/type combination executes. An unlisted variant such as `GatherND` stays refused even when a related operator is on the list. Admission reads every operator out of the document, including those inside an `If`, `Loop` or `Scan` body and inside a model-local function, so inspect what your exporter emitted: it can differ from what you wrote."
msgstr "这份列表是部署策略的一个快照，并不承诺每种算子/类型组合都能执行。未列出的变体（如 `GatherND`）即使有相关算子在列表上，也仍被拒绝。审核会读出文档中的每一个算子，包括 `If`、`Loop` 或 `Scan` 主体内以及模型局部函数内的算子，所以要检查导出器实际生成了什么：它可能与你写的不同。"

#: src/models/format.md:35
msgid "**A season's list can only narrow what the runtime serves.** A season may publish a shorter list of its own, and the platform intersects it with this one, so a season cannot allow an operator the runtime cannot run. Allowing one would admit a model that then fails at play, the worst moment for a rejection."
msgstr "**赛季的列表只能收窄运行时所支持的范围**。赛季可以发布自己更短的列表，平台会将其与这份列表取交集，所以赛季无法允许运行时跑不了的算子。若允许了，就会放过一个在对局中才失败的模型，那是最糟糕的拒绝时机。"

#: src/models/format.md:40
msgid "Attributes are not operators"
msgstr "属性不是算子"

#: src/models/format.md:42
msgid "The allowlist names operators and says nothing about their attributes. `Conv` is on the list, so a **dilated** convolution is allowed: in ONNX, dilation is an attribute of `Conv`, and a dilated graph inspects as `Conv` like any other. Strides, groups and asymmetric kernels are attributes too, and the same holds for them."
msgstr "允许列表只列算子，对它们的属性不作规定。`Conv` 在列表上，所以**空洞**卷积是允许的：在 ONNX 中，膨胀率是 `Conv` 的一个属性，带空洞的计算图检查起来和其他任何 `Conv` 一样。步长、分组和非对称卷积核也都是属性，同理适用。"

#: src/models/format.md:47
msgid "The observation is a board, and your graph's **receptive field** (the distance from which an input can influence a cell's output) bounds what a unit standing there can respond to. A stack of ordinary 3x3 convolutions grows it by two cells a layer. Double the dilation at each layer and the growth becomes a power of two. With dilations 1, 2, 4 and 8, four layers reach fifteen cells each way; four undilated layers hold the same parameters and reach four."
msgstr "观测是一张地图，你计算图的**感受野**（输入能影响某格输出的最远距离）限定了站在该格的单元能响应的范围。一叠普通的 3x3 卷积每层让它增长两格。每层把膨胀率翻倍，增长就变成 2 的幂。膨胀率为 1、2、4、8 时，四层就能向每个方向触及十五格；四层不带空洞的卷积参数量相同，却只触及四格。"

#: src/models/format.md:53
msgid "Inputs and outputs"
msgstr "输入与输出"

#: src/models/format.md:55
msgid "**The manifest names them, and the names must be the graph's own.** Each entry in `inputs` gives a graph input's name, dtype and shape, plus the adapter that builds it; each entry in `outputs` gives an output's name, dtype and shape. The node reads them from `graph.input` and `graph.output` in the document. Those are tensor names. The nodes that produce the tensors carry names of their own, which the exporter picks, such as `/fc2/Gemm`, and the manifest must not use them."
msgstr "**清单给出它们的名称，且名称必须是计算图自己的**。`inputs` 中的每一项给出一个计算图输入的名称、dtype 和形状，以及构建它的适配器；`outputs` 中的每一项给出一个输出的名称、dtype 和形状。节点从文档的 `graph.input` 和 `graph.output` 中读取它们。这些是张量名称。计算图里产出这些张量的节点另有自己的名称，由导出器选定，例如 `/fc2/Gemm`，清单不得使用它们。"

#: src/models/format.md:61
msgid "Boundary dtypes are `bool`, `i8`, `u8`, `i16`, `u16`, `i32`, `u32`, `i64`, `u64`, `f32` and `f64`. Declare the ONNX boundary types as the graph has them: a dtype used inside the graph does not become a boundary dtype, and a `float16` _initializer_ under a `Cast` is an `f32` boundary."
msgstr "边界 dtype 有 `bool`、`i8`、`u8`、`i16`、`u16`、`i32`、`u32`、`i64`、`u64`、`f32` 和 `f64`。按计算图实际的样子声明 ONNX 边界类型：计算图内部使用的 dtype 不会成为边界 dtype，经过 `Cast` 的 `float16` <em>初始化器</em>，其边界是 `f32`。"

#: src/models/format.md:65
msgid "**Support every board size.** A dimension may be a name ([how](adapters.md#a-dimension-may-be-a-name)), so a fully convolutional graph declares `[1, P, \"H\", \"W\"]` and one admitted session serves every board a season plays, including one it adds later. A graph that computes indices inside itself cannot name its spatial axes, because the runtime cannot type-check that against a symbol. It must declare concrete axes, so it plays one board size and the runtime refuses it on the others."
msgstr "**支持每一种地图尺寸**。维度可以是名称（[怎么做](adapters.md#a-dimension-may-be-a-name)），所以全卷积计算图声明 `[1, P, \"H\", \"W\"]`，通过一次审核就能应付赛季所用的每张地图，包括后来新增的。在内部自行计算索引的计算图无法为空间轴命名，因为运行时无法用符号对其做类型检查。它必须声明具体的轴，于是只能玩一种地图尺寸，其他尺寸会被运行时拒绝。"

#: src/models/format.md:72
msgid "The node keeps nothing from one turn to the next. **A model's memory is carried by the runner, in the open**: declare an output named `memory` (the board) or `ant_memory` (one row per ant), and the runner hands its last value back on your seat's next observation under the same name, for your adapter to read. Your season's weight class sets how large it may be, and a class that allows none refuses a model that declares one. [Memory](memory.md) covers both, the carry and the cap."
msgstr "节点在回合之间什么都不保留。**模型的记忆由运行器公开携带**：声明一个名为 `memory`（整张地图）或 `ant_memory`（每只蚂蚁一行）的输出，运行器就会在你席位的下一次观测中以同一名称把上次的值交还给你，供你的适配器读取。你所在赛季的重量级规定它可以多大，不允许记忆的重量级会拒绝声明了记忆的模型。[记忆](memory.md)一页涵盖传递和上限两方面。"

#: src/models/format.md:78
msgid "How size is measured"
msgstr "大小如何测量"

#: src/models/format.md:80
msgid "The competition metric is:"
msgstr "比赛的度量是："

#: src/models/format.md:86
msgid "The node compresses nothing and estimates nothing. It measures both terms against digests it re-hashes, so **no way of packing your weights into the file can understate it**. `tinybrains check` reports it as `size metric`."
msgstr "节点不做压缩，也不做估算。两项都按它重新计算哈希后的摘要来测量，所以**无论怎样把权重打包进文件，都不会让它显得更小**。`tinybrains check` 以 `size metric` 报告这个值。"

#: src/models/format.md:90
msgid "**Raw bytes close a hole.** A metric that compressed the graph's _initializers_ would miss a graph that carries its trained weights as `Constant` node attributes: that graph has no initializers at all, and would measure as almost nothing."
msgstr "**原始字节堵住了一个漏洞**。如果度量对计算图的<em>初始化器</em>做压缩，就会漏掉把训练好的权重放在 `Constant` 节点属性里的计算图：那种图根本没有初始化器，测出来几乎为零。"

#: src/models/format.md:94
msgid "Admission assigns the smallest [weight class](weight-classes.md) that fits `S'`. It reports your parameter count beside the class, and the count plays no part in assigning it. A season may set its own cap on the count, which covers every value the document carries, wherever it carries it."
msgstr "审核分配能容纳 `S'` 的最小[重量级](weight-classes.md)。它在重量级旁报告你的参数数量，但参数数量不参与分配。赛季可以对参数数量另设上限，该上限涵盖文档携带的每一个数值，无论放在哪里。"

#: src/models/format.md:98
msgid "Hashes identify the files byte for byte, so a manifest edit that changes only formatting changes your hash and your size."
msgstr "哈希逐字节标识文件，所以哪怕只改了格式的清单编辑，也会改变你的哈希和大小。"

#: src/models/format.md:101
msgid "What is inspected"
msgstr "审核检查什么"

#: src/models/format.md:103
msgid "Admission re-hashes both files against what you declared and reads the graph from the protobuf (parameters, nodes, operators, IR version, opset). It builds a plan, runs five inferences on zero-filled inputs at your `probe_dims`, applies the platform's policy to what it measured, and runs your manifest over the game's reference observations. It reports the input shapes it used, what each adapter charged, and the measured inference time. **One time is a threshold: the probe's median must fit the game's turn**, 1,000 ms for Ants, because a model slower than a turn at the largest board cannot play one. No class caps your compute beyond that, and the turn deadline at play is the bound that matters."
msgstr "审核按你声明的值重新计算两个文件的哈希，并从 protobuf 中读取计算图（参数、节点、算子、IR 版本、opset）。它构建执行计划，在你的 `probe_dims` 下用全零输入运行五次推理，把平台的策略应用到测得的结果上，再在游戏的参考观测上运行你的清单。它报告所用的输入形状、每个适配器的开销，以及测得的推理时间。**有一个时间是门槛：探测的中位数必须在游戏的一个回合之内**，Ants 是 1,000 ms，因为在最大地图上比一个回合还慢的模型根本打不了一局。除此之外没有任何重量级限制你的算力，对局时的回合时限才是真正起作用的边界。"

#: src/models/format.md:112
msgid "[Testing before you submit](testing.md) shows how to make the same measurements on your machine with the same two libraries. A pass shows compatibility on the reference cases. It proves nothing about playing strength, and it does not guarantee that every future observation fits your budget."
msgstr "[提交前的测试](testing.md)介绍如何在你的机器上用同样的两个库做同样的测量。通过表示在参考用例上兼容。它完全不能证明对局实力，也不保证未来的每一份观测都在你的预算之内。"

#: src/models/weight-classes.md:3
msgid "TinyBrains groups entries by the size of the two files you submit. Admission assigns your class; you do not choose it when you submit. Every active entry carries one rating, on the Open ladder."
msgstr "TinyBrains 按你提交的两个文件的大小给参赛模型分组。重量级由审核分配，不由你在提交时选择。每个参赛中的作品都带有一个评分，位于无差别级天梯上。"

#: src/models/weight-classes.md:6
msgid "The classes are the season's"
msgstr "重量级由赛季决定"

#: src/models/weight-classes.md:8
msgid "**A season declares its own size limits, so read them from the season you are entering; this page shows the defaults.** The API returns them on every season it reports: `GET /v1/games/{game}` and `GET /v1/games/{game}/seasons` both carry a `weight_classes` table. The site shows them on the home page and beside your entry. A season may also offer only some of the classes. A focused season might run Nano alone, and admission rejects a model that measures into a class the season is not running with `CLASS_NOT_OFFERED`, a different refusal from being too large for every class."
msgstr "**每个赛季声明自己的大小限制，所以请从你要参加的赛季中读取；本页展示的是默认值**。API 在它报告的每个赛季上都会返回这些限制：`GET /v1/games/{game}` 和 `GET /v1/games/{game}/seasons` 都带有 `weight_classes` 表。网站在首页和你的参赛模型旁显示它们。赛季也可以只开放部分重量级。一个专注的赛季可能只开 Nano，模型若测量后落入赛季未开放的重量级，审核会以 `CLASS_NOT_OFFERED` 拒绝，这与对每个重量级都过大是不同的拒绝原因。"

#: src/models/weight-classes.md:15
msgid "These are the platform's starting limits, and a new season takes the previous season's limits as its default:"
msgstr "以下是平台的初始限制，新赛季默认沿用上一赛季的限制："

#: src/models/weight-classes.md:18 src/reference/glossary.md:14
msgid "Class"
msgstr "重量级"

