#: src/models/weight-classes.md:89
msgid "The deadline limits a big model before the class does"
msgstr "时限比重量级更早限制大模型"

#: src/models/weight-classes.md:91
msgid "The table is generous at the top, and the turn is tight. **Your seat owns the whole turn**: 1,000 ms, one `model_infer` call per seat with its own deadline. Even so, **a fully convolutional network over the largest Ants board runs out of turn long before it runs out of bytes.** To fill Mini and above, spend parameters where they cost less per turn: at a reduced resolution, or in a lookup the graph reads without multiplying. A wider copy of the same network runs out of turn first."
msgstr "表格的上端很宽裕，而回合很紧。**你的席位独占整个回合**：1,000 ms，每个席位一次 `model_infer` 调用，各有自己的时限。即便如此，**在最大的 Ants 地图上，全卷积网络耗尽回合时间远早于耗尽字节**。要填满 Mini 及以上的重量级，把参数花在每回合开销更低的地方：降低分辨率，或者放进计算图无需乘法即可读取的查找表。同一网络单纯加宽的版本会先耗尽回合时间。"

#: src/models/weight-classes.md:97
msgid "A convolution applies every parameter at every cell, so bytes and arithmetic move together, and no tuning separates them: one parameter costs one multiply-accumulate per cell, `2 × cells` arithmetic operations, and the kernel size, the grouping and the dtype leave that ratio unchanged. A class cap is a budget in bytes and the turn is a budget in arithmetic, and the two run out at different sizes."
msgstr "卷积在每个格子上都应用全部参数，所以字节数和运算量同步增长，任何调参都无法把它们分开：一个参数在每个格子上花费一次乘加，即 `2 × cells` 次算术运算，卷积核大小、分组和 dtype 都不会改变这个比例。重量级上限是字节预算，回合是运算预算，两者在不同的规模上耗尽。"

#: src/models/weight-classes.md:102
msgid "Admission refuses only a model whose probe at its `probe_dims` takes longer than a turn ([`PROBE_TOO_SLOW`](../reference/rejection-reasons.md)). A model that fits but runs close to the line finds out in play, where each missed turn is a [strike](../competing/matches.md)."
msgstr "审核只拒绝在其 `probe_dims` 下探测耗时超过一个回合的模型（[`PROBE_TOO_SLOW`](../reference/rejection-reasons.md)）。装得下但跑得接近临界的模型要到对局里才会发现问题，那里每错过一个回合就是一次[判罚](../competing/matches.md)。"

#: src/models/weight-classes.md:106
msgid "How admission decides your class"
msgstr "审核如何决定重量级"

#: src/models/weight-classes.md:108
msgid "The [size metric](format.md#how-size-is-measured) is `bytes(model.onnx) + bytes(manifest.json)`. Admission chooses the smallest class whose size limit contains that total **in the season you submitted to**. Admission makes no second check and never moves you to another class for more compute, since a class rations no compute."
msgstr "[大小度量](format.md#how-size-is-measured)是 `bytes(model.onnx) + bytes(manifest.json)`。审核在**你提交到的那个赛季**里选择大小限制能容纳这个总和的最小重量级。审核不做第二次检查，也绝不会因为算力把你挪到别的重量级，因为重量级不配给算力。"

#: src/models/weight-classes.md:113
msgid "Measure the pair's bytes. An estimate from parameter count misses graph metadata, an exporter's node names and the manifest's own length, which all count, and a larger manifest can push an unchanged network into the next class."
msgstr "直接测量这两个文件的字节数。按参数数量估算会漏掉计算图元数据、导出器的节点名称和清单本身的长度，而这些都算在内；清单变大可能把一个没有改动的网络推进下一个重量级。"

#: src/models/weight-classes.md:117
msgid "The Open ladder"
msgstr "无差别级天梯"

#: src/models/weight-classes.md:119
msgid "Open is the single rated ladder, and it spans every size. Each entry has one rating on it, and every match updates that one rating, whatever classes it paired."
msgstr "无差别级是唯一的评分天梯，涵盖所有大小。每个参赛模型在它上面只有一个评分，每场对局都更新这一个评分，无论配对的是哪些重量级。"

#: src/models/weight-classes.md:122
msgid "A weight class is a **view** of Open: it ranks you among versions in your size class, drawn from the same rating rather than a separate one. So compare entries of different sizes on Open directly, and read a class view to see how you rank among your size peers."
msgstr "重量级是无差别级的一个**视图**：它把你和同一大小级别的版本放在一起排名，用的是同一个评分而不是单独的评分。所以不同大小的参赛模型直接在无差别级上比较，而查看重量级视图可以了解你在同等体量的对手中排在哪里。"

#: src/models/weight-classes.md:126
msgid "Choosing what to enter"
msgstr "选择参赛的模型"

#: src/models/weight-classes.md:128
msgid "Begin with a model you can train, inspect and run without surprises. Measure size early, leave operation-budget headroom for larger observations, and watch your inference time against the turn deadline. Verify every basic board (together they span the game's limits) before you optimize for a boundary."
msgstr "从一个你能训练、检查和运行而不出意外的模型开始。尽早测量大小，为更大的观测留出算子预算余量，并盯住推理时间与回合时限的差距。在针对某个边界做优化之前，先在每张基础地图上验证（它们合起来覆盖游戏的全部限制）。"

#: src/models/weight-classes.md:133
msgid "Unused bytes within a class earn no score bonus. Size is the constraint you engineer against, and [ranking](../competing/ranking.md) comes from game results. Compare revisions by both their measured size and their match performance."
msgstr "重量级内没用完的字节不会带来任何加分。大小是你做工程时要对抗的约束，而[排名](../competing/ranking.md)来自对局结果。比较不同修订版时，既看实测大小，也看对局表现。"

#: src/models/adapters.md:3
msgid "Your entry is two files: the network, and `manifest.json`. The manifest declares what your graph takes and returns (each input and output by name, dtype and shape) and carries one small program per input: an **adapter** that turns the game's observation into that tensor. The graph never sees JSON, and the game never sees a tensor."
msgstr "你的参赛模型由两个文件组成：网络本身，以及 `manifest.json`。清单声明你的计算图接收什么、返回什么（每个输入和输出的名字、数据类型和形状），并为每个输入带上一段小程序：一个**适配器**，把游戏的观测变成那个张量。计算图从不接触 JSON，游戏也从不接触张量。"

#: src/models/adapters.md:8
msgid "An adapter is a JSONLogic expression tree with tensor operators: **data that the node evaluates** under an operation budget it counts itself. The platform hashes the manifest's exact bytes into your submission and **adds them to the graph's bytes** to give your size metric."
msgstr "适配器是一棵带张量操作符的 JSONLogic 表达式树：**由节点求值的数据**，并受节点自己计数的操作预算约束。平台把清单的原始字节哈希进你的提交，并**把它们加到计算图的字节数上**，得出你的大小指标。"

#: src/models/adapters.md:12
msgid "One turn, end to end"
msgstr "一个回合，从头到尾"

#: src/models/adapters.md:14
msgid "```text\nobservation (JSON)           {\"size\": [64, 96], \"mine\": [[12, 30], …], …}\n      │\n      ▼   adapter            the node evaluates your program, once per declared input\ntensors                      {\"board\": i8[1, 7, 64, 96]}\n      │\n      ▼   model.onnx         tract runs your graph\ntensors                      {\"policy\": f32[1, 5, 64, 96]}\n      │\n      ▼   the referee        the platform reads your policy head\naction (JSON)                [\"N\", \"-\", \"E\"]\n```"
msgstr "```text\n观测 (JSON)                  {\"size\": [64, 96], \"mine\": [[12, 30], …], …}\n      │\n      ▼   适配器             节点对你的程序求值，每个声明的输入各一次\n张量                         {\"board\": i8[1, 7, 64, 96]}\n      │\n      ▼   model.onnx         tract 运行你的计算图\n张量                         {\"policy\": f32[1, 5, 64, 96]}\n      │\n      ▼   裁判               平台读取你的策略头\n动作 (JSON)                  [\"N\", \"-\", \"E\"]\n```"

#: src/models/adapters.md:27
msgid "All three steps share one turn deadline, 1,000 ms for the whole seat, and each adapter has its own [budget](adapters/budget.md) of 1,000,000 operations."
msgstr "这三步共用一个回合时限，整个席位一共 1,000 ms；每个适配器各有自己的 1,000,000 次操作的[预算](adapters/budget.md)。"

#: src/models/adapters.md:30
msgid "**The last arrow is the referee's.** The channel order, the gather at your ants' cells and the argmax are rules of the _game_. [What your model answers](actions.md) is the whole contract, and a section below explains [why](#why-you-do-not-write-the-head)."
msgstr "**最后一个箭头属于裁判**。通道顺序、在你的蚂蚁所在格子上取值（gather）以及 argmax，都是<em>游戏</em>的规则。[模型回答什么](actions.md)就是全部的约定，下文有一节解释[原因](#why-you-do-not-write-the-head)。"

