#: src/models/adapters.md:154
msgid "`scatter` marks a 1 at each of your ants' coordinates on a board of `size`; `rle_expand` turns the water run-length list into a plane of the same size; `stack` puts them on a new leading axis, and `reshape` prepends the batch axis the declaration asks for. `{\"var\": \"size\"}` is `[64, 96]` for [the worked observation](observation.md#a-worked-example), so the result is `i8[1, 2, 64, 96]`: `H` binds to 64 and `W` to 96, and the output must match the same two."
msgstr "`scatter` 在一张 `size` 大小的地图上，在你每只蚂蚁的坐标处写入 1；`rle_expand` 把水域的游程列表展开成同样大小的平面；`stack` 把两者放到一个新的首轴上，`reshape` 再在前面加上声明要求的批次轴。对[示例观测](observation.md#a-worked-example)来说，`{\"var\": \"size\"}` 是 `[64, 96]`，所以结果是 `i8[1, 2, 64, 96]`：`H` 绑定为 64，`W` 绑定为 96，输出也必须与这两个值一致。"

#: src/models/adapters.md:160
msgid "Open the adapter in DataLogic Studio to see the arguments each operator receives:"
msgstr "在 DataLogic Studio 中打开这个适配器，看看每个操作符收到的参数："

#: src/models/adapters.md:165
msgid "The manifest is complete, and its encoding is poor: it ignores foes, food, hills and visibility. [A real manifest, piece by piece](adapters/walkthrough.md) covers the one the platform's own baselines play with."
msgstr "这份清单是完整的，但编码很差：它忽略了敌方蚂蚁、食物、蚁丘和视野。[逐段解读一份真实清单](adapters/walkthrough.md)讲的是平台自家基线所用的那一份。"

#: src/models/adapters.md:169
msgid "Why you do not write the head"
msgstr "为什么策略头不由你来写"

#: src/models/adapters.md:171
msgid "The manifest has no program that reads the graph's output and produces the move, and the reason explains a shape in your graph."
msgstr "清单里没有读取计算图输出并产生走法的程序，这背后的原因解释了你计算图中的一个形状。"

#: src/models/adapters.md:174
msgid "A result expression's document is **the output tensors alone**, without the observation. Reading a per-cell policy means gathering at your ants' cells, and those cells are in the _observation_, so no one could write that program unless the platform handed the observation back to it."
msgstr "result 表达式的文档**只有输出张量**，不含观测。读取逐格策略意味着在你的蚂蚁所在格子上取值，而那些格子在<em>观测</em>里，所以除非平台把观测交回去，否则没人写得出这个程序。"

#: src/models/adapters.md:178
msgid "The platform could hand it back. Instead the referee reads the head itself, because every entry's version of that program would be the same gather, character for character: the channel order is a rule of Ants, like the rule that a move is one cell. [What your model answers](actions.md) states that rule once, and no competitor's copy of it can differ by a detail."
msgstr "平台本可以把它交回去。但裁判选择自己读取策略头，因为每个参赛模型写出的这段程序都会是同一个取值操作，一个字符都不差：通道顺序是 Ants 的规则，就像“一步只能走一格”也是规则一样。[模型回答什么](actions.md)把这条规则写明一次，任何参赛者的副本都不可能在细节上有出入。"

#: src/models/adapters.md:183
msgid "**You gain** a free gather: those operations cost nothing against your budget, and a whole class of mistake (a transposed axis, a channel order off by one) cannot happen. **You lose** nothing you could use. Admission refuses a head in any shape but the two published ones, before the referee could mis-read it."
msgstr "**你得到的**是一次免费的取值：这些操作不计入你的预算，而且一整类错误（轴转置了、通道顺序差一位）根本不可能发生。**你失去的**没有任何你用得上的东西。策略头只要不是公布的两种形状之一，审核就会在裁判可能误读它之前先拒绝。"

#: src/models/adapters.md:188
msgid "Getting one right"
msgstr "把它写对"

#: src/models/adapters.md:190
msgid "Read [a real manifest](adapters/walkthrough.md) end to end: seven planes in, a per-cell policy out, and what each piece costs."
msgstr "从头到尾读一遍[一份真实的清单](adapters/walkthrough.md)：七个平面输入，逐格策略输出，以及每一段的开销。"

#: src/models/adapters.md:192
msgid "Open your adapters in [DataLogic Studio](adapters/studio.md) to watch the JSON half run, and learn the places where the Studio and the arena disagree."
msgstr "在 [DataLogic Studio](adapters/studio.md) 中打开你的适配器，观察 JSON 部分的运行，并记住 Studio 与竞技场不一致的地方。"

#: src/models/adapters.md:194
msgid "Keep [the expression language](adapters/dialect.md)'s scope rule in mind: inside `map`, `filter` and `reduce`, the document is the element, and an outer path reads `null` without an error."
msgstr "记住[表达式语言](adapters/dialect.md)的作用域规则：在 `map`、`filter` 和 `reduce` 内部，文档就是那个元素，读取外层路径得到 `null`，而且不会报错。"

#: src/models/adapters.md:196
msgid "Look up any operator in [Operators](adapters/operators.md), and its price in [The budget](adapters/budget.md)."
msgstr "任何操作符都可以在[操作符](adapters/operators.md)里查到，它的价格则在[预算](adapters/budget.md)里。"

#: src/models/adapters.md:198
msgid "Run [`tinybrains adapt`](testing.md#see-the-tensors-your-adapter-builds) and compare its tensors with your trainer's encoder, element for element, before you train on anything."
msgstr "在拿任何东西训练之前，先运行 [`tinybrains adapt`](testing.md#see-the-tensors-your-adapter-builds)，把它输出的张量与你训练器的编码器逐个元素比对。"

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:3
msgid "The trained models in the starter kit (`nano-bc` and `micro-bc` in [ants-starter/models](https://github.com/Tiny-Brains/ants-starter/tree/main/models), trained by [ants/baselines](https://github.com/Tiny-Brains/ants/tree/main/baselines)) play with one manifest, 930 bytes for `nano-bc` and one byte more for `micro-bc`, whose `name` is a character longer. It declares one input and one output, and its single adapter turns an observation into seven planes stacked as one tensor, `board: i8[1, 7, H, W]`. The graph answers `policy: f32[1, 5, H, W]`, and the referee reads it."
msgstr "入门套件里训练好的模型（[ants-starter/models](https://github.com/Tiny-Brains/ants-starter/tree/main/models) 中的 `nano-bc` 和 `micro-bc`，由 [ants/baselines](https://github.com/Tiny-Brains/ants/tree/main/baselines) 训练）共用一份清单：`nano-bc` 的是 930 字节，`micro-bc` 的多一个字节，因为它的 `name` 长一个字符。清单声明一个输入和一个输出，唯一的适配器把观测变成堆叠为一个张量的七个平面，`board: i8[1, 7, H, W]`。计算图回答 `policy: f32[1, 5, H, W]`，由裁判读取。"

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:11
msgid "The baselines generate it. `ants/baselines/src/tb_baselines/planes.py` declares each plane once, with two renderings side by side (the JSONLogic below, and the numpy the trainer uses), and a test proves the two agree. [The same encoding in your trainer](#the-same-encoding-in-your-trainer) shows why your trainer needs that test too."
msgstr "这份清单由基线生成。`ants/baselines/src/tb_baselines/planes.py` 把每个平面只声明一次，并排给出两种写法（下面的 JSONLogic，以及训练器所用的 numpy），再用一个测试证明两者一致。[训练器里的同一套编码](#the-same-encoding-in-your-trainer)解释了为什么你的训练器也需要这个测试。"

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:16
msgid "Every fragment below has a link that opens it in [DataLogic Studio](studio.md), against this illustrative observation:"
msgstr "下面每个片段都带一个链接，可以在 [DataLogic Studio](studio.md) 中打开，针对的是这个示意性的观测："

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:26
msgid "It holds three ants (one on your hill at `[12, 30]`, one beside it, and a third within sight of the enemy hill at `[44, 70]`), a foe next to the first two, one food, three cells of known water on row 13, and the eleven cells visible this turn."
msgstr "它包含三只蚂蚁（一只在你位于 `[12, 30]` 的蚁丘上，一只在它旁边，第三只在能看到位于 `[44, 70]` 的敌方蚁丘的位置）、一只紧挨着前两只的敌方蚂蚁、一份食物、第 13 行上三格已知的水域，以及本回合可见的十一格。"

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:30
msgid "The declaration"
msgstr "声明"

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:38
msgid "`H` and `W` are **names**. They bind to the size of the board each call brings, and because the output names the same two, the graph must answer at the size it received. A season's boards can be any size from 24 to 124 a side and at most 14,880 squares, and one admitted session serves them all. This manifest's `probe_dims` admits it at 128 × 128, 16,384 squares, which is more than any board the game allows, so its probe covers every board. The largest is 14,880 squares, the 120 × 124 basic board: declare at least that in a manifest of your own ([why](../adapters.md#probe-at-the-biggest-board))."
msgstr "`H` 和 `W` 是**名字**。它们绑定到每次调用带来的地图尺寸，而由于输出也用了同样的两个名字，计算图必须按收到的尺寸作答。一个赛季的地图边长可以是 24 到 124 之间的任意值，最多 14,880 格，一个通过审核的会话就能应对全部。这份清单的 `probe_dims` 让它按 128 × 128、即 16,384 格通过审核，比游戏允许的任何地图都大，所以它的探测覆盖了每一张地图。最大的地图是 14,880 格，即 120 × 124 的基础地图：在你自己的清单里至少要声明这么大（[原因](../adapters.md#probe-at-the-biggest-board)）。"

