#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:207
msgid "**You pay for the board's cells.** The node charges a plane-building operator for every cell it produces, whether or not it writes anything there. Five scatters and two RLE expansions each produce a full grid, and the stack reads all seven planes again: fourteen charges per cell, 208,320 at 120 × 124. The ants, foes, food and hills add a few operations each, and everything else is noise."
msgstr "**你为地图的格子付费**。构建平面的操作符每产出一格，节点就计一次费，不管那一格有没有写入东西。五次散布和两次游程展开各自产出一整张网格，堆叠又把七个平面全部读一遍：每格十四次计费，在 120 × 124 的地图上就是 208,320 次。蚂蚁、敌方蚂蚁、食物和蚁丘各自再加几次操作，其余都是零头。"

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:212
msgid "The referee gathers the policy at your ants and charges your budget nothing for it ([why](../adapters.md#why-you-do-not-write-the-head)). A program of your own that read the policy back would pay for all five channels of every cell: another 82,000 operations at 128 × 128, a third of the total."
msgstr "裁判在你的蚂蚁处取策略值，不向你的预算收一分钱（[原因](../adapters.md#why-you-do-not-write-the-head)）。如果由你自己的程序读回策略，就要为每一格的全部五个通道付费：在 128 × 128 的地图上又是 82,000 次操作，占总数的三分之一。"

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:217
msgid "[The budget](budget.md#what-each-operator-charges) lists what every operator charges."
msgstr "[预算](budget.md#what-each-operator-charges)列出了每个操作符的计费。"

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:219
msgid "Where the head goes"
msgstr "策略头的去向"

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:221
msgid "The graph answers `policy: f32[1, 5, H, W]`, five scores for every move at every cell. The referee gathers the five channels at each of your ants' cells, in `mine` order, and takes the argmax of each. The channel order is `N, E, S, W, -`, published in [What your model answers](../actions.md#the-two-head-shapes)."
msgstr "计算图回答 `policy: f32[1, 5, H, W]`，每一格每种走法各一个分数。裁判在你每只蚂蚁所在的格子上取出五个通道，按 `mine` 的顺序，对每一个取 argmax。通道顺序是 `N, E, S, W, -`，公布在[模型回答什么](../actions.md#the-two-head-shapes)里。"

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:226
msgid "Your graph's channels must mean the letters in that order. The baselines put the hold, `-`, last. A graph whose last channel wins everywhere plays valid actions, and its whole colony stands still for the entire match. [Testing](../testing.md#check-the-actions-too) shows one, and how to count your own moves."
msgstr "你的计算图的各个通道必须按这个顺序对应这些字母。基线把原地不动 `-` 放在最后。一个最后一个通道处处胜出的计算图，走的都是合法动作，而整个蚁群会整场对局一动不动。[测试](../testing.md#check-the-actions-too)展示了这样一个例子，以及如何统计你自己的走法。"

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:231
msgid "If your graph indexes into the board itself and answers `[N, 5]` in `mine` order, declare that shape instead and the referee skips the gather. It is cheaper on large boards, and it limits which axes you may name ([why](../adapters.md#a-dimension-may-be-a-name))."
msgstr "如果你的计算图自己对地图做索引，按 `mine` 的顺序回答 `[N, 5]`，那就改为声明这个形状，裁判会跳过取值这一步。它在大地图上更便宜，但会限制你可以给哪些轴起名字（[原因](../adapters.md#a-dimension-may-be-a-name)）。"

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:235
msgid "The same encoding in your trainer"
msgstr "训练器里的同一套编码"

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:237
msgid "A model you train in Python sees observations through a numpy encoder and plays through `manifest.json`: one encoding, written twice. If the two disagree, nothing fails. The model trains on one distribution and plays on another, and the only symptom is a rating below what training promised."
msgstr "你用 Python 训练的模型，通过 numpy 编码器看到观测，通过 `manifest.json` 参赛：同一套编码，写了两遍。如果两者不一致，不会有任何报错。模型在一个分布上训练，在另一个分布上比赛，唯一的症状是评分低于训练时的预期。"

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:242
msgid "Copy the baselines' answer. `planes.py` declares every plane once, with both renderings next to each other, and `tests/test_adapter_conformance.py` runs `tinybrains adapt` (**datalogic, the evaluator a node runs the manifest on**) over the cartridge's reference observations and asserts that the adapter's tensors equal the numpy encoder's, element for element:"
msgstr "照抄基线的做法。`planes.py` 把每个平面只声明一次，两种写法并排放在一起；`tests/test_adapter_conformance.py` 运行 `tinybrains adapt`（**datalogic，节点运行清单所用的求值器**）处理卡带的参考观测，并断言适配器的张量与 numpy 编码器的张量逐个元素相等："

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:248 src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:249
msgid "\"case-"
msgstr "\"case-"

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:248 src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:249
msgid "\""
msgstr "\""

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:248
msgid "\"board.npy\""
msgstr "\"board.npy\""

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:248
msgid "# the ladder's own tensor\n"
msgstr "# 天梯自己的张量\n"

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:249
msgid "\"observation.json\""
msgstr "\"observation.json\""

#: src/models/adapters/walkthrough.md:253
msgid "[Testing before you submit](../testing.md#see-the-tensors-your-adapter-builds) shows the command."
msgstr "[提交前的测试](../testing.md#see-the-tensors-your-adapter-builds)给出了命令。"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:3
msgid "[DataLogic Studio](https://goplasmatic.github.io/datalogic-rs/playground/) is a visual editor and debugger for JSONLogic, built on datalogic-rs, **the engine the platform runs your adapter on**. The Studio runs the arena's language: it draws your adapter as a flow diagram, runs it against an observation, and steps through the evaluation one node at a time."
msgstr "[DataLogic Studio](https://goplasmatic.github.io/datalogic-rs/playground/) 是 JSONLogic 的可视化编辑器和调试器，基于 datalogic-rs 构建，**也就是平台运行你适配器所用的引擎**。Studio 运行的就是竞技场的语言：它把你的适配器画成流程图，拿一个观测运行它，并逐节点单步跟踪求值。"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:8
msgid "Every example in this chapter has an **Open in DataLogic Studio** link. The link carries the expression and the data, so it opens that example evaluated, with no account and nothing to save. A link you make works the same way: it carries your adapter, and anyone you send it to can read it."
msgstr "本章的每个示例都有一个 **Open in DataLogic Studio** 链接。链接里带着表达式和数据，所以打开时该示例已经求值完毕，不需要账户，也没有什么要保存的。你自己生成的链接也一样：它带着你的适配器，你发给谁，谁就能读。"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:12
msgid "The Studio still differs from the referee in a few narrow places, and the table below lists them."
msgstr "Studio 与裁判仍有几处细微差别，下面的表格一一列出。"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:14
msgid "Opening your own adapter"
msgstr "打开你自己的适配器"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:16
msgid "Open the [Studio](https://goplasmatic.github.io/datalogic-rs/playground/)."
msgstr "打开 [Studio](https://goplasmatic.github.io/datalogic-rs/playground/)。"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:17
msgid "Tick **Templating**, above the diagram."
msgstr "勾选图表上方的 **Templating**。"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:18
msgid "Paste **one adapter** into Logic: the value of one input's `adapter` key, without the rest of the manifest."
msgstr "把**一个适配器**粘贴进 Logic：也就是某个输入的 `adapter` 键的值，不带清单的其余部分。"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:20
msgid "Paste an observation into Data."
msgstr "把一个观测粘贴进 Data。"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:21
msgid "**Share** copies a link to what is on the screen."
msgstr "**Share** 会复制一个指向屏幕上内容的链接。"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:23
msgid "For observations to paste, [What your model sees](../observation.md#a-worked-example) has a small one, and `tinybrains adapt` writes every reference observation beside the tensors it produced, as `case-N/observation.json` ([how](../testing.md#see-the-tensors-your-adapter-builds))."
msgstr "可以粘贴的观测，[模型看到什么](../observation.md#a-worked-example)里有一个小的；`tinybrains adapt` 会把每个参考观测写在它生成的张量旁边，文件名为 `case-N/observation.json`（[方法](../testing.md#see-the-tensors-your-adapter-builds)）。"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:27
msgid "What you are looking at"
msgstr "你看到的是什么"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:29
msgid "**Logic, Data, Result.** Result holds the Studio's output. For an adapter, that is the tensor call at the top with its arguments evaluated: `{\"scatter\": [[[12, 30], [13, 30], [43, 66]], [64, 96], \"i8\"]}` says that the node's `scatter` will receive those three points, that shape, and that dtype."
msgstr "**Logic、Data、Result**。Result 是 Studio 的输出。对适配器来说，那是顶层的张量调用及其求值后的参数：`{\"scatter\": [[[12, 30], [13, 30], [43, 66]], [64, 96], \"i8\"]}` 表示节点的 `scatter` 将收到这三个点、这个形状和这个数据类型。"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:33
msgid "**The diagram.** The Studio draws each operator as a node, with its inputs flowing in. **Flow** draws the data left to right; **Hierarchy** draws the JSON's nesting."
msgstr "**图表**。Studio 把每个操作符画成一个节点，它的输入流入其中。**Flow** 从左到右画数据流；**Hierarchy** 画的是 JSON 的嵌套结构。"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:35
msgid "**The debugger.** The step controls walk the evaluation one node at a time, and the current node shows the value it produced. Stepping is the quickest way to watch a `map` body receive each element in turn, or a `reduce` accumulator grow."
msgstr "**调试器**。单步控件让求值逐节点推进，当前节点显示它产生的值。要观察 `map` 主体如何依次收到每个元素，或者 `reduce` 的累加器如何增长，单步是最快的办法。"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:39
msgid "Where the Studio and the arena differ"
msgstr "Studio 与竞技场的差异"

