msgstr "节点链接的版本，记录在你的版本上，字段为 `orion_version`"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:53
msgid "**Remember the objects rows**: an object is data in all three places, so an expression that returns `{\"mine\": …, \"theirs\": …}` gives a tidy result in the Studio, and a node refuses it because it is not a tensor. Return an array."
msgstr "**记住关于对象的那几行**：对象在这三处都是数据，所以返回 `{\"mine\": …, \"theirs\": …}` 的表达式在 Studio 里会得到一个整齐的结果，而节点会拒绝它，因为它不是张量。请返回数组。"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:57
msgid "A trap the Studio reproduces"
msgstr "Studio 也会重现的陷阱"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:59
msgid "`{\"var\": \"3\"}` on a `[row, col, owner]` triple is `null`, and `null` compares equal to `0`. This filter keeps **every** hill, yours and your opponents', and neither the Studio nor the arena reports a problem:"
msgstr "对 `[row, col, owner]` 三元组求 `{\"var\": \"3\"}` 得到的是 `null`，而 `null` 与 `0` 比较时相等。这个 filter 会保留**每一个**蚁丘，你的和对手的都在内，而 Studio 和竞技场都不会报任何问题："

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:64
msgid "\"3\""
msgstr "\"3\""

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:70
msgid "This is the most expensive mistake an adapter can make, and the Studio shows it the way the arena runs it. To avoid it, compare with `===`, read a field that resolves, or give `var` a fallback: `{\"var\": [\"3\", -1]}`."
msgstr "这是适配器能犯的代价最高的错误，而 Studio 展示它的方式与竞技场运行它的方式一致。要避免它，请用 `===` 比较，读取一个确实存在的字段，或者给 `var` 一个回退值：`{\"var\": [\"3\", -1]}`。"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:74
msgid "When the Studio is enough, and when it is not"
msgstr "Studio 够用和不够用的时候"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:76
msgid "The Studio shows you whether your JSON half picks out the right things: the right lists, fields, coordinates and shape. A scope mistake, a filter on the wrong field, or a shape assembled in the wrong order shows up in the Result pane."
msgstr "Studio 能告诉你 JSON 部分是否挑出了正确的东西：正确的列表、字段、坐标和形状。作用域错误、filter 用错了字段、形状拼装顺序不对，都会在 Result 面板里显露出来。"

#: src/models/adapters/studio.md:80
msgid "The Studio cannot tell you whether your adapter builds the tensor your graph was trained on, fits the budget, or produces a tensor the graph accepts. [`tinybrains adapt`](../testing.md#see-the-tensors-your-adapter-builds) writes out the tensors and what each one charged, and [`tinybrains check`](../testing.md#check-it-the-way-admission-will) measures what admission measures."
msgstr "Studio 无法告诉你适配器构建的张量是否就是你的计算图训练时用的那个、是否在预算之内、计算图是否接受它。[`tinybrains adapt`](../testing.md#see-the-tensors-your-adapter-builds) 会写出张量和每一个的计费，[`tinybrains check`](../testing.md#check-it-the-way-admission-will) 测量的则正是审核所测量的东西。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:3
msgid "An adapter is JSONLogic, evaluated by **datalogic**, the expression engine the platform's own workflows run on, with its tensor operators. JSONLogic is a published language with its own reference. This page covers the part an adapter uses and the rules that catch people out."
msgstr "适配器是一段 JSONLogic，由 **datalogic** 求值；这是平台自身工作流所运行的表达式引擎，外加它的张量操作符。JSONLogic 是一门公开发布的语言，有自己的参考文档。本页只讲适配器用到的那部分，以及容易让人踩坑的规则。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:7
msgid "The node that admits your model and the node that plays it run the same engine at the same version, and both count every operation they evaluate. A general JSONLogic engine, [DataLogic Studio](studio.md) included, runs the JSON half the same way (with the differences that page lists) and counts nothing."
msgstr "审核你模型的节点和运行它比赛的节点使用同一版本的同一引擎，两者都会统计求值的每一次运算。通用的 JSONLogic 引擎，包括 [DataLogic Studio](studio.md)，以同样的方式运行其中的 JSON 部分（差异见那一页所列），但不统计任何运算。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:12
msgid "Expressions, and the one rule about objects"
msgstr "表达式，以及关于对象的唯一规则"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:14
msgid "A number, a string, `true`, `false` or `null` evaluates to itself. An array evaluates each of its elements. The node evaluates an adapter in datalogic's templating mode, and `tinybrains check` and `tinybrains adapt` evaluate it on the same engine, so one rule decides what an object means:"
msgstr "数字、字符串、`true`、`false` 和 `null` 求值得到自身。数组会对每个元素求值。节点以 datalogic 的模板模式对适配器求值，`tinybrains check` 和 `tinybrains adapt` 用同一引擎求值，所以一个对象的含义由一条规则决定："

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:18
msgid "**An object whose only key names an operator is an operation.** The key is the operator's name, and the value is the argument list."
msgstr "**只有一个键、且这个键是操作符名称的对象，就是一次运算**。键是操作符的名称，值是参数列表。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:21
msgid "Every other object is data. An object with more than one key is a template: the engine evaluates each value and returns an object with the same keys. An object whose only key names no operator comes back as it is."
msgstr "其他所有对象都是数据。有多个键的对象是模板：引擎对每个值求值，返回一个键相同的对象。只有一个键但这个键不是任何操作符名称的对象，原样返回。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:25
msgid "**Keep your values out of objects.** A program's values are scalars, arrays and tensors. An adapter that returns `{\"mine\": …, \"theirs\": …}` returns no tensor, and the node refuses it. To carry two things through a `reduce`, use an array: `[width, points]`, which you read back as `accumulator.0` and `accumulator.1`, and which has no key an operator could claim."
msgstr "**不要把你的值放进对象里**。程序的值是标量、数组和张量。返回 `{\"mine\": …, \"theirs\": …}` 的适配器没有返回张量，节点会拒绝它。要在 `reduce` 中传递两样东西，用数组：`[width, points]`，读回时写成 `accumulator.0` 和 `accumulator.1`，而且它没有任何可能被操作符占用的键。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:30
msgid "**A misspelt operator is data.** `{\"scattr\": …}` names no operator, so the engine returns it as an object, and your adapter fails later, where that object reaches a tensor operator or stands in for the tensor your adapter returns. A misspelling inside a condition fails nowhere: `{\"if\": [{\"=\": [a, b]}, …]}` takes its first branch every time, because an object is truthy. `tinybrains check` and `tinybrains adapt` print a warning for every single-key object whose key names no operator, with its path in the adapter. Read those warnings before you submit: the node gives none."
msgstr "**拼错的操作符是数据**。`{\"scattr\": …}` 不是任何操作符的名称，所以引擎把它当作对象返回，你的适配器会在后面某处失败：这个对象传到了某个张量操作符，或者顶替了适配器本该返回的张量。条件里的拼写错误则哪里都不会失败：`{\"if\": [{\"=\": [a, b]}, …]}` 每次都走第一个分支，因为对象为真。`tinybrains check` 和 `tinybrains adapt` 会对每一个键不对应任何操作符的单键对象打印警告，并给出它在适配器中的路径。提交前先读这些警告：节点不会给出任何警告。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:38
msgid "An operator's arguments go in an array, and you may write a single argument bare: `{\"var\": \"mine\"}` is `{\"var\": [\"mine\"]}`."
msgstr "操作符的参数放在数组里，单个参数可以不加数组直接写：`{\"var\": \"mine\"}` 就是 `{\"var\": [\"mine\"]}`。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:41
msgid "**A key that collides with an operator calls it.** Seven of the tensor operators are ordinary words (`shape`, `full`, `cast`, `pad`, `crop`, `concat`, `stack`), so the engine evaluates an object you meant as data if one of those is its only key. Escape the key with `$`: `{\"$shape\": [6, 7]}` is the data `{\"shape\": [6, 7]}`, on the node and in `tinybrains`. A `$`\\-escaped key is data by intent, so `tinybrains` gives no warning for it."
msgstr "**与操作符同名的键会调用它**。张量操作符中有七个是普通单词（`shape`、`full`、`cast`、`pad`、`crop`、`concat`、`stack`），所以你本想写成数据的对象，如果唯一的键是其中之一，引擎就会把它当作运算求值。用 `$` 转义这个键：`{\"$shape\": [6, 7]}` 就是数据 `{\"shape\": [6, 7]}`，在节点上和在 `tinybrains` 中都是如此。用 `$` 转义的键是有意写成的数据，所以 `tinybrains` 不会对它发出警告。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:47
msgid "Core operators"
msgstr "核心操作符"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:49
msgid "An adapter has these operators and the tensor operators in [Operators](operators.md). datalogic's extension families are on as well: more string, array and math operators, `try` and `throw`, and date operators. A single key that names none of them is data."
msgstr "适配器可以使用这些操作符，以及[操作符](operators.md)一页中的张量操作符。datalogic 的扩展操作符族也已启用：更多的字符串、数组和数学操作符，`try` 和 `throw`，以及日期操作符。单个键若不是其中任何一个的名称，就是数据。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:53
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr "用途"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:55
msgid "Access and presence"
msgstr "访问与存在性"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:55
msgid "`var`, `val`, `missing`, `missing_some`, `??`"
msgstr "`var`, `val`, `missing`, `missing_some`, `??`"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:56
msgid "Branching and Boolean logic"
msgstr "分支与布尔逻辑"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:56
msgid "`if`, `?:`, `!`, `!!`, `and`, `or`"
msgstr "`if`, `?:`, `!`, `!!`, `and`, `or`"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:57
msgid "Comparisons"
msgstr "比较"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:57
msgid "`==`, `===`, `!=`, `!==`, `>`, `>=`, `<`, `<=`"
msgstr "`==`, `===`, `!=`, `!==`, `>`, `>=`, `<`, `<=`"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:58
msgid "Scalar arithmetic"
msgstr "标量算术"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:58
msgid "`+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `%`, `max`, `min`, `abs`, `ceil`, `floor`"
msgstr "`+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `%`, `max`, `min`, `abs`, `ceil`, `floor`"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:59
msgid "Strings and membership"
msgstr "字符串与成员判断"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:59
msgid "`cat`, `substr`, `in`"
msgstr "`cat`, `substr`, `in`"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:60
msgid "Collections"
msgstr "集合"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:60
msgid "`merge`, `map`, `filter`, `reduce`, `all`, `some`, `none`, `length`, `slice`, `sort`, `distinct`"
msgstr "`merge`, `map`, `filter`, `reduce`, `all`, `some`, `none`, `length`, `slice`, `sort`, `distinct`"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:61
msgid "Object inspection"
msgstr "对象检查"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:61
msgid "`keys`, `values`, `entries`, `type`"
msgstr "`keys`, `values`, `entries`, `type`"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:63
msgid "Two exceptions apply to every adapter:"
msgstr "有两条例外适用于每个适配器："

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:65
msgid "**`secret`, `now` and `random` are refused.** An adapter may not read the deployment's secrets, and a replay of an inference must reproduce the same tensors, so it may not read the clock or draw randomness either. The node refuses an adapter that uses any of the three at upload, and so does `tinybrains`."
msgstr "**`secret`、`now` 和 `random` 会被拒绝**。适配器不能读取部署的密钥；而重放一次推理必须得到相同的张量，所以它也不能读时钟或取随机数。上传时，节点会拒绝用了这三者之一的适配器，`tinybrains` 也一样。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:69
msgid "**Orion's own operators run only on the node.** The node also has `join` and the `base64`, `base64url`, `hex` and `url` codecs (`base64_encode`, `hex_decode` and the rest). `tinybrains` cannot evaluate them, so it refuses an adapter that calls one rather than test something else. Keep them out of an adapter."
msgstr "**Orion 自有的操作符只在节点上运行**。节点还有 `join`，以及 `base64`、`base64url`、`hex` 和 `url` 编解码器（`base64_encode`、`hex_decode` 等）。`tinybrains` 无法对它们求值，所以它会拒绝调用了其中任何一个的适配器，而不是去测试别的东西。不要在适配器里用它们。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:74
msgid "`if`, `and` and `or` evaluate only the branches they need, and a branch they skip costs nothing. `??` returns its first argument that is not `null`. `/` and `%` by zero return `null` and leave the turn running, so follow them with `??` when a count can be zero. `>`, `>=`, `<` and `<=` compare two strings as strings and anything else as numbers, and take a third argument for a range: `{\"<=\": [0, {\"var\": \"0\"}, 63]}` is `0 ≤ row ≤ 63`. `sort` orders values that read as numbers by value, and the rest as text."
msgstr "`if`、`and` 和 `or` 只对需要的分支求值，跳过的分支没有开销。`??` 返回第一个不是 `null` 的参数。`/` 和 `%` 除以零时返回 `null`，回合照常进行，所以当计数可能为零时，在后面接一个 `??`。`>`、`>=`、`<` 和 `<=` 比较两个字符串时按字符串比较，其他情况按数字比较，并可接受第三个参数表示区间：`{\"<=\": [0, {\"var\": \"0\"}, 63]}` 就是 `0 ≤ row ≤ 63`。`sort` 把能读作数字的值按数值排序，其余按文本排序。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:81
msgid "**The language has no regular expression operator.** `match` works as a `switch` and takes no pattern. To branch on a string, test it for equality."
msgstr "**这门语言没有正则表达式操作符**。`match` 的作用相当于 `switch`，不接受模式。要按字符串分支，就测试它是否相等。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:84
msgid "Variables and scope"
msgstr "变量与作用域"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:86
msgid "`{\"var\": \"size.0\"}` reads the first element of `size`: a path splits on `.`, and a number indexes an array. An empty path, `{\"var\": \"\"}`, is the whole document. A path that does not resolve reads `null`, unless you give `var` a second argument as its fallback: `{\"var\": [\"hills.0.2\", -1]}`."
msgstr "`{\"var\": \"size.0\"}` 读取 `size` 的第一个元素：路径按 `.` 拆分，数字用来索引数组。空路径 `{\"var\": \"\"}` 是整个文档。解析不到的路径读到 `null`，除非你给 `var` 第二个参数作为后备值：`{\"var\": [\"hills.0.2\", -1]}`。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:90
msgid "**Inside `map`, `filter`, `all`, `some` and `none`, the document is the element.** For a coordinate pair, `{\"var\": \"0\"}` is its row. An outer path read from inside a body reads `null` without failing:"
msgstr "**在 `map`、`filter`、`all`、`some` 和 `none` 内部，文档就是当前元素**。对一个坐标对来说，`{\"var\": \"0\"}` 是它的行。在循环体内读取外层路径会读到 `null`，而不会失败："

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:94 src/models/adapters/dialect.md:144
msgid "\"size.1\""
msgstr "\"size.1\""

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:100
msgid "Every ant comes back with a `null` where you meant the board's width to be. `scatter` reads a `null` coordinate as `0`, so every point lands in column 0 and nothing reports a problem."
msgstr "每只蚂蚁返回的结果里，你本想放地图宽度的位置都是 `null`。`scatter` 把 `null` 坐标读作 `0`，于是每个点都落在第 0 列，而且没有任何东西报告问题。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:103
msgid "Reaching outwards, and the one place you cannot"
msgstr "向外访问，以及唯一不能访问的地方"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:105
msgid "`{\"val\": [[N], …]}` climbs out of an iterator. A leading `[N]` at or above the number of enclosing iterators resolves against the **root** document, so from inside one `map` over `mine`:"
msgstr "`{\"val\": [[N], …]}` 可以从迭代器中向外跳出。开头的 `[N]` 若等于或超过外层迭代器的层数，就会相对**根**文档解析，所以在一个遍历 `mine` 的 `map` 内部："

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:109 src/models/adapters/dialect.md:168
msgid "\"val\""
msgstr "\"val\""

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:115
msgid "**One level up from one iterator is the root, with nothing in between.** Inside a _nested_ iterator you cannot address the enclosing element: `{\"val\": [[1], …]}` reads the innermost frame, and every higher level resolves against the root. You cannot write a cross product whose inner body needs the outer element as two nested iterators, and no missing operator causes that: the scope rule sets the limit. (The observation carries [`vis`](../observation.md#what-you-can-see-this-turn) for this reason: a visibility mask is a disk drawn per ant, the exact shape this rule forbids.)"
msgstr "**从一个迭代器向上一层就是根，中间没有别的层级**。在 _嵌套_ 的迭代器里，你无法访问外层元素：`{\"val\": [[1], …]}` 读取最内层，再往上的每一层都相对根解析。你不能用两层嵌套迭代器写出内层循环体需要外层元素的笛卡尔积，而这不是缺了某个操作符造成的：是作用域规则划定了界限。（观测正因此携带了 [`vis`](../observation.md#what-you-can-see-this-turn)：视野掩码是按每只蚂蚁画出的一个圆盘，恰好是这条规则所禁止的形状。）"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:122
msgid "**`reduce` reaches outward.** Its body sees `{\"current\": <element>, \"accumulator\": <so far>}`, and the engine evaluates its third argument, the starting accumulator, _outside_ the loop. Put an outer value the body needs into the accumulator, and each step hands it on. **Make the accumulator an array**, which no operator name can claim:"
msgstr "**`reduce` 能向外访问**。它的循环体看到的是 `{\"current\": <element>, \"accumulator\": <so far>}`，而引擎在循环 _之外_ 对它的第三个参数（初始累加器）求值。把循环体需要的外层值放进累加器，每一步都会把它传下去。**把累加器写成数组**，这样就没有操作符名称能占用它："

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:128 src/models/adapters/dialect.md:130
msgid "\"reduce\""
msgstr "\"reduce\""

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:133 src/models/adapters/dialect.md:138
msgid "\"accumulator.0\""
msgstr "\"accumulator.0\""

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:135
msgid "\"accumulator.1\""
msgstr "\"accumulator.1\""

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:137
msgid "\"+\""
msgstr "\"+\""

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:138
msgid "\"*\""
msgstr "\"*\""

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:138
msgid "\"current.0\""
msgstr "\"current.0\""

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:139 src/models/adapters/dialect.md:147
msgid "\"current.1\""
msgstr "\"current.1\""

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:155
msgid "Copy three things from that example:"
msgstr "从那个例子里照搬三点："

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:157
msgid "The body returns the **whole** accumulator, `[width, indices]`, or the next step loses the width."
msgstr "循环体返回**整个**累加器 `[width, indices]`，否则下一步就丢了宽度。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:158
msgid "You read the two halves as `accumulator.0` and `accumulator.1`. They have no names."
msgstr "两个部分分别以 `accumulator.0` 和 `accumulator.1` 读取。它们没有名字。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:159
msgid "The outer `{\"reduce\": [[<inner>], {\"var\": \"current.1\"}, null]}` gets the part you wanted out: a reduce over a one-element array whose body projects. It costs one operation, and it is the only way to index into a value the program computed, as against one the document holds."
msgstr "外层的 `{\"reduce\": [[<inner>], {\"var\": \"current.1\"}, null]}` 把你想要的那部分取出来：对一个单元素数组做 reduce，循环体只做投影。它只花一次运算，也是对程序计算出的值（而不是文档中已有的值）做索引的唯一办法。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:163
msgid "A path segment may be computed"
msgstr "路径段可以计算得出"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:165
msgid "The engine evaluates `{\"val\": …}`'s segments, so a computed index works as a path:"
msgstr "引擎会对 `{\"val\": …}` 的各段求值，所以计算出的索引可以用作路径："

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:168
msgid "\"data\""
msgstr "\"data\""

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:168
msgid "\"dirs\""
msgstr "\"dirs\""

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:168
msgid "\"\""
msgstr "\"\""

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:171
msgid "reads `dirs[i]` from the root, where `i` is the element. It turns an index into a name with no `at` operator, and replaces a nested `if` chain that costs one comparison per branch."
msgstr "从根读取 `dirs[i]`，其中 `i` 是当前元素。它不需要 `at` 操作符就把索引变成了名称，还取代了每个分支都要花一次比较的嵌套 `if` 链。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:174
msgid "Tensor values"
msgstr "张量值"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:176
msgid "A tensor is an opaque value with a shape and a dtype, which one tensor operator makes and another consumes. It is not a nested JSON array. A program may ask it two things, `shape` and `dtype`, and nothing else: no indexing, no `map`, no arithmetic."
msgstr "张量是一个不透明的值，带有形状和数据类型，由一个张量操作符生成、另一个消费。它不是嵌套的 JSON 数组。程序只能向它询问两件事，`shape` 和 `dtype`，别的都不行：不能索引，不能 `map`，不能做算术。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:180
msgid "The dtypes are `bool`, `i8`, `u8`, `i16`, `u16`, `i32`, `u32`, `i64`, `u64`, `f32` and `f64`. The operators that only move bytes also serve `f16` and `bf16`."
msgstr "数据类型有 `bool`、`i8`、`u8`、`i16`、`u16`、`i32`、`u32`、`i64`、`u64`、`f32` 和 `f64`。只搬运字节的操作符还支持 `f16` 和 `bf16`。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:183
msgid "On the wire a tensor is `{\"tensor\": {\"dtype\", \"shape\", \"data\": \"<base64>\"}}`, and you see that form if you print one. A program cannot build a tensor that way."
msgstr "在传输格式中，张量是 `{\"tensor\": {\"dtype\", \"shape\", \"data\": \"<base64>\"}}`，打印一个张量时你看到的就是这种形式。程序不能用这种方式构造张量。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:186
msgid "A tensor is truthy, and equal only to itself. [Operators](operators.md) lists the ways into a tensor, and the ways back out."
msgstr "张量为真，而且只与自身相等。[操作符](operators.md)一页列出了进入张量的途径，以及从张量回来的途径。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:189
msgid "Equality and truth"
msgstr "相等与真值"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:191
msgid "`==` compares the way JavaScript does, with one rule to remember: **`{\"==\": [0, null]}` is true.** An unresolved path reads as `null`, and `null` compares equal to every falsy value. A filter written against a path that does not resolve neither fails nor returns an empty list: it selects the falsy elements, and looks right for as long as the value it compares against is zero."
msgstr "`==` 的比较方式和 JavaScript 一样，要记住一条规则：**`{\"==\": [0, null]}` 为真**。解析不到的路径读作 `null`，而 `null` 与每一个假值都相等。针对一条解析不到的路径写的 filter 既不会失败，也不会返回空列表：它会选出假值元素，而且只要被比较的值是零，看起来就一直是对的。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:196
msgid "**Compare with `===`, or compare against something that resolves.** This is the most expensive mistake an adapter can make, and the platform's own workflows can make it too."
msgstr "**用 `===` 比较，或者与一个能解析到的值比较**。这是适配器可能犯的代价最大的错误，平台自己的工作流也会犯。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:199
msgid "`0`, `\"\"`, `null` and `[]` are false, and everything else is true, `{}` included. `all` and `some` over an empty list are `false`, and `none` is `true`. Test the turn with no foes and no food in sight, where all three meet an empty list."
msgstr "`0`、`\"\"`、`null` 和 `[]` 为假，其他一切为真，包括 `{}`。对空列表求 `all` 和 `some` 得到 `false`，`none` 得到 `true`。测试一下视野内既无敌人也无食物的回合，这三者在那里都会遇到空列表。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:203
msgid "What the language will not do"
msgstr "这门语言不做的事"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:205
msgid "The language has no tensor arithmetic beyond `cast` and `normalize`: no add, no multiply, no matrix multiply, no convolution. The platform left them out on purpose. The node prices a tensor operator by the elements it reads or produces, a fair price for moving data and the wrong one for computing with it: a 128 × 128 matrix multiply would cost about 32,769 operations for two million multiply-adds. An adapter that could compute would be a second, unpriced model in front of the priced one."
msgstr "除了 `cast` 和 `normalize`，这门语言没有张量算术：没有加法，没有乘法，没有矩阵乘法，没有卷积。平台是有意不提供的。节点按张量操作符读取或生成的元素数计价，这对搬运数据来说是公平的价格，对计算来说则不对：一次 128 × 128 的矩阵乘法只需约 32,769 次运算，却做了两百万次乘加。能做计算的适配器，就会成为排在计价模型前面的第二个不计价的模型。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:212
msgid "Arithmetic in the adapter would cost you time as well. The node interprets the adapter and runs the graph compiled, threaded and vectorised, and the two share one turn deadline. Put the arithmetic in the graph."
msgstr "在适配器里做算术还会花掉你的时间。节点以解释方式运行适配器，而计算图是编译过的、多线程且向量化的，两者共用一个回合时限。把算术放进计算图里。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:216
msgid "If you miss an operator, ask whether it moves or reshapes information, or computes with it. The language moves information, and the graph computes."
msgstr "如果你觉得少了某个操作符，先问问它是在搬运或重塑信息，还是在用信息做计算。这门语言负责搬运信息，计算图负责计算。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:219
msgid "Versions, and what moves under you"
msgstr "版本，以及会变动的东西"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:221
msgid "You declare no `dialect` field: the manifest's `abi` names the contract, and the node supplies the engine. The platform records **the Orion version** that admitted your entry, because that version names the expression engine and its counting rules."
msgstr "你不需要声明 `dialect` 字段：清单的 `abi` 指明了契约，引擎由节点提供。平台会记录你的参赛模型通过审核时的 **Orion 版本**，因为这个版本决定了表达式引擎及其计数规则。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:225
msgid "The engine's own documentation states that an operation count **can change between versions**: a new fast path or a constant fold changes what the engine dispatches. **Budget for the work, with headroom above the count you measured.** An adapter at 990,000 against a 1,000,000 ceiling is one patch release from a strike."
msgstr "引擎自己的文档写明，运算次数**可能随版本变化**：新的快速路径或常量折叠会改变引擎实际分派的内容。**按实际工作量做预算，在你测得的次数之上留出余量**。上限 1,000,000 而用到 990,000 的适配器，离一次判罚只差一个补丁版本。"

#: src/models/adapters/dialect.md:230
msgid "After a platform upgrade, a sweep re-checks admitted versions against the new engine. Re-run [local validation](../testing.md) after an announced upgrade; an older pass says nothing about the new engine."
msgstr "平台升级后，会有一次复查，用新引擎重新检查已通过审核的版本。公告升级之后，请重新运行[本地验证](../testing.md)；旧的通过结果说明不了新引擎的情况。"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:3
msgid "An adapter has twenty tensor operators on top of [the core ones](dialect.md#core-operators). You call each as `{\"name\": [arguments]}`. In the tables below, `T` is a tensor, a shape is a list of non-negative integers, and axes count from 0. [The budget](budget.md#what-each-operator-charges) lists what each one costs."
msgstr "在[核心操作符](dialect.md#core-operators)之上，适配器还有二十个张量操作符。每个都以 `{\"name\": [arguments]}` 的形式调用。下面的表格中，`T` 是张量，形状是非负整数列表，轴从 0 开始计数。[预算](budget.md#what-each-operator-charges)一页列出了每个操作符的开销。"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:8
msgid "**Seven of these names are ordinary words**: `shape`, `full`, `cast`, `pad`, `crop`, `concat` and `stack`. An object whose only key is one of them calls it. Put `$` before a data key that collides with one: `{\"$shape\": [6, 7]}` is the data `{\"shape\": [6, 7]}`, on the node and in `tinybrains`."
msgstr "**其中七个名称是普通单词**：`shape`、`full`、`cast`、`pad`、`crop`、`concat` 和 `stack`。唯一的键是其中之一的对象会调用它。与之同名的数据键前面加上 `$`：`{\"$shape\": [6, 7]}` 就是数据 `{\"shape\": [6, 7]}`，在节点上和在 `tinybrains` 中都是如此。"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:12
msgid "Building tensors"
msgstr "构建张量"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:14 src/models/adapters/operators.md:45 src/models/adapters/operators.md:65 src/models/adapters/operators.md:79 src/models/adapters/budget.md:32
msgid "Operator"
msgstr "操作符"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:14 src/models/adapters/operators.md:45 src/models/adapters/operators.md:65 src/models/adapters/operators.md:79
msgid "Arguments"
msgstr "参数"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:16
msgid "`zeros`"
msgstr "`zeros`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:16
msgid "`shape, dtype`"
msgstr "`shape, dtype`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:16
msgid "A tensor of zeros"
msgstr "全零张量"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:17
msgid "`full`"
msgstr "`full`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:17
msgid "`shape, dtype, value`"
msgstr "`shape, dtype, value`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:17
msgid "A tensor filled with `value`"
msgstr "用 `value` 填满的张量"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:18 src/models/adapters/budget.md:35
msgid "`tensor`"
msgstr "`tensor`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:18
msgid "`value, dtype?`"
msgstr "`value, dtype?`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:18
msgid "A nested JSON array as a tensor, in the shape the array has"
msgstr "把嵌套的 JSON 数组变成张量，形状与数组相同"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:19 src/models/adapters/budget.md:36
msgid "`scatter`"
msgstr "`scatter`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:19
msgid "`points, shape, dtype, value?`"
msgstr "`points, shape, dtype, value?`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:19
msgid "Zeros, with each point written: `[r, c]` writes `value` (default `1`), and `[r, c, v]` writes `v`"
msgstr "全零，再写入每个点：`[r, c]` 写入 `value`（默认 `1`），`[r, c, v]` 写入 `v`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:20 src/models/adapters/budget.md:37
msgid "`rle_expand`"
msgstr "`rle_expand`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:20
msgid "`runs, shape, dtype`"
msgstr "`runs, shape, dtype`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:20
msgid "`[v0, n0, v1, n1, …]` expanded in row-major order. Runs past the end fail; the operator pads runs short of it with zeros"
msgstr "`[v0, n0, v1, n1, …]` 按行优先顺序展开。游程超出末尾则失败；不足末尾的，操作符用零补齐"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:21 src/models/adapters/budget.md:38
msgid "`one_hot`"
msgstr "`one_hot`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:21
msgid "`indices, depth, dtype`"
msgstr "`indices, depth, dtype`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:21
msgid "`[len(indices), depth]`, with a `1` at each index. An index outside `0 … depth − 1` gives a row of zeros. It takes no axis argument"
msgstr "形状 `[len(indices), depth]`，在每个索引处放一个 `1`。索引超出 `0 … depth − 1` 的得到一行零。它不接受轴参数"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:23
msgid "`scatter` **drops a point outside the shape** and does not wrap it round the board, and a later point on the same cell overwrites an earlier one. Every write saturates the value to the dtype: `300` into `i8` gives `127`, where a wrapping cast would give `44`."
msgstr "`scatter` **会丢弃形状之外的点**，不会把它环绕到地图另一边；同一格上后面的点会覆盖前面的点。每次写入都把值饱和到数据类型的范围：把 `300` 写入 `i8` 得到 `127`，而回绕式转换会得到 `44`。"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:27
msgid "A point's third element is a value, so you strip foes and hills to `[r, c]` before they make a presence plane:"
msgstr "点的第三个元素是值，所以在用敌人和蚁丘构建存在平面之前，先把它们裁成 `[r, c]`："

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:38
msgid "The `map` inside it, run against an observation:"
msgstr "其中的 `map`，在一份观测上运行的结果："

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:43
msgid "Reshaping and combining"
msgstr "重塑与组合"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:47
msgid "`stack`"
msgstr "`stack`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:47 src/models/adapters/operators.md:48
msgid "`tensors, axis`"
msgstr "`tensors, axis`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:47
msgid "A new axis at `axis`. Every input must have the same shape and dtype"
msgstr "在 `axis` 处新增一个轴。所有输入的形状和数据类型必须相同"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:48
msgid "`concat`"
msgstr "`concat`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:48
msgid "Joined along an existing axis. Every other dimension must agree"
msgstr "沿已有的轴拼接。其他各维必须一致"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:49
msgid "`unstack`"
msgstr "`unstack`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:49 src/models/adapters/operators.md:81
msgid "`T, axis`"
msgstr "`T, axis`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:49
msgid "A JSON list of tensors, one for each index along `axis`"
msgstr "一个张量的 JSON 列表，`axis` 上每个索引对应一个"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:50
msgid "`reshape`"
msgstr "`reshape`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:50
msgid "`T, shape`"
msgstr "`T, shape`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:50
msgid "The same elements in a new shape. The element counts must match, and it takes no `-1`"
msgstr "同样的元素，换成新形状。元素数必须相等，且不接受 `-1`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:51
msgid "`transpose`"
msgstr "`transpose`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:51
msgid "`T, perm?`"
msgstr "`T, perm?`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:51
msgid "The axes reordered: `perm[i]` is the input axis that becomes axis `i`. Without `perm`, the axes are reversed"
msgstr "重排各轴：`perm[i]` 是将成为第 `i` 轴的输入轴。不给 `perm` 时，轴顺序反转"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:52
msgid "`pad`"
msgstr "`pad`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:52
msgid "`T, before, after, value`"
msgstr "`T, before, after, value`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:52
msgid "`before[d]` and `after[d]` cells added on each axis `d`, filled with `value` (default `0`)"
msgstr "在每个轴 `d` 上添加 `before[d]` 和 `after[d]` 个格子，以 `value` 填充（默认 `0`）"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:53
msgid "`crop`"
msgstr "`crop`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:53
msgid "`T, offset, shape`"
msgstr "`T, offset, shape`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:53
msgid "The `shape`\\-sized region that starts at `offset`. Any part of it past the input's edge is zeros"
msgstr "从 `offset` 开始、大小为 `shape` 的区域。超出输入边缘的部分为零"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:55
msgid "Stacking seven `[H, W]` planes on axis 0 gives `[7, H, W]`, and reshaping that to `[1, 7, H, W]` adds the batch axis a graph expects. [A real manifest](walkthrough.md#stacking-and-the-batch-axis) builds the second shape from the observation's size, so one adapter serves every board."
msgstr "把七个 `[H, W]` 平面在第 0 轴上堆叠得到 `[7, H, W]`，再重塑为 `[1, 7, H, W]` 就加上了计算图期望的批次轴。[一份真实的清单](walkthrough.md#stacking-and-the-batch-axis)根据观测的大小构建第二个形状，所以一个适配器适用于每张地图。"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:59
msgid "`stack` takes no dtype argument. Every plane must already be the dtype the input declares, so give each plane's own constructor that dtype. Mixed dtypes are an error, and `stack` never promotes one."
msgstr "`stack` 不接受数据类型参数。每个平面必须已经是输入所声明的数据类型，所以要给每个平面各自的构造操作符传入这个数据类型。数据类型混杂是错误，`stack` 从不做类型提升。"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:63
msgid "Converting and normalising"
msgstr "转换与归一化"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:67
msgid "`cast`"
msgstr "`cast`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:67
msgid "`T, dtype`"
msgstr "`T, dtype`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:67
msgid "Converted. Integer dtypes saturate and truncate toward zero"
msgstr "转换后的张量。整数类型会饱和，并向零截断"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:68
msgid "`normalize`"
msgstr "`normalize`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:68
msgid "`T, mean, scale?`"
msgstr "`T, mean, scale?`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:68
msgid "`(x − mean) × scale`, as `f32`. `scale` defaults to `1`"
msgstr "`(x − mean) × scale`，结果为 `f32`。`scale` 默认为 `1`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:70
msgid "These two are all the arithmetic the language has. It leaves out add, multiply and convolution on purpose ([why](dialect.md#what-the-language-will-not-do))."
msgstr "这两个就是这门语言全部的算术。它有意不提供加法、乘法和卷积（[为什么](dialect.md#what-the-language-will-not-do)）。"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:73
msgid "**There is no `dilate`.** Marking every cell within a squared radius of a non-zero cell, with wrapping, serves one plane, the visibility mask, and the observation carries [`vis`](../observation.md#what-you-can-see-this-turn) for it. That plane is one `rle_expand`."
msgstr "**没有 `dilate`**。把非零格周围距离平方范围内的每一格都标记出来（含环绕），只服务于一个平面，即视野掩码，而观测为此携带了 [`vis`](../observation.md#what-you-can-see-this-turn)。那个平面只需一次 `rle_expand`。"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:77
msgid "Reading tensors"
msgstr "读取张量"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:81 src/models/adapters/budget.md:42
msgid "`argmax`"
msgstr "`argmax`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:81
msgid "A flat JSON list: the winning index along `axis` for every position of the other axes, in row-major order. On a tie, the first wins"
msgstr "一个扁平的 JSON 列表：其他各轴每个位置上沿 `axis` 的最大值索引，按行优先顺序。并列时取第一个"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:82
msgid "`gather`"
msgstr "`gather`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:82
msgid "`T, indices, axis?`"
msgstr "`T, indices, axis?`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:82
msgid "A **tensor** of the slices at `indices` along `axis` (default `0`). An index past the end fails the call"
msgstr "沿 `axis`（默认 `0`）取 `indices` 处各切片组成的**张量**。索引超出末尾则调用失败"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:83
msgid "`to_list`"
msgstr "`to_list`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:83 src/models/adapters/operators.md:84 src/models/adapters/operators.md:85
msgid "`T`"
msgstr "`T`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:83
msgid "The tensor as nested JSON lists"
msgstr "张量，以嵌套 JSON 列表表示"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:84
msgid "`shape`"
msgstr "`shape`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:84
msgid "Its shape, as a list"
msgstr "它的形状，以列表表示"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:85
msgid "`dtype`"
msgstr "`dtype`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:85
msgid "Its dtype, as a string"
msgstr "它的数据类型，以字符串表示"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:87
msgid "**An adapter must end in a tensor**, so use these along the way and never as the last step. `shape` and `dtype` let a program branch on what it has. The node prices `to_list` per element like everything else, so converting a whole board costs the whole board."
msgstr "**适配器必须以张量结尾**，所以这些只能在中途使用，绝不能作为最后一步。`shape` 和 `dtype` 让程序能根据手上的东西分支。节点对 `to_list` 和其他操作符一样按元素计价，所以转换整张地图就要付整张地图的开销。"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:91
msgid "**The referee reads your head with `argmax` and `gather`**, and you write no head with them. An adapter may use them (one feeding a graph with two inputs might derive the second from a tensor it built), but a typical entry calls neither."
msgstr "**裁判用 `argmax` 和 `gather` 读取你的策略头**，你不需要用它们来写策略头。适配器可以使用它们（为双输入计算图供数的适配器，可能会从自己构建的张量推导出第二个输入），但典型的参赛模型两者都不会调用。"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:95
msgid "What is not here"
msgstr "这里没有的"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:97
msgid "`at`, `get`, `len` and `range` are not operators in this language. Use these instead:"
msgstr "`at`、`get`、`len` 和 `range` 不是这门语言的操作符。改用下面这些："

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:99
msgid "Instead of"
msgstr "原想用"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:99
msgid "Use"
msgstr "改用"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:101
msgid "`at(list, i)`"
msgstr "`at(list, i)`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:101
msgid "`{\"val\": [[N], …, {\"var\": \"\"}]}`: the engine evaluates a path segment, so a computed index is a path ([scope](dialect.md#a-path-segment-may-be-computed))"
msgstr "`{\"val\": [[N], …, {\"var\": \"\"}]}`：引擎会对路径段求值，所以计算出的索引就是路径（[作用域](dialect.md#a-path-segment-may-be-computed)）"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:102
msgid "`get(value, path)`"
msgstr "`get(value, path)`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:102
msgid "`{\"var\": \"accumulator.0\"}` for a reduce's accumulator; a one-element `reduce` to project out of any other computed value ([the pattern](dialect.md#reaching-outwards-and-the-one-place-you-cannot))"
msgstr "对 reduce 的累加器用 `{\"var\": \"accumulator.0\"}`；对其他任何计算出的值，用单元素 `reduce` 投影取出（[这种写法](dialect.md#reaching-outwards-and-the-one-place-you-cannot)）"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:103
msgid "`len(list)`"
msgstr "`len(list)`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:103
msgid "`{\"length\": […]}`, a core operator"
msgstr "`{\"length\": […]}`，核心操作符之一"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:104
msgid "`range(n)`"
msgstr "`range(n)`"

#: src/models/adapters/operators.md:104
msgid "No equivalent. Build the list you need, or let `scatter` and `rle_expand` do the looping"
msgstr "没有对应物。自己构建需要的列表，或者让 `scatter` 和 `rle_expand` 来做循环"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:3
msgid "Ants allows **1,000,000 operations per adapter evaluation**. Each declared input's adapter gets its own million, so a manifest with two inputs gets two: the ceiling applies to each evaluation, and one call evaluates every input's adapter. The count leaves out inference, and the whole call (your adapters and the graph) has to fit the turn deadline."
msgstr "Ants 允许**每次适配器求值 1,000,000 次运算**。每个已声明输入的适配器各有自己的一百万，所以有两个输入的清单就有两份：上限按每次求值计，而一次调用会对每个输入的适配器求值。这个计数不含推理，而整个调用（你的适配器加上计算图）必须在回合时限内完成。"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:8
msgid "What counts as an operation"
msgstr "什么算一次运算"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:10
msgid "**Every node the evaluator visits costs 1**: an operator, a literal, each element of an array written in the program. A loop body pays again for every element it runs over, and a branch the evaluator skips pays nothing."
msgstr "**求值器访问的每一个表达式节点计 1**：一个操作符、一个字面量、程序中写出的数组的每个元素。循环体对它遍历的每个元素都再付一次，求值器跳过的分支不付费。"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:13
msgid "**A constant-folded subtree costs nothing**, and the evaluator charges once for a subtree it recognises twice. Both are optimisations, and both can change between versions."
msgstr "**被常量折叠的子树不计费**，求值器识别出同一子树出现了两次时也只计一次。两者都是优化，也都可能随版本变化。"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:15
msgid "**Every tensor operator also charges for the elements it moves**, by its own rule below. The node charges **before** the work, so it refuses an operator that would exceed the budget and never runs it."
msgstr "**每个张量操作符还要为它搬运的元素计费**，各自的规则见下文。节点在执行**之前**计费，所以会超出预算的操作符会被拒绝，根本不会运行。"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:18
msgid "**The collection and string operators charge for their items**: `merge`, `in`, `keys`, `values`, `entries`, `sort`, `distinct`, `group_by`, `cat`, `split` and deep equality charge one per item, or per 64 bytes of string. So an accumulator built with `merge` inside a `reduce` pays for every item it copies, on every step, and grows quadratically."
msgstr "**集合和字符串操作符按项计费**：`merge`、`in`、`keys`、`values`、`entries`、`sort`、`distinct`、`group_by`、`cat`、`split` 和深度相等比较，每项计一次，字符串则每 64 字节计一次。所以在 `reduce` 里用 `merge` 构建的累加器，每一步都要为它复制的每一项付费，开销按平方增长。"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:23
msgid "`{\"zeros\": [[128, 128], \"i8\"]}` costs about 16,389: 1 for the operator, 16,384 for the elements it produces, and a handful for evaluating its arguments (the shape array, its two numbers, and the dtype)."
msgstr "`{\"zeros\": [[128, 128], \"i8\"]}` 的开销约为 16,389：操作符本身 1，它生成的元素 16,384，再加上对参数求值的几次（形状数组、其中的两个数字，以及数据类型）。"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:27
msgid "What each operator charges"
msgstr "各操作符的计费"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:29
msgid "Each operator charges the amount below on top of its own 1 and the cost of evaluating its arguments. `n` is the number of elements in the tensor argument, and `m` the number in the result."
msgstr "每个操作符在自身的 1 和对参数求值的开销之外，再收取下面的费用。`n` 是张量参数的元素数，`m` 是结果的元素数。"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:32
msgid "Charge"
msgstr "计费"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:34
msgid "`zeros`, `full`"
msgstr "`zeros`, `full`"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:34 src/models/adapters/budget.md:35
msgid "`m`"
msgstr "`m`"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:36
msgid "the larger of the number of points and `m`. **A scatter pays for the whole grid**, however few points it writes"
msgstr "点数和 `m` 中的较大者。**一次 scatter 要为整个网格付费**，无论它写入的点多么少"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:37
msgid "the larger of `len(runs)` and `m`"
msgstr "`len(runs)` 和 `m` 中的较大者"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:38
msgid "`len(indices) × depth`"
msgstr "`len(indices) × depth`"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:39
msgid "`stack`, `concat`"
msgstr "`stack`, `concat`"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:39
msgid "the elements of all the inputs"
msgstr "所有输入的元素总数"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:40
msgid "`unstack`, `transpose`, `cast`, `normalize`, `to_list`"
msgstr "`unstack`, `transpose`, `cast`, `normalize`, `to_list`"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:40
msgid "`n`"
msgstr "`n`"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:41
msgid "`pad`, `crop`, `gather`"
msgstr "`pad`, `crop`, `gather`"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:41
msgid "the larger of `n` and `m`"
msgstr "`n` 和 `m` 中的较大者"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:42
msgid "`n`: it reads everything"
msgstr "`n`：它要读取全部元素"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:43
msgid "`reshape`, `shape`, `dtype`"
msgstr "`reshape`, `shape`, `dtype`"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:43
msgid "1: a reshape moves no elements"
msgstr "1：重塑不搬运任何元素"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:45
msgid "**The platform does not promise these numbers.** The engine's own documentation says an operation count can change between versions: a new fast path or a constant fold changes what the engine dispatches. Budget for the work, with headroom above the number you measured. An adapter at 990,000 against a 1,000,000 ceiling is one patch release away from a strike."
msgstr "**平台不保证这些数字**。引擎自己的文档写明，运算次数可能随版本变化：新的快速路径或常量折叠会改变引擎实际分派的内容。按实际工作量做预算，在你测得的数字之上留出余量。上限 1,000,000 而用到 990,000 的适配器，离一次判罚只差一个补丁版本。"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:50
msgid "What a real manifest costs"
msgstr "真实清单的开销"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:52
msgid "The baselines' adapter builds seven planes, and [A real manifest, piece by piece](walkthrough.md) reads it in full. `tinybrains adapt` measured it over the reference observations on 1 October 2026, across the five basic boards the set is drawn on. The worst case on the smallest, one in the middle and the largest:"
msgstr "基线的适配器构建七个平面，[逐段解读一份真实清单](walkthrough.md)完整讲解了它。2026 年 10 月 1 日，`tinybrains adapt` 在参考观测上测量了它，覆盖该参考集所取自的五张基础地图。最小、中等和最大地图上的最差情况："

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:59
msgid "8,131"
msgstr "8,131"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:60
msgid "43,113"
msgstr "43,113"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:61
msgid "208,427"
msgstr "208,427"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:63
msgid "**The cost follows the board's cells**: about 14 operations per cell, because each of the seven planes is a full grid and the stack reads all seven again. The ants, foes, food and hills add a few operations each, lost in the rounding. A season's boards can run from 24 × 24 (576 cells) to 14,880 cells, and the largest costs a fifth of the budget."
msgstr "**开销随地图的格数变化**：每格约 14 次运算，因为七个平面每个都是完整的网格，而 stack 又把七个全读了一遍。蚂蚁、敌人、食物和蚁丘各加几次运算，在取整里就被忽略了。赛季的地图可以从 24 × 24（576 格）到 14,880 格不等，最大的那张花掉预算的五分之一。"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:68
msgid "What over budget means"
msgstr "超出预算意味着什么"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:70
msgid "The node stops evaluation the moment a charge crosses the budget. At admission that is a rejection, `ADAPTER_OVER_BUDGET`; in a match it is a strike, like a missed deadline, and five cumulative strikes forfeit the seat. The node never retries: the same adapter on the same observation costs the same on any machine."
msgstr "计费一越过预算，节点就立刻停止求值。在审核时这是拒绝，原因为 `ADAPTER_OVER_BUDGET`；在对局中这是一次判罚，和错过时限一样，累计五次判罚该席位就判负。节点从不重试：同一个适配器在同一份观测上，在任何机器上的开销都相同。"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:75
msgid "Passing admission does not prove every later turn fits. The node counts on real input, and a late-game turn (more ants, more food and foes in sight) can cost more than any reference case. An adapter whose cost follows the board, as the baselines' does, stays predictable; one whose loops run over ants or visible objects grows with the game."
msgstr "通过审核并不能证明之后的每个回合都在预算内。节点是在真实输入上计数的，残局的回合（更多蚂蚁，视野内更多食物和敌人）可能比任何参考用例都贵。开销随地图变化的适配器（基线的就是这样）保持可预测；循环遍历蚂蚁或可见物体的适配器，开销会随对局推进而增长。"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:80
msgid "Measuring before you submit"
msgstr "提交前测量"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:82
msgid "`tinybrains adapt model.onnx manifest.json` prints what every reference case charged, and `--obs` measures observations of your own. `tinybrains check` reports the worst case and the fraction of the budget it used. [Testing before you submit](../testing.md) has both."
msgstr "`tinybrains adapt model.onnx manifest.json` 打印每个参考用例的计费，`--obs` 则测量你自己的观测。`tinybrains check` 报告最差情况及其占预算的比例。[提交前的测试](../testing.md)两者都有讲。"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:86
msgid "Spending less"
msgstr "节省开销"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:88
msgid "Build planes with `scatter` and `rle_expand`, never with a JSON loop over cells."
msgstr "用 `scatter` 和 `rle_expand` 构建平面，绝不要用 JSON 循环逐格构建。"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:89
msgid "**Each plane costs about two operations per cell**: one to build it and one for the stack to read it. Dropping a plane your graph does not use is the cheapest saving there is."
msgstr "**每个平面每格约两次运算**：构建它一次，stack 读取它一次。去掉计算图用不到的平面，是成本最低的节省办法。"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:91
msgid "Read `vis`: it is one `rle_expand`, and the language cannot express deriving it ([why](dialect.md#reaching-outwards-and-the-one-place-you-cannot))."
msgstr "读取 `vis`：它只需一次 `rle_expand`，而且这门语言无法表达它的推导过程（[为什么](dialect.md#reaching-outwards-and-the-one-place-you-cannot)）。"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:93
msgid "Prefer one input over several. Each is its own evaluation with its own million, and each re-reads the observation."
msgstr "尽量用一个输入而不是多个。每个输入都是一次独立的求值，有自己的一百万，也都要重新读一遍观测。"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:95
msgid "The head costs you nothing, because the referee reads it. A program of your own that read it back would pay for all five channels of every cell: ~82,000 operations at 128 × 128."
msgstr "策略头不花你任何开销，因为是裁判来读它。如果你自己写程序把它读回来，就要为每一格的全部五个通道付费：在 128 × 128 上约 82,000 次运算。"

#: src/models/adapters/budget.md:98
msgid "Test across [the limits](../../games/ants/maps.md#the-limits-every-board-is-inside): a 120 × 124 board has about 26 times the cells of a 24 × 24 one, and an adapter whose cost follows the board costs that much more on it."
msgstr "在[限制](../../games/ants/maps.md#the-limits-every-board-is-inside)的整个范围内测试：120 × 124 的地图格数约是 24 × 24 的 26 倍，开销随地图变化的适配器在它上面的开销也就是那么多倍。"

#: src/models/memory.md:3
msgid "A model can remember. When your season's [weight class](weight-classes.md) allows it, your graph writes a tensor on one turn and your adapter reads it back on the next, for the rest of the match. **The runner carries the memory in the open**: it is an output your manifest declares, handed back on your seat's next view under the output's own name. No node keeps it and none hides it, and a model that declares no memory plays as it did before this page existed."
msgstr "模型可以拥有记忆。只要你所在赛季的[重量级](weight-classes.md)允许，你的计算图就能在某一回合写出一个张量，由你的适配器在下一回合读回，并一直延续到对局结束，而**运行器公开地携带这份记忆**：它是你清单中声明的一个输出，会以该输出自己的名字，在你席位的下一次视图中交还给你。没有哪个节点保存它，也没有哪个节点隐藏它；而不声明记忆的模型，玩法和这一页出现之前完全一样。"

#: src/models/memory.md:9
msgid "Two memories"
msgstr "两种记忆"

#: src/models/memory.md:11
msgid "A manifest may declare an output named `memory`, one named `ant_memory`, both or neither, beside its `policy`:"
msgstr "清单可以在 `policy` 之外，再声明一个名为 `memory` 的输出、一个名为 `ant_memory` 的输出，两者都声明，或者都不声明："

#: src/models/memory.md:14
msgid "Output"
msgstr "输出"

#: src/models/memory.md:14
msgid "What it is for"
msgstr "用途"

#: src/models/memory.md:16
msgid "`memory`"
msgstr "`memory`"

#: src/models/memory.md:16
msgid "fixed, or `[1, K, \"H\", \"W\"]`"
msgstr "固定形状，或 `[1, K, \"H\", \"W\"]`"

#: src/models/memory.md:16
msgid "The board: scent, where food was seen, where foes were, what has been explored"
msgstr "地图层面：气味、见过食物的位置、敌人出现过的位置、已探索的区域"

#: src/models/memory.md:17
msgid "`ant_memory`"
msgstr "`ant_memory`"

#: src/models/memory.md:17
msgid "`[1, \"N\", K]`"
msgstr "`[1, \"N\", K]`"

#: src/models/memory.md:17
msgid "One row per ant, in this turn's `mine` order: a target, a role, how long it has chased one"
msgstr "每只蚂蚁一行，按本回合 `mine` 的顺序：目标、角色、追逐目标已有多少回合"

#: src/models/memory.md:19
msgid "`ant_memory` needs to know which ant is which, and the observation says so in [`ids`](observation.md#ant-ids). `memory` needs nothing but the board."
msgstr "`ant_memory` 需要分清每只蚂蚁是谁，观测中的 [`ids`](observation.md#ant-ids) 正是为此；`memory` 只需要地图本身。"

#: src/models/memory.md:25 src/models/memory.md:60 src/models/memory.md:61
msgid "\"memory\""
msgstr "\"memory\""

#: src/models/memory.md:29
msgid "One turn, two steps"
msgstr "一个回合，两个步骤"

#: src/models/memory.md:31
msgid "Each turn the memory passes through two steps, in this order:"
msgstr "每个回合，记忆都会依次经过两个步骤："

#: src/models/memory.md:33
msgid "**The adapter, before the model.** It reads last turn's memory and this turn's observation, updates what it can, and hands the model its inputs: the memory as updated, and the board."
msgstr "**先是适配器，在模型之前**。它读取上一回合的记忆和本回合的观测，更新它能更新的部分，再把输入交给模型：更新后的记忆，以及地图。"

#: src/models/memory.md:35
msgid "**The model, after.** It computes its moves, and its `memory` output is the memory for the next turn. Where it changes nothing, that output is its input again, through `Identity`, which costs nothing."
msgstr "**然后是模型**。它算出走法，其 `memory` 输出就是下一回合的记忆。在不需要改动的地方，这个输出就是通过 `Identity` 原样送回的输入，不花任何开销。"

#: src/models/memory.md:39
msgid "**The memory carried to the next turn is whatever the model outputs.** An update the adapter makes reaches it only through a model input, so a graph that should keep the adapter's work echoes that input back with `Identity`."
msgstr "**带到下一回合的记忆，就是模型输出的内容**。适配器所做的更新只能通过模型输入才能到达那里，所以想保留适配器成果的计算图，要用 `Identity` 把那个输入原样送回。"

#: src/models/memory.md:43
msgid "The adapter language has no arithmetic between tensors ([why](adapters/dialect.md#what-the-language-will-not-do)), so the two steps are good at different things. The adapter selects, re-keys and looks things up, and the graph computes:"
msgstr "适配器语言没有张量之间的算术运算（[原因](adapters/dialect.md#what-the-language-will-not-do)），所以这两个步骤各有所长。适配器负责选取、按 id 重新对齐和查表，计算图负责计算："

#: src/models/memory.md:47
msgid "Scent (`memory`)"
msgstr "气味（`memory`）"

#: src/models/memory.md:47
msgid "A target per ant (`ant_memory`)"
msgstr "每只蚂蚁一个目标（`ant_memory`）"

#: src/models/memory.md:49 src/reference/glossary.md:7
msgid "Adapter"
msgstr "适配器"

#: src/models/memory.md:49
msgid "Passes the scent through, and builds this turn's deposit plane from `mine` with `scatter`"
msgstr "把气味原样传递，并用 `scatter` 从 `mine` 构建本回合的沉积平面"

#: src/models/memory.md:49
msgid "Re-keys last turn's rows to this turn's ants by id, and looks up the food at each stored target"
msgstr "按 id 把上一回合的行重新对齐到本回合的蚂蚁，并查出每个已存目标处的食物"

#: src/models/memory.md:50 src/reference/glossary.md:31
msgid "Model"
msgstr "模型"

#: src/models/memory.md:50
msgid "`Max(scent × 0.95, deposit)`: decay, then deposit"
msgstr "`Max(scent × 0.95, deposit)`：先衰减，再沉积"

#: src/models/memory.md:50
msgid "Drops targets that are reached, gone or stale, picks new ones, moves, and outputs a row for every ant"
msgstr "丢弃已到达、已消失或已过期的目标，挑选新目标，移动，并为每只蚂蚁输出一行"

#: src/models/memory.md:52
msgid "Reading the memory in an adapter"
msgstr "在适配器中读取记忆"

#: src/models/memory.md:54
msgid "On turn 0 the view has no `memory`, so the adapter builds its own zeros. After that it reads the key like any other field:"
msgstr "第 0 回合的视图里没有 `memory`，所以适配器要自己构建零张量。此后它像读取其他字段一样读取这个键："

#: src/models/memory.md:58
msgid "\"scent_in\""
msgstr "\"scent_in\""

#: src/models/memory.md:59
msgid "\"if\""
msgstr "\"if\""

#: src/models/memory.md:61
msgid "\"tensor\""
msgstr "\"tensor\""

#: src/models/memory.md:62
msgid "\"zeros\""
msgstr "\"zeros\""

#: src/models/memory.md:65
msgid "**Read it with `{\"tensor\": [{\"var\": \"memory\"}]}`.** On a node and in `tinybrains` alike, the key holds the tensor your graph wrote, and `tensor` passes it through with the dtype and shape your output declared. A tensor is opaque: an adapter can read its shape and dtype, never its fields, so a program that looks inside the value finds nothing on either. The one place memory is JSON is an observation file you give `tinybrains adapt`, which decodes it into a tensor as it loads."
msgstr "**用 `{\"tensor\": [{\"var\": \"memory\"}]}` 读取它**。无论在节点上还是在 `tinybrains` 里，这个键保存的都是你的计算图写出的张量，`tensor` 会按你输出声明的数据类型和形状把它原样传递。张量是不透明的：适配器能读到它的形状和数据类型，却读不到里面的元素，所以试图查看其内部值的程序在两边都一无所获。记忆唯一以 JSON 形式出现的地方，是你交给 `tinybrains adapt` 的观测文件，它在加载时会把记忆解码成张量。"

#: src/models/memory.md:71
msgid "From there the rest of the adapter language applies. `crop` and `concat` shift a history along, `gather` and `to_list` read a stored value back into JSON for a comparison, and `scatter` writes this turn's facts onto a plane of the board's size."
msgstr "从这里开始，适配器语言的其余部分照常适用。`crop` 和 `concat` 可以推移一段历史，`gather` 和 `to_list` 能把存下的值读回 JSON 用于比较，`scatter` 则把本回合的事实写到一个地图大小的平面上。"

#: src/models/memory.md:75
msgid "Scent on the board"
msgstr "地图上的气味"

#: src/models/memory.md:77
msgid "A scent trail is a board memory. The adapter passes last turn's scent through, as above, and builds a deposit plane from `mine` as a second input:"
msgstr "气味轨迹是一种地图记忆。适配器像上面那样把上一回合的气味原样传递，再从 `mine` 构建一个沉积平面作为第二个输入："

#: src/models/memory.md:81
msgid "\"deposit\""
msgstr "\"deposit\""

#: src/models/memory.md:87
msgid "The graph decays the old scent and lays the new one over it, and outputs the result as `memory`:"
msgstr "计算图让旧气味衰减，再把新气味叠加上去，并把结果作为 `memory` 输出："

#: src/models/memory.md:93
msgid "It needs no ids: a cell is a cell on every turn. The same pattern keeps food seen, foe hills seen or explored land, with `Max` to remember and a decayed copy to forget."
msgstr "这不需要 id：每个回合里，格子还是那个格子。同样的模式也能记住见过的食物、见过的敌方蚁丘或已探索的陆地：用 `Max` 来记住，用衰减后的副本来遗忘。"

#: src/models/memory.md:96
msgid "A memory per ant"
msgstr "每只蚂蚁一份记忆"

#: src/models/memory.md:98
msgid "`ant_memory` keeps one row per ant, and **the rows follow the ants by id**, never by position: `mine` is sorted afresh every turn, so the third row this turn is usually a different ant from the third row last turn."
msgstr "`ant_memory` 为每只蚂蚁保留一行，而且**各行按 id 跟随蚂蚁**，从不按位置：`mine` 每回合都会重新排序，所以本回合的第三行通常和上一回合的第三行不是同一只蚂蚁。"

#: src/models/memory.md:102
msgid "The adapter hands the model this turn's `ids` as an input, and the model writes each ant's id into column 0 of its row. On the next turn the adapter turns last turn's rows into a table indexed by id, then reads that table back in this turn's `ids` order:"
msgstr "适配器把本回合的 `ids` 作为一个输入交给模型，模型把每只蚂蚁的 id 写进它那一行的第 0 列。到了下一回合，适配器把上一回合的各行变成一张按 id 索引的表，再按本回合 `ids` 的顺序把这张表读回来："

#: src/models/memory.md:113
msgid "Every step is an operator the adapter language already has: `to_list`, `map`, `scatter`, `concat`, `gather` and `reshape`. The `map` body reads only its own row, so the [scope rule](adapters/dialect.md) never bites. Say last turn's ants were 7, 3 and 12, and this turn's are 3, 12 and 20: ant 7 has died and ant 20 is new. The rows come back as 3's row, then 12's, then zeros."
msgstr "每一步都是适配器语言已有的操作符：`to_list`、`map`、`scatter`、`concat`、`gather` 和 `reshape`。`map` 的主体只读取自己那一行，所以[作用域规则](adapters/dialect.md)不会造成麻烦。假设上一回合的蚂蚁是 7、3 和 12，本回合是 3、12 和 20：蚂蚁 7 已经死亡，蚂蚁 20 是新出生的。读回的各行依次是 3 的那一行、12 的那一行，然后是全零。"

#: src/models/memory.md:119
msgid "Keying by id makes three cases work with no code of their own:"
msgstr "按 id 作键，让三种情况无需额外代码就能正常工作："

#: src/models/memory.md:121
msgid "**A struck turn.** The memory stays at the last one written ([below](#the-carry)), and ids do not change, so the rows still find their ants."
msgstr "**被判罚的回合**。记忆停留在最后一次写入的值（[见下文](#the-carry)），而 id 不会变，所以各行仍能找到自己的蚂蚁。"

#: src/models/memory.md:123
msgid "**A dead ant's row** is never read back, and drops out of the next output."
msgstr "**死亡蚂蚁的那一行**不会再被读回，并从下一次输出中消失。"

#: src/models/memory.md:124
msgid "**A new ant** reads a row of zeros, and the model gives it whatever a new ant gets."
msgstr "**新出生的蚂蚁**读到的是全零的一行，模型按新蚂蚁的待遇处理它。"

#: src/models/memory.md:126
msgid "On turn 0 there is no `ant_memory`, and the adapter builds zeros of `[1, N, K]` directly."
msgstr "第 0 回合没有 `ant_memory`，适配器直接构建 `[1, N, K]` 的零张量。"

#: src/models/memory.md:128
msgid "**`S`, the table's height, is yours to choose.** `gather` fails the call on an id at or past `S`, and a seat spawns at most one ant per hill per turn, so `S` above hills per seat × (turns + 1) is never reached. A smaller `S` can take `id % S` on both sides and accept that two living ants may share a row. The join's cost grows with `S` and with the number of ants; at `S` = 4,096 it is under 5% of an adapter's [budget](adapters/budget.md). Measure yours with [`tinybrains adapt`](testing.md#see-the-tensors-your-adapter-builds)."
msgstr "**表的高度 `S` 由你决定**。遇到大于等于 `S` 的 id，`gather` 会让这次调用失败；而一个席位每回合每个蚁丘最多出生一只蚂蚁，所以只要 `S` 超过每席位蚁丘数 × (回合数 + 1)，就永远不会触及。较小的 `S` 可以在两边都取 `id % S`，并接受两只活着的蚂蚁可能共用一行。这次连接的开销随 `S` 和蚂蚁数量增长；在 `S` = 4,096 时，它不到适配器[预算](adapters/budget.md)的 5%。用 [`tinybrains adapt`](testing.md#see-the-tensors-your-adapter-builds) 测量你自己的开销。"

#: src/models/memory.md:135
msgid "A target held until it is reached or no longer valid"
msgstr "保持目标直到到达或失效"

#: src/models/memory.md:137
msgid "Store each ant's target as an absolute cell, with `ant_memory` columns `[id, has_target, tr, tc, turns]`."
msgstr "把每只蚂蚁的目标存成一个绝对坐标的格子，`ant_memory` 的各列为 `[id, has_target, tr, tc, turns]`。"

#: src/models/memory.md:140
msgid "**The adapter, before the model:**"
msgstr "**先是适配器，在模型之前：**"

#: src/models/memory.md:142
msgid "Re-key last turn's rows to this turn's ants by id, as above."
msgstr "像上面那样，按 id 把上一回合的行重新对齐到本回合的蚂蚁。"

#: src/models/memory.md:143
msgid "Look up what the model needs at each stored target. For food, flatten the food plane and gather it at `tr × W + tc` for each row, as a second input of shape `[1, N]`. The target is an absolute cell, so this is one `map` over the rows."
msgstr "在每个已存目标处查出模型需要的信息。以食物为例，把食物平面展平，对每一行在 `tr × W + tc` 处取出它的值，作为形状为 `[1, N]` 的第二个输入。目标是绝对坐标的格子，所以这只是对各行的一次 `map`。"

#: src/models/memory.md:147
msgid "**The model, after:**"
msgstr "**然后是模型：**"

#: src/models/memory.md:149
msgid "Keep an ant's target unless it has been reached, the food at it is gone, or the ant has chased it for too many turns. That is a `Where` in the graph."
msgstr "保留蚂蚁的目标，除非已经到达、那里的食物已经消失，或者蚂蚁追逐它的回合数太多。这在计算图里就是一个 `Where`。"

#: src/models/memory.md:151
msgid "Where no target is kept, let the policy head pick a new one."
msgstr "没有保留目标的地方，让策略头挑一个新的。"

#: src/models/memory.md:152
msgid "Move toward the target, and output `ant_memory` with a row for every ant."
msgstr "朝目标移动，并输出 `ant_memory`，每只蚂蚁一行。"

#: src/models/memory.md:154
msgid "A blocked move needs no prediction. The engine resolves every move, and next turn the ant's id says where it ended up."
msgstr "被阻挡的移动不需要预测。引擎会结算每一次移动，下一回合蚂蚁的 id 就会告诉你它到了哪里。"

#: src/models/memory.md:157
msgid "The carry"
msgstr "记忆的携带"

#: src/models/memory.md:159
msgid "The runner keeps, for each seat of each match, the last value of each memory output, and hands it back under the same key:"
msgstr "运行器为每场对局的每个席位保存每个记忆输出的最新值，并以同一个键交还："

#: src/models/memory.md:162 src/models/memory.md:221
msgid "When"
msgstr "时机"

#: src/models/memory.md:162
msgid "The view's `memory` (and `ant_memory`)"
msgstr "视图中的 `memory`（以及 `ant_memory`）"

#: src/models/memory.md:164
msgid "Turn 0"
msgstr "第 0 回合"

#: src/models/memory.md:164
msgid "Absent. The adapter builds its own zeros"
msgstr "不存在。适配器自己构建零张量"

#: src/models/memory.md:165
msgid "After a call that answered"
msgstr "一次有应答的调用之后"

#: src/models/memory.md:165
msgid "That call's output of the same name"
msgstr "那次调用的同名输出"

#: src/models/memory.md:166
msgid "After a call that failed or timed out"
msgstr "一次失败或超时的调用之后"

#: src/models/memory.md:166
msgid "Unchanged: the last memory the model wrote"
msgstr "不变：模型最后一次写入的记忆"

#: src/models/memory.md:167
msgid "A new match"
msgstr "新的对局"

#: src/models/memory.md:167
msgid "Absent again"
msgstr "再次不存在"

#: src/models/memory.md:169
msgid "**Seats never share a memory**, even two seats of one model in one match. The referee reads `policy` alone, and the rules never read a memory, so a replay carries none: re-simulating a match needs only its actions."
msgstr "**席位之间从不共享记忆**，即使同一场对局里的两个席位是同一个模型。裁判只读取 `policy`，游戏规则从不读取记忆，所以回放里没有记忆：重新模拟一场对局只需要它的动作。"

#: src/models/memory.md:173
msgid "A strike leaves the memory as it was, so a model that fails a call keeps its notes and picks up where it left off. A model whose memory input cannot take its own output fails every turn after the first; admission's round trip ([below](#what-admission-checks)) is there to catch that before a match does."
msgstr "判罚不会改动记忆，所以一次调用失败的模型仍保有自己的笔记，可以从上次停下的地方继续。而记忆输入无法接受自己输出的模型，从第二回合起每回合都会失败；审核的往返检查（[见下文](#what-admission-checks)）正是为了在对局暴露它之前先抓住它。"

#: src/models/memory.md:178
msgid "The cap"
msgstr "上限"

#: src/models/memory.md:180
msgid "A class allows memory with two numbers, both set by the season: `memory_flat_bytes` and `memory_cell_bytes`. On a board of `rows × cols` cells, your two memories together may take"
msgstr "重量级用两个数字来允许记忆，都由赛季设定：`memory_flat_bytes` 和 `memory_cell_bytes`。在一张有 `rows × cols` 个格子的地图上，你的两种记忆合计最多可占"

#: src/models/memory.md:187
msgid "Both default to 0, which is no memory. [Weight classes](weight-classes.md#memory) says where to read a season's numbers."
msgstr "两者默认都是 0，即没有记忆。[重量级](weight-classes.md#memory)一页说明了在哪里查看赛季的数字。"

#: src/models/memory.md:190
msgid "**Your memory's price follows its declared shape.** Each output costs its elements times its dtype's width: 1 byte for `i8`, `u8` and `bool`, 2 for `i16` and `u16`, 4 for `f32`, `i32` and `u32`, and 8 for `f64`, `i64` and `u64`. An output with no named dimension is a fixed cost. An output with any named dimension is priced **per cell**: the product of its numbers, times the board's cells. That covers `ant_memory`'s ant axis too, because a seat can never have more ants than the board has cells."
msgstr "**记忆的价格取决于它声明的形状**。每个输出的开销是元素个数乘以数据类型的宽度：`i8`、`u8` 和 `bool` 为 1 字节，`i16` 和 `u16` 为 2 字节，`f32`、`i32` 和 `u32` 为 4 字节，`f64`、`i64` 和 `u64` 为 8 字节。没有命名维度的输出是固定开销。带有任何命名维度的输出按**每格**计价：其数字维度的乘积，乘以地图的格子数。这也涵盖了 `ant_memory` 的蚂蚁维度，因为一个席位的蚂蚁数永远不会超过地图的格子数。"

#: src/models/memory.md:197
msgid "`memory` may name at most two dimensions, and `ant_memory` at most one."
msgstr "`memory` 最多可有两个命名维度，`ant_memory` 最多一个。"

#: src/models/memory.md:198
msgid "A shape may not use a name twice."
msgstr "一个形状不能重复使用同一个名字。"

#: src/models/memory.md:200
msgid "Admission prices the two outputs together at the smallest board a season can play, 576 cells (24 × 24), and the largest, 14,880 cells. Both sides grow in a straight line with the cell count, so a model that fits at both ends fits on every board between, including one the season adds later. Nothing checks the cap again at play."
msgstr "审核会把两个输出合计，分别在赛季可用的最小地图（576 格，24 × 24）和最大地图（14,880 格）上计价。两边都随格子数线性增长，所以在两端都放得下的模型，在之间的每一张地图上也放得下，包括赛季之后新增的地图。对局时不会再检查上限。"

#: src/models/memory.md:205
msgid "A worked example: `memory` as `f32[1, 2, \"H\", \"W\"]` is 8 bytes a cell, and `ant_memory` as `i8[1, \"N\", 5]` is 5 more. At 14,880 cells that is 193,440 bytes, so the class needs a `memory_cell_bytes` of 13 or more, or a flat allowance that covers the difference at both ends. Store what you can as `u8` or `i8` and `Cast` inside the graph: a byte a value is a quarter of the price of `f32`."
msgstr "举个例子：`memory` 声明为 `f32[1, 2, \"H\", \"W\"]` 是每格 8 字节，`ant_memory` 声明为 `i8[1, \"N\", 5]` 再加 5 字节。在 14,880 格时合计 193,440 字节，所以重量级的 `memory_cell_bytes` 需要达到 13 或更高，或者有一个在两端都能补足差额的固定配额。能存成 `u8` 或 `i8` 的就这么存，并在计算图内 `Cast`：每个值一字节，价格只有 `f32` 的四分之一。"

#: src/models/memory.md:211
msgid "**Memory counts nothing toward your size.** Your class is still decided by the two files' bytes ([`S'`](format.md#how-size-is-measured)). A competitor who wants more memory enters a larger class. A memory starts at zero every match, so it cannot smuggle weights in."
msgstr "**记忆完全不计入你的大小**。你的重量级仍由两个文件的字节数决定（[`S'`](format.md#how-size-is-measured)）。想要更多记忆的参赛者，就进入更大的重量级。记忆在每场对局开始时都是零，所以无法借它偷带权重。"

#: src/models/memory.md:215
msgid "What admission checks"
msgstr "审核检查什么"

#: src/models/memory.md:217
msgid "Admission decides three of these from your manifest and your class, with no model run, and the fourth by running your model on its own memory. Each is final and names something only you can change:"
msgstr "其中三项审核仅凭你的清单和重量级判定，不运行模型；第四项则通过让你的模型吃回自己的记忆来判定。每一项都是最终结论，所指出的问题也只有你能改变："

#: src/models/memory.md:221 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:44 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:55 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:72 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:91 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:100
msgid "Reason"
msgstr "原因"

#: src/models/memory.md:221 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:11 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:44 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:55 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:72 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:91 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:100 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:145
msgid "Next step"
msgstr "下一步"

#: src/models/memory.md:223 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:93
msgid "`MEMORY_NOT_ALLOWED`"
msgstr "`MEMORY_NOT_ALLOWED`"

#: src/models/memory.md:223
msgid "You declare a memory output, and your class allows 0 and 0"
msgstr "你声明了记忆输出，而你的重量级允许的是 0 和 0"

#: src/models/memory.md:223
msgid "Remove the output, or enter a class this season gives memory"
msgstr "删掉这个输出，或进入本赛季允许记忆的重量级"

#: src/models/memory.md:224 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:94
msgid "`MEMORY_TOO_LARGE`"
msgstr "`MEMORY_TOO_LARGE`"

#: src/models/memory.md:224
msgid "The memory's price is past the class's cap at 576 or at 14,880 cells"
msgstr "记忆的价格在 576 格或 14,880 格时超过了重量级的上限"

#: src/models/memory.md:224
msgid "Shrink the shape or the dtype, or enter a larger class"
msgstr "缩小形状或数据类型，或进入更大的重量级"

#: src/models/memory.md:225 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:95
msgid "`MEMORY_SHAPE`"
msgstr "`MEMORY_SHAPE`"

#: src/models/memory.md:225
msgid "Too many named dimensions, a name used twice, or a memory output without a dtype and a shape"
msgstr "命名维度过多、同一名字用了两次，或记忆输出缺少数据类型和形状"

#: src/models/memory.md:225
msgid "Declare it as the [two memories](#two-memories) show"
msgstr "按[两种记忆](#two-memories)所示的方式声明"

#: src/models/memory.md:226 src/reference/rejection-reasons.md:96
msgid "`MEMORY_ROUND_TRIP`"
msgstr "`MEMORY_ROUND_TRIP`"

#: src/models/memory.md:226
msgid "Fed its own memory, the model's call failed"
msgstr "喂回自己的记忆后，模型的调用失败了"

#: src/models/memory.md:226
msgid "Check that each memory input takes exactly what its output writes"
msgstr "检查每个记忆输入接受的正是其输出写出的内容"

#: src/models/memory.md:228
msgid "**The round trip chains the reference observations.** Admission plays them in order, and each call gets the memory the previous one wrote, whenever both observations are on the same board and the previous call answered. So a model that reads its memory wrongly fails admission, rather than striking on turn 1 of every match. A bug that shows only later in a match is not caught there: play a match on your machine to find it."
msgstr "**往返检查会把参考观测串联起来**。审核按顺序运行它们，只要前后两个观测在同一张地图上且上一次调用有应答，每次调用就会拿到上一次写出的记忆。所以读错自己记忆的模型会在审核时失败，而不是在每场对局的第 1 回合被判罚。只在对局后期才显现的 bug 在这里抓不到：在你自己的机器上打一场对局来找它。"

#: src/models/memory.md:234
msgid "One device"
msgstr "单一设备"

#: src/models/memory.md:236
msgid "Every runner executes models on the CPU, pinned in its configuration. Both seats of a match play on one runner, so no device can favour a seat, but a memory feeds a last-digit difference back into every later turn. Pinning the device keeps a match with memory reproducible, and it is also the faster choice for graphs of this size."
msgstr "每个运行器都在 CPU 上执行模型，这一点固定在它的配置里。一场对局的两个席位在同一个运行器上进行，所以没有哪个设备能偏袒某个席位；但记忆会把末位数字的差异带入之后的每一个回合。固定设备让带记忆的对局可以复现，而且对这种规模的计算图来说，这也是更快的选择。"

#: src/models/memory.md:241
msgid "Testing it"
msgstr "测试记忆"

#: src/models/memory.md:243
msgid "`tinybrains` carries memory under the same rules as a runner: [play a match](testing.md) and your seat gets its own memory back every turn. `tinybrains check` prints what your memory costs, fixed and per cell, and takes `--memory-flat-bytes` and `--memory-cell-bytes` to judge it against a class. `check` also runs the reference observations chained, as admission does. `tinybrains adapt` accepts an observation carrying `memory` or `ant_memory` as nested arrays or in the wire form, so a trainer can compare its tensors with the adapter's with the memory set ([Testing](testing.md#check-it-the-way-admission-will))."
msgstr "`tinybrains` 按与运行器相同的规则携带记忆：[打一场对局](testing.md)，你的席位每回合都会拿回自己的记忆。`tinybrains check` 会打印你的记忆开销，固定部分和每格部分各是多少，并接受 `--memory-flat-bytes` 和 `--memory-cell-bytes` 来对照某个重量级评判。`check` 也像审核那样串联运行参考观测。`tinybrains adapt` 接受带有 `memory` 或 `ant_memory` 的观测，既可以是嵌套数组，也可以是传输格式，所以训练器可以在设置了记忆的情况下比较自己的张量和适配器的张量（[测试](testing.md#check-it-the-way-admission-will)）。"

#: src/models/memory.md:251
msgid "One detail of the carry: a call that answers with a head the referee cannot read is a strike, but the memory it wrote is kept."
msgstr "携带规则的一个细节：如果一次调用返回的策略头裁判无法读取，那算一次判罚，但它写出的记忆会被保留。"

#: src/models/memory.md:254
msgid "A trainer carries its own memory in Python, under the same carry rules. A memory that is a fixed function of the observations, such as the scent above, trains with the loops you already have: the trainer computes the same planes in numpy and feeds them in. A memory the graph computes has to be trained in turn order, since each turn's memory is the graph's own output on the turn before: a recurrent network with truncated backpropagation through time, carrying between turns the rounded integer the runner will carry."
msgstr "训练器在 Python 里按同样的携带规则携带自己的记忆。如果记忆是观测的固定函数，比如上面的气味，用你已有的训练循环就能训练：训练器在 numpy 里算出同样的平面，再喂进去。由计算图计算的记忆则必须按回合顺序训练，因为每一回合的记忆都是计算图在上一回合的输出：这是一个用截断的时序反向传播训练的循环网络，在回合之间携带的是运行器将会携带的那个取整后的整数。"

#: src/models/memory.md:261
msgid "The platform's own baselines do both. `ants/baselines` trains any class with `--memory`, two planes of food seen and enemy hills seen kept with `Max`; its `train/seq.py` trains the same two planes as a gated update the optimiser shapes, and with `--ants` a row per ant that follows the ant by id, exactly as [above](#a-memory-per-ant). Its conformance test runs every memory adapter, the join by id included, through `tinybrains adapt`. Read its `README.md` for what each carried and what it was worth."
msgstr "平台自己的基线两种都做了。`ants/baselines` 用 `--memory` 训练任意重量级，带两个用 `Max` 保留的平面：见过的食物和见过的敌方蚁丘；它的 `train/seq.py` 把同样两个平面训练成由优化器塑造的门控更新，加上 `--ants` 后还有每只蚂蚁一行、按 id 跟随蚂蚁的记忆，与[上文](#a-memory-per-ant)完全一样。它的一致性测试通过 `tinybrains adapt` 运行每一个记忆适配器，包括按 id 的连接。各自携带了什么、又带来了多少收益，请读它的 `README.md`。"

#: src/models/testing.md:3
msgid "Test the **exact ONNX and manifest files** you will submit. Check the interface first, then the budget and timing, then the play: a graph that runs and an adapter that returns prove nothing about whether your entry plays valid or useful actions."
msgstr "测试的必须是**你将要提交的那两个 ONNX 和清单文件**。先检查接口，再检查预算和时间，最后检查实际对局：计算图能运行、适配器能返回，都不能证明你的参赛模型给出的动作是有效的或有用的。"

#: src/models/testing.md:7
msgid "Reference observations"
msgstr "参考观测"

#: src/models/testing.md:9
msgid "Admission probes every entry against the cartridge's **reference set**: 207 observations the engine generates, one for every seat of every [basic board](../games/ants/maps.md#the-basic-boards) at turns 20, 150 and 400 (or the last turn a match was still being played), on three seeds. They span boards from 24 × 24 to 120 × 124, two seats to eight, colonies from a seat with no ants left to twenty-nine ants, and opponents numbered up to 7. Every season's board must fit inside the limits the basic boards span, so a model admitted on them can play a board a season adds later. Admission plays the first sixty-four of them and nothing else, and anything they miss goes unchecked. The `tinybrains` commands below read the same file, all 207."
msgstr "审核用卡带的**参考集**探测每个参赛模型：由引擎生成的 207 个观测，覆盖每张[基础地图](../games/ants/maps.md#the-basic-boards)的每个席位，取第 20、150 和 400 回合（或对局仍在进行的最后一个回合），各用三个种子。它们涵盖从 24 × 24 到 120 × 124 的地图、两到八个席位、从一只蚂蚁都不剩到二十九只蚂蚁的蚁群，以及编号最高到 7 的对手。每个赛季的地图都必须落在基础地图所张成的限制之内，所以在它们上面通过审核的模型，也能在赛季之后新增的地图上对局。审核只运行其中前六十四个，别的一概不管，它们没覆盖到的情况就无人检查。下面的 `tinybrains` 命令读取的是同一个文件，全部 207 个。"

#: src/models/testing.md:18
msgid "Your own tests should cover what the set does not reach: colonies larger than thirty ants, and the positions your own entry plays into. A simple greedy walker played the set's matches, so no model chose any of its positions. Owners in `hills` and `foes` are [relative to you](observation.md#ownership-labels), so both seats of a match see the same encoding."
msgstr "你自己的测试应当覆盖参考集没触及的部分：超过三十只蚂蚁的蚁群，以及你自己的参赛模型会走入的局面。参考集的对局是由一个简单的贪心行走脚本打的，所以其中没有任何局面是模型选出来的。`hills` 和 `foes` 中的归属是[相对于你](observation.md#ownership-labels)的，所以一场对局的两个席位看到的编码是一样的。"

#: src/models/testing.md:23
msgid "The `tinybrains` CLI"
msgstr "`tinybrains` CLI"

#: src/models/testing.md:25
msgid "`tinybrains` is the platform's command-line tool: it plays matches on your machine and makes admission's own measurements without a server. **It links the two libraries a node links**, `datalogic-rs` for your manifest's adapters and `tract-onnx` for the graph, so it reports the numbers the platform will report."
msgstr "`tinybrains` 是平台的命令行工具：它在你的机器上打对局，并且不需要服务器就能做出审核所做的那些测量，而且**它链接的是节点所链接的那两个库**，处理清单中适配器的 `datalogic-rs` 和运行计算图的 `tract-onnx`，所以它报告的数字就是平台将会报告的数字。"

#: src/models/testing.md:30
msgid "It is one binary, [released](https://github.com/Tiny-Brains/cli/releases/latest) for macOS 26 or newer on Apple silicon and for Linux (glibc 2.35 or newer) and Windows on arm64 and x86-64, and it needs no other checkout. On macOS or Linux:"
msgstr "它是一个单独的二进制文件，[发布版本](https://github.com/Tiny-Brains/cli/releases/latest)覆盖 Apple 芯片上的 macOS 26 或更新版本，以及 arm64 和 x86-64 上的 Linux（glibc 2.35 或更新）和 Windows，不需要检出任何其他仓库。在 macOS 或 Linux 上："

#: src/models/testing.md:41
msgid "On Windows, or without Homebrew, download your platform's archive from the release (`tinybrains-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip`, `tinybrains-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz` and so on), check it against the release's `SHA256SUMS`, and put the binary inside on your `PATH`. With a Rust toolchain, `cargo install --locked --git https://github.com/Tiny-Brains/cli` builds the same binary from source."
msgstr "在 Windows 上，或者不用 Homebrew 的话，从发布版本下载你平台对应的压缩包（`tinybrains-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip`、`tinybrains-aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz` 等），用发布版本的 `SHA256SUMS` 核对它，再把里面的二进制文件放到你的 `PATH` 上。有 Rust 工具链的话，`cargo install --locked --git https://github.com/Tiny-Brains/cli` 会从源码构建出同一个二进制文件。"

#: src/models/testing.md:47
msgid "Every game has a starter kit, `<game>-starter`, with a trained entry, `train.py`, two match files and a `games.toml`. Run the CLI from there: it reads the game from a registry, looking for `$TINYBRAINS_REGISTRY`, then `games.toml` and `tinybrains.toml` in the directory you run it from, then `registry.toml` in its cache. The starter's copy pins a release of the cartridge by two digests, the archive's and the engine's. The first command that needs the game downloads it once into the CLI's cache (`~/Library/Caches/tinybrains/cartridges/` on macOS, `~/.cache/tinybrains/cartridges/` or `$XDG_CACHE_HOME` on Linux, `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\tinybrains\\cartridges` on Windows, or wherever `TINYBRAINS_HOME` points) and refuses it unless both digests match. Copy that file into any other repository and it works the same way there."
msgstr "每个游戏都有一个入门套件 `<game>-starter`，里面有一个训练好的参赛模型、`train.py`、两个对局文件和一个 `games.toml`。请在那里运行 CLI：它从注册表读取游戏，依次查找 `$TINYBRAINS_REGISTRY`，然后是运行目录下的 `games.toml` 和 `tinybrains.toml`，最后是其缓存中的 `registry.toml`。入门套件里的那份注册表用两个摘要（压缩包的和引擎的）固定了卡带的一个发布版本。第一个需要这个游戏的命令会把它下载一次到 CLI 的缓存中（macOS 上是 `~/Library/Caches/tinybrains/cartridges/`，Linux 上是 `~/.cache/tinybrains/cartridges/` 或 `$XDG_CACHE_HOME`，Windows 上是 `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\tinybrains\\cartridges`，或者 `TINYBRAINS_HOME` 指向的任何位置），并且只有两个摘要都匹配才会接受。把那个文件复制到任何别的仓库，它在那里也一样能用。"

#: src/models/testing.md:57
msgid "`tinybrains games` prints each registered game, where it comes from and its engine digest. Check it first when a local result disagrees with a ladder one."
msgstr "`tinybrains games` 会打印每个已注册的游戏、它的来源和引擎摘要。当本地结果与天梯上的结果不一致时，先检查这个。"

#: src/models/testing.md:60
msgid "Check it the way admission will"
msgstr "按审核的方式检查"

#: src/models/testing.md:66
msgid "`check` reads the graph from the protobuf, evaluates your manifest over the reference set and runs the graph on what the manifest produced. It prints the two hashes, the opset, the parameter count, the node count, the operators, the size metric, the worst operation count against the budget, and the slowest inference. It refuses what admission refuses on the document alone: an operator off the [allowlist](format.md#onnx-compatibility) is `OP_NOT_ALLOWED`, and an opset outside 13 to 19 is `OPSET`. Last it runs admission's probe as a node runs it: five inferences on zero-filled inputs at your `probe_dims`, whose median must fit the game's turn, 1,000 ms for Ants:"
msgstr "`check` 从 protobuf 读取计算图，在参考集上对你的清单求值，再用清单产出的张量运行计算图。它会打印两个哈希、opset、参数数量、节点数、所用算子、大小指标、相对预算的最坏操作数，以及最慢的一次推理。凡是审核仅凭文件本身就会拒绝的，它也拒绝：不在[允许列表](format.md#onnx-compatibility)中的算子是 `OP_NOT_ALLOWED`，13 到 19 之外的 opset 是 `OPSET`。最后它像节点那样运行审核的探测：在你的 `probe_dims` 下对全零输入做五次推理，其中位数必须在游戏的回合时限之内，Ants 是 1,000 ms："

#: src/models/testing.md:100
msgid "`--json` prints the run as one object, with `failing_case` naming the observation that failed, if one did. **A pass is necessary and not sufficient**: admission decides the size class against _your season's_ table, and your machine has no season. The admitting runner also measures the probe again on its own hardware, so a median close to the turn can pass here and fail there."
msgstr "`--json` 把这次运行打印成一个对象，如果有观测失败，`failing_case` 会指出是哪一个。不过**通过是必要条件，而非充分条件**：审核是对照<em>你所在赛季</em>的表来判定重量级的，而你的机器上没有赛季。审核运行器还会在自己的硬件上再测一次探测，所以接近回合时限的中位数可能在这里通过、在那里失败。"

#: src/models/testing.md:105
msgid "**A model with [memory](memory.md)** gets two more things from `check`. It prints what the memory costs, fixed and per cell, and the total at the smallest and the largest board. `--memory-flat-bytes N` and `--memory-cell-bytes N` judge that total against a class's two numbers (a number left out is 0), with the verdicts admission gives: `MEMORY_NOT_ALLOWED`, `MEMORY_TOO_LARGE` and `MEMORY_SHAPE`. The reference observations also run chained, as admission runs them: each call is fed the memory the call before it wrote, when both are the same size. A fed call that fails is `MEMORY_ROUND_TRIP`, and `check` names the observation it failed on."
msgstr "**带[记忆](memory.md)的模型**还能从 `check` 得到两样东西。它会打印记忆的开销，固定部分和每格部分各是多少，以及在最小和最大地图上的总量。`--memory-flat-bytes N` 和 `--memory-cell-bytes N` 用重量级的两个数字评判这个总量（省略的数字视为 0），给出的结论与审核相同：`MEMORY_NOT_ALLOWED`、`MEMORY_TOO_LARGE` 和 `MEMORY_SHAPE`。参考观测也会像审核那样串联运行：只要前后两个观测大小相同，每次调用就会被喂入上一次调用写出的记忆。被喂入记忆后失败的调用是 `MEMORY_ROUND_TRIP`，`check` 会指出它在哪个观测上失败。"

#: src/models/testing.md:113
msgid "See the tensors your adapter builds"
msgstr "查看适配器构建的张量"

#: src/models/testing.md:119
msgid "`adapt` evaluates every adapter through **datalogic** over every reference observation, and writes each input tensor as a numpy `.npy` file beside the observation that produced it:"
msgstr "`adapt` 通过 **datalogic** 在每个参考观测上对每个适配器求值，并把每个输入张量写成 numpy 的 `.npy` 文件，放在产生它的那个观测旁边："

#: src/models/testing.md:130
msgid "`--obs FILE` runs your own observations instead: one, a list of them, or `{\"observations\": [...]}`. An observation may carry `memory` or `ant_memory`, either as nested arrays, which are decoded into the dtype your manifest declares for that output, or in the wire form a runner hands back. So you can compare your trainer's tensors with the adapter's with the memory set."
msgstr "`--obs FILE` 改为运行你自己的观测：一个观测、一个观测列表，或者 `{\"observations\": [...]}`。观测可以带有 `memory` 或 `ant_memory`，既可以是嵌套数组（会按你清单为该输出声明的数据类型解码），也可以是运行器交回的传输格式。这样你就能在设置了记忆的情况下，比较训练器的张量和适配器的张量。"

#: src/models/testing.md:136
msgid "The ladder feeds your graph these same tensors. **Before you train, assert that your trainer's encoder produces the same ones**, element for element. If your encoder disagrees with the adapter, you train a model on inputs the arena never serves, and nothing fails: your rating comes out lower than training promised. [A real manifest](adapters/walkthrough.md#the-same-encoding-in-your-trainer) shows the test the platform's own baselines run."
msgstr "天梯喂给你计算图的正是这些张量，所以**训练之前，先断言你训练器的编码器产出的张量与之完全相同**，逐个元素一致。如果你的编码器和适配器不一致，你训练出的模型面对的输入在天梯上从不会出现，而且什么都不会报错：只是你的评分比训练时承诺的要低。[一个真实的清单](adapters/walkthrough.md#the-same-encoding-in-your-trainer)展示了平台自己的基线所运行的这项测试。"

#: src/models/testing.md:143
msgid "Play a match"
msgstr "打一场对局"

#: src/models/testing.md:146
msgid "# from a starter checkout\n"
msgstr "# 在入门套件的检出目录中\n"

#: src/models/testing.md:150
msgid "A match file names a model and a manifest for each seat. On your own machine, your entry can play the starter's trained opponents in `models/`, itself, or last week's version, through the real cartridge and the real evaluator. Each run prints the mean operations and inference per seat-turn, and the fraction of the turn the worst one used. `-v` prints each strike, forfeit, inference error and over-turn warning as it happens; `--timings` measures each phase of the run; `--out DIR` writes the replays somewhere other than `replays/`. `view` opens a replay in your browser with the match graph under it: each seat's ants alive, hills standing or score, turn by turn."
msgstr "对局文件为每个席位指定一个模型和一个清单。在你自己的机器上，你的参赛模型可以通过真实的卡带和真实的求值器，对战入门套件 `models/` 中训练好的对手、它自己，或者上周的版本。每次运行都会打印每席位回合的平均操作数和平均推理时间，以及最慢的一次占回合时限的比例。`-v` 会在判罚、判负、推理错误和超出回合时限的警告发生时逐条打印；`--timings` 测量运行的每个阶段；`--out DIR` 把回放写到 `replays/` 以外的地方。`view` 在浏览器中打开回放，下方附有对局图表：每个席位存活的蚂蚁、尚存的蚁丘或得分，逐回合显示。"

#: src/models/testing.md:158
msgid "Match files"
msgstr "对局文件"

