#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:163
msgid "**A board carries its own seat count**, because a seat count belongs to a board and the game has none of its own. The manifest declares no pool either: it names no board a season plays. `limits.boards` is what any board may be, and the platform reads it in one place, a season's upload. `maps` holds metadata and a digest per basic board, so a competitor's tooling can list the boards the release ships and check an exported copy without loading the component. `about` is plain text only: it comes from a repository, and a browser renders it."
msgstr "**地图自带席位数**，因为席位数属于地图，游戏本身没有自己的席位数。清单也不声明任何地图池：它不指定赛季要玩哪张地图。`limits.boards` 规定任何地图可以是什么样，平台只在一个地方读它，就是赛季的上传。`maps` 保存每张基础地图的元数据和摘要，这样参赛者的工具不用加载组件就能列出发布版本自带的地图，并核对导出的副本。`about` 只能是纯文本：它来自仓库，而由浏览器渲染。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:170
msgid "Generate registration facts from the definitions the engine uses, so board sizes and seat counts cannot drift, and ship the component and manifests together. Ants generates `cartridge.json` from its basic boards and derives `limits.boards` from them, so the bound and the boards that prove it cannot disagree. Its own GitHub Actions workflow builds the component, both manifests, the basic boards, the reference observations and the viewer, and publishes them as one release archive, which every consumer fetches by tag or as the latest."
msgstr "注册信息要从引擎所用的定义生成，这样地图尺寸和席位数就不会漂移；组件和清单要一起发布。Ants 从基础地图生成 `cartridge.json`，并由它们推导出 `limits.boards`，所以界限和证明它的地图不可能不一致。它自己的 GitHub Actions 工作流构建组件、两份清单、基础地图、参考观测和查看器，并把它们作为一个发布版本压缩包发布，每个使用方按标签或取最新版获取。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:177
msgid "Building the component"
msgstr "构建组件"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:179
msgid "Build a Rust `cdylib` on `orion-plugin-sdk` for `wasm32-unknown-unknown`, and turn it into a component with `wasm-tools component new`. **Do not target WASI**: its standard library imports WASI, and Orion would refuse the component. A refusal is a `PluginError` with a stable code matching `^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]{0,63}$` and a class: `caller_input` when the same input can never succeed, `internal` when the cartridge itself failed. Choose codes a caller can act on: `WAVE_STATE_CORRUPT` beats `ERROR`."
msgstr "基于 `orion-plugin-sdk` 构建一个面向 `wasm32-unknown-unknown` 的 Rust `cdylib`，再用 `wasm-tools component new` 把它转成组件。**不要以 WASI 为目标**：它的标准库会导入 WASI，Orion 会拒绝这样的组件。一次拒绝是一个 `PluginError`，带有一个符合 `^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]{0,63}$` 的稳定错误码和一个类别：同样的输入永远不可能成功时是 `caller_input`，卡带自身出错时是 `internal`。选择调用方能据以行动的错误码：`WAVE_STATE_CORRUPT` 胜过 `ERROR`。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:186
msgid "**Pin the toolchain and remap build paths.** rustc bakes into the binary the absolute path of every source file a panic can name, so the same commit, built on two machines, gives two engine digests. Ants builds its component in its GitHub `build` workflow on `ubuntu-24.04-arm`, with rustc pinned to a patch version in `rust-toolchain.toml`, wasm-tools pinned in `build.sh`, and `--remap-path-prefix`. The build host is part of the digest too, so a laptop's build is never the ladder's: every consumer takes the component from the Ants release and runs no build of its own."
msgstr "**锁定工具链并重映射构建路径**。rustc 会把 panic 可能提到的每个源文件的绝对路径烤进二进制文件，所以同一个提交在两台机器上构建，会得到两个引擎摘要。Ants 在它的 GitHub `build` 工作流里、在 `ubuntu-24.04-arm` 上构建组件，rustc 在 `rust-toolchain.toml` 里锁定到补丁版本，wasm-tools 在 `build.sh` 里锁定，并使用 `--remap-path-prefix`。构建主机同样是摘要的一部分，所以笔记本上的构建永远不是天梯的：每个使用方都从 Ants 的发布版本获取组件，自己不做任何构建。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:193
msgid "The ceilings"
msgstr "上限"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:195
msgid "Every invocation runs in a fresh instance under limits the operator sets. A manifest requests nothing, and a per-plugin override may only lower a ceiling."
msgstr "每次调用都在一个全新的实例里运行，受运维方设定的限制约束。清单不能请求任何资源，而按插件的覆盖设置只能调低上限。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:198
msgid "Ceiling"
msgstr "上限"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:198
msgid "Default"
msgstr "默认值"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:198
msgid "What it bounds"
msgstr "限制的是什么"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:200
msgid "`max_memory_bytes`"
msgstr "`max_memory_bytes`"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:200
msgid "Linear memory per invocation"
msgstr "每次调用的线性内存"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:201
msgid "`max_timeout_ms`"
msgstr "`max_timeout_ms`"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:201
msgid "5,000"
msgstr "5,000"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:201
msgid "Wall clock; the task's own deadline applies too, and the shorter wins"
msgstr "实际耗时；任务自身的时限同样生效，以较短者为准"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:202
msgid "`max_request_bytes`"
msgstr "`max_request_bytes`"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:202 src/platform/adding-a-game.md:203
msgid "1 MiB"
msgstr "1 MiB"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:202
msgid "The evaluated input, and so the wave size"
msgstr "求值的输入，也就限制了波次的大小"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:203
msgid "`max_response_bytes`"
msgstr "`max_response_bytes`"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:203
msgid "The returned JSON"
msgstr "返回的 JSON"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:204
msgid "`max_concurrency_per_function`"
msgstr "`max_concurrency_per_function`"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:204
msgid "64"
msgstr "64"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:204
msgid "Invocations of one function at once"
msgstr "同一函数的并发调用数"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:205
msgid "`fuel_backstop`"
msgstr "`fuel_backstop`"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:205
msgid "10¹¹ instructions"
msgstr "10¹¹ 条指令"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:205
msgid "A backstop sized well above what the clock admits, and no contract"
msgstr "一道兜底，远高于时限内所能执行的量，不构成契约"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:207
msgid "**Orion retries a timeout and no other failure**, because a pure function retries for free. It retries no `caller_input` or `internal` refusal, trap, panic, size limit or non-JSON result. Cache nothing across calls: nothing survives from one call to the next."
msgstr "**Orion 只重试超时，不重试其他任何失败**，因为纯函数重试没有代价。它不重试 `caller_input` 或 `internal` 拒绝、trap、panic、超出大小限制或非 JSON 的结果。不要跨调用缓存任何东西：没有什么能从一次调用留到下一次。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:211
msgid "Signing"
msgstr "签名"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:213
msgid "**Components carry signatures, and Orion enforces them.** Every plugin carries a detached Ed25519 signature over its digest string (`sha256:<64 hex>`). Whoever holds the deployment's trust key mints it; the package does not. Orion checks it when you upload the component and again on every node that loads it, and a missing or mismatched signature quarantines the channels that call the component, and the node stops at its boot apply. Sign a new game's component the same way, and re-sign it on every rebuild, because a rebuild changes the digest."
msgstr "**组件带有签名，而且 Orion 会强制校验**。每个插件都带有一个对其摘要字符串（`sha256:<64 hex>`）的分离式 Ed25519 签名。签名由持有该部署信任密钥的人签发，而不是由包签发。Orion 在你上传组件时检查它，在每个加载它的节点上再检查一次；签名缺失或不匹配会把调用该组件的频道隔离，节点也会在启动应用包时停下。新游戏的组件要以同样方式签名，并且每次重新构建后都要重新签名，因为重新构建会改变摘要。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:220
msgid "Registering and integrating"
msgstr "注册与集成"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:222
msgid "Load the component on compatible Kalam workers, register its manifest and engine digest, and supply reference observations for admission. Update the execution function references, the component Soma loads to judge uploaded boards, and the deployment wiring wherever they name Ants. Align the game's live season identity with the engine that will claim its matches."
msgstr "在兼容的 Kalam 工作节点上加载组件，注册它的清单和引擎摘要，并为审核提供参考观测。凡是写着 Ants 的地方都要更新：执行函数的引用、Soma 用来评判上传地图的组件，以及部署接线。让游戏当前赛季的标识与将要认领其对局的引擎保持一致。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:227
msgid "Provide reference cases covering the smallest and largest states and the boundary conditions that matter, and **generate them from the engine**. Admission validates an adapter against these observations and nothing else, so a hand-kept set tests a shape the game may no longer produce. Validate a real model and adapter against them: an empty or unrepresentative reference set gives admission nothing to hold an adapter to."
msgstr "提供覆盖最小与最大状态以及关键边界条件的参考用例，并且**从引擎生成它们**。审核只用这些观测来验证适配器，别无其他，所以手工维护的集合测试的可能是游戏早已不再产生的形状。用真实的模型和适配器对它们做验证：空的或没有代表性的参考集，会让审核没有任何依据去约束适配器。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:233
msgid "The viewer"
msgstr "查看器"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:235
msgid "The viewer is the one part of a cartridge outside the component: an ES module the platform loads by convention from `/cartridges/{slug}/viz.js`. It exports `mount(target, replay, opts)`, which returns an object with a `destroy()`. Ants' viewer takes a `tier` (the whole stage, a player, a card's tile or a thumbnail), `turn`, a `from`/`to` range, `autoplay`, `speed`, `theme`, `labels` (what the host calls each seat) and an `onTurn` callback, among others, and exports `drawFrame`, `mountGraph` and `mountMap` beside `mount`."
msgstr "查看器是卡带中唯一位于组件之外的部分：一个 ES 模块，平台按约定从 `/cartridges/{slug}/viz.js` 加载它。它导出 `mount(target, replay, opts)`，返回一个带 `destroy()` 的对象。Ants 的查看器接受的选项包括 `tier`（整个舞台、播放器、卡片里的小块或缩略图）、`turn`、`from`/`to` 范围、`autoplay`、`speed`、`theme`、`labels`（宿主给每个席位的称呼）和 `onTurn` 回调等，并在 `mount` 之外还导出 `drawFrame`、`mountGraph` 和 `mountMap`。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:242
msgid "**The viewer re-simulates through your own `replay-decode`**, transpiled with `jco` from the same component digest that recorded the match, so the viewer and the referee cannot disagree. A JavaScript re-implementation of a rule would be a second engine. Record the digest you built the bundle from: a viewer re-simulating with a different engine raises no error and draws a plausible match that never happened. **A viewer never runs a model.** It replays recorded actions, so a host can embed it anywhere without inheriting the evaluator's security surface."
msgstr "**查看器通过你自己的 `replay-decode` 重新模拟**，它用 `jco` 从记录这场对局的同一个组件摘要转译而来，所以查看器和裁判不可能有分歧。用 JavaScript 重新实现一条规则就等于第二个引擎。记下你构建打包文件所用的摘要：用不同引擎重新模拟的查看器不会报任何错误，只会画出一场看似合理却从未发生过的对局。**查看器从不运行模型**。它只回放记录下来的动作，所以宿主可以把它嵌到任何地方，而不必继承求值器的安全暴露面。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:249
msgid "Ants ships the whole player (transport, timeline, title bar), because its three hosts are separate applications: the web application, this book and `tinybrains view`. The cost: a second cartridge writes its own scrubber, until two real viewers show what is worth extracting. A viewer owes its host page these rules:"
msgstr "Ants 把整个播放器（播放控件、时间轴、标题栏）一并发布，因为它的三个宿主是各自独立的应用：网站、本书和 `tinybrains view`。代价是：第二个卡带得自己写进度条，直到有了两个真实的查看器，才看得出什么值得抽出来共用。查看器对它的宿主页面要遵守这些规则："

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:254
msgid "**Scope every style rule to your root class.** A viewer injects one stylesheet into the host document; an unscoped rule lands on the host's own elements."
msgstr "**把每条样式规则都限定在你的根类名之下**。查看器会向宿主文档注入一份样式表；没有限定范围的规则会落到宿主自己的元素上。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:256
msgid "**Take the chrome's colours from the host's tokens, and keep the board's.** A match should look like itself in either theme."
msgstr "**界面外框的颜色取自宿主的设计令牌，地图的颜色保持自己的**。一场对局在两种主题下都应该看起来是它自己。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:258
msgid "**Give the board the frame.** A host embeds a viewer at whatever height it can spare, so anything permanent beside the board has to earn its height."
msgstr "**把画面留给地图**。宿主只会用它能匀出的高度来嵌入查看器，所以地图旁边任何常驻的东西都得配得上它占的高度。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:260
msgid "**Take the layout question yourself.** If a host needs another layout, give it an option on `mount()`; the host's stylesheet never reaches into your class names."
msgstr "**布局问题由你自己承担**。如果宿主需要另一种布局，就在 `mount()` 上给它一个选项；宿主的样式表永远不会伸进你的类名里。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:262
msgid "**Take the width the host gives you.** Anything that does not wrap becomes the viewer's minimum width; `contain: inline-size` on the root keeps content from sizing the host's column."
msgstr "**接受宿主给你的宽度**。任何不换行的东西都会变成查看器的最小宽度；在根元素上设置 `contain: inline-size`，内容就不会反过来决定宿主那一栏的宽度。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:265
msgid "What a game must not need"
msgstr "游戏不得需要的东西"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:267
msgid "If adding your game needs any of these, raise it; do not work around it. The seam is worth having only while it holds."
msgstr "如果添加你的游戏需要下面任何一项，请提出来，不要绕过去。这条分界线只有守得住才有价值。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:272
msgid "A change to the five functions"
msgstr "改动五个函数"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:272
msgid "The set is the ABI; a sixth function is a design conversation"
msgstr "这组函数就是 ABI；第六个函数是一场设计讨论"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:273
msgid "Floating-point game state"
msgstr "浮点数的游戏状态"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:273
msgid "It breaks replays before it breaks anything else"
msgstr "它最先弄坏的就是回放"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:274
msgid "State held between invocations"
msgstr "在两次调用之间保留状态"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:274
msgid "There is nowhere to put it; thread it through the wave state"
msgstr "没有地方可放；把它穿在波次状态里传递"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:275
msgid "I/O of any kind"
msgstr "任何形式的 I/O"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:275
msgid "Nothing in a cartridge may read a file, a clock, a socket or a secret"
msgstr "卡带里的任何东西都不得读取文件、时钟、套接字或密钥"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:276
msgid "Knowledge of ratings, classes, users or seasons"
msgstr "了解评分、重量级、用户或赛季"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:276
msgid "You score a match and rank its players; the platform does the rest"
msgstr "你给对局计分并给玩家排名次；其余交给平台"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:277
msgid "A per-match step function"
msgstr "按单场对局的 step 函数"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:277
msgid "It would cost the wave its batching"
msgstr "它会让波次失去批处理"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:278
msgid "Your own tensor layout"
msgstr "你自己的张量布局"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:278
msgid "The competitor's manifest turns a payload into tensors"
msgstr "参赛者的清单负责把观测数据变成张量"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:280
msgid "Documentation competitors need"
msgstr "参赛者需要的文档"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:282
msgid "Publish a game overview, a world description, the exact turn order, the ending and scoring rules, the limits a board may be, the observation schema, the action schema and working examples. Give what a model cannot see the same care as what it can. State the exact limits and the exact behavior of an invalid action. **Ants publishes its protocol in this book**: _What your model sees_ and _What your model answers_ are the contract, and a change to what the engine sends lands with a change to them."
msgstr "发布游戏概览、世界描述、精确的回合顺序、结束与计分规则、地图的限制范围、观测结构、动作结构以及可运行的示例。对模型看不到的东西，要和看得到的东西一样用心。写明精确的限制，以及无效动作的精确行为。**Ants 把它的协议发布在本书里**：<em>模型看到什么</em>和<em>模型回答什么</em>就是契约，引擎发送内容的改动必须连同它们的改动一起落地。"

#: src/platform/adding-a-game.md:289
msgid "If a visual explanation helps, reserve a replay visualiser placeholder that names the concept, the player perspective it needs and the turns to select. Attach real recorded games later, with matching engine identities and text captions. A competitor should understand the rule from the text before anyone implements the viewer."
msgstr "如果配图解释有帮助，先预留一个回放可视化占位，写明它要说明的概念、需要的玩家视角和要选取的回合。之后再附上真实录制的对局，带上相匹配的引擎标识和文字说明。在任何人实现查看器之前，参赛者就应该能从文字读懂规则。"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:3
msgid "A useful contribution makes competition easier to understand, enter, run or verify. Start by finding the [repository](repositories.md) that owns the behavior, then read its README, its source and the relevant tests. The application repositories are separate Git checkouts, even when you develop them under one parent directory."
msgstr "有用的贡献让比赛更容易理解、参加、运行或验证。先找到拥有这个行为的[仓库](repositories.md)，然后读它的 README、源码和相关测试。各应用仓库是彼此独立的 Git 检出，即使你把它们放在同一个父目录下开发也是如此。"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:8
msgid "Where things are written"
msgstr "各类内容写在哪里"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:10
msgid "What it holds"
msgstr "包含什么"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:12
msgid "This section"
msgstr "本章节"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:12
msgid "How the platform is built, at the level of its parts and their contracts"
msgstr "平台如何构成，到各个部件及其契约的层面"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:13
msgid "A repository's `README.md`"
msgstr "仓库的 `README.md`"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:13
msgid "How to run, configure, operate and release it; its layout, its invariants and its known gaps"
msgstr "如何运行、配置、运维和发布它；它的目录布局、不变量和已知缺口"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:14
msgid "A repository's `CLAUDE.md`"
msgstr "仓库的 `CLAUDE.md`"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:14
msgid "The checks to run after a change, and the rules and pitfalls the code does not state"
msgstr "改动之后要运行的检查，以及代码本身没有说明的规则和陷阱"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:15
msgid "The source"
msgstr "源码"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:15
msgid "Everything else: statements, workflow descriptions and comments are the specification"
msgstr "其余一切：SQL 语句、工作流描述和注释就是规范"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:17
msgid "The platform keeps no decision log and no status log. A repository's **Known gaps** section is its open work: keep it current in the change that opens or closes a gap. Verify a claim against the current producer and consumer before you copy it into code or docs. For a user-visible change, describe what the competitor does and what they then see, as well as the internal component involved."
msgstr "平台不保留决策记录，也不保留状态日志。仓库的 **Known gaps**（已知缺口）一节就是它的待办工作：在打开或关闭一个缺口的那次改动里把它更新到最新。在把一个说法写进代码或文档之前，先对照当前的生产方和消费方核实它。对用户可见的改动，要描述参赛者做了什么、随后看到什么，以及涉及的内部组件。"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:23
msgid "Every repository commits straight to `main`; there are no feature branches."
msgstr "每个仓库都直接提交到 `main`；没有功能分支。"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:25
msgid "Source conventions"
msgstr "源码约定"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:27
msgid "**Soma's and Kalam's packages are committed whole**, and you edit the committed files: there is no generator and nothing to regenerate. The built plugins and Ants' artifacts stay out of git and ship in each repository's image, or, for Ants, its GitHub release."
msgstr "**Soma 和 Kalam 的包是整个提交的**，你直接编辑提交的文件：没有生成器，也没有什么需要重新生成。构建出的插件和 Ants 的构建产物不进 git，而是随各自仓库的镜像发布，Ants 则随它的 GitHub 发布版本发布。"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:31
msgid "**Publishing an Ants release updates the engine Kalam plays**: Kalam's image takes the component from Ants' latest release, or the tag `ANTS_RELEASE` names, and vendors no copy. A local rebuild reaches a Kalam image only when you build it with `--build-context ants=<an ants dist/>`. Any source edit to the component changes its digest, comments included. Prove a refactor with artifact diffs and per-turn output hashes, since the wasm itself changes, and re-sign the plugins after."
msgstr "**发布一个 Ants 发布版本就是在更新 Kalam 所玩的引擎**：Kalam 的镜像从 Ants 的最新发布版本、或 `ANTS_RELEASE` 指定的标签获取组件，自己不内置副本。本地重新构建的结果只有在你用 `--build-context ants=<an ants dist/>` 构建 Kalam 镜像时才会进入镜像。对组件源码的任何改动都会改变它的摘要，注释也不例外。既然 wasm 本身会变，重构就要用产物差异和逐回合输出哈希来证明，之后再重新给插件签名。"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:37
msgid "Put schema changes in Soma's two migration files, and rewrite them in place while the schema is pre-release; then check every consuming package. Keep deployment addresses and credentials in configuration. Lint definitions with the pinned Orion version, because another version can report misleading compatibility failures."
msgstr "数据库模式的改动放进 Soma 的两个迁移文件，在模式尚未正式发布期间就地重写它们；然后检查每一个使用它的包。部署地址和凭据放在配置里。用锁定的 Orion 版本对定义做 lint，因为别的版本可能报出误导性的兼容性错误。"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:42
msgid "Checks that matter"
msgstr "重要的检查"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:44
msgid "Run the checks for the repository and the boundary you changed:"
msgstr "运行你改动的仓库和边界所对应的检查："

#: src/platform/contributing.md:46
msgid "Area"
msgstr "范围"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:46
msgid "Existing checks, from that repository's root"
msgstr "现有的检查，在该仓库根目录运行"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:48
msgid "Docs"
msgstr "文档"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:48
msgid "`mdbook build`; `tutorials/build.sh`, whose digest check refuses a replay the vendored viewer would draw wrong"
msgstr "`mdbook build`；`tutorials/build.sh`，它的摘要检查会拒绝内置查看器画不对的回放"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:49
msgid "`./build.sh`: the determinism check, `cargo test` in `engine/` and `mapgen/`, then every artifact into `dist/`; `viz/build.sh` for the viewer; `tools/equivalence.py` plays a release against the checkout turn by turn"
msgstr "`./build.sh`：确定性检查、`engine/` 和 `mapgen/` 里的 `cargo test`，然后把每个产物输出到 `dist/`；`viz/build.sh` 构建查看器；`tools/equivalence.py` 逐回合比对发布版本与检出"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:50
msgid "Soma plugins"
msgstr "Soma 插件"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:50
msgid "`cargo test --manifest-path plugins/Cargo.toml`, both crates"
msgstr "`cargo test --manifest-path plugins/Cargo.toml`，两个 crate 都要跑"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:51
msgid "Soma, Kalam definitions"
msgstr "Soma、Kalam 的定义"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:51
msgid "`./scripts/check-defs.sh` in both: the names and tags, clippy and fmt on the definitions, and every workflow's offline cases; Soma's `./scripts/check-sql.sh` and `./scripts/verify/run.sh`"
msgstr "两个仓库里的 `./scripts/check-defs.sh`：名称和标签、对定义的 clippy 和 fmt，以及每个工作流的离线用例；Soma 的 `./scripts/check-sql.sh` 和 `./scripts/verify/run.sh`"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:52
msgid "`npm run lint` and `npm run build`"
msgstr "`npm run lint` 和 `npm run build`"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:53
msgid "The stack"
msgstr "整个栈"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:53
msgid "web's `./scripts/check/configs.sh`, and a representative end-to-end flow on web's compose stack with a Kalam runner (`scripts/dev/submission-storm.py`)"
msgstr "web 的 `./scripts/check/configs.sh`，以及在 web 的 compose 栈上配合一个 Kalam 运行器跑一遍有代表性的端到端流程（`scripts/dev/submission-storm.py`）"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:54
msgid "CLI"
msgstr "CLI"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:54
msgid "`cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --locked --release -- -D warnings`, `cargo test --locked --release`, the starter kit's match played with the build, and `tinybrains conform` on the replay Kalam wrote that the repository keeps under `fixtures/`"
msgstr "`cargo fmt --check`、`cargo clippy --locked --release -- -D warnings`、`cargo test --locked --release`，用这次构建打一遍入门套件的对局，并对仓库保存在 `fixtures/` 下、由 Kalam 写出的回放运行 `tinybrains conform`"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:56
msgid "`check/configs.sh` spans repositories: it asserts the constants that must be equal on both sides of a boundary (the engine digest against what the season and each replica name, the model prefix, the adapter budget and the Orion version)."
msgstr "`check/configs.sh` 横跨多个仓库：它断言边界两侧必须相等的常量（引擎摘要与赛季及每个副本所指定的值、模型前缀、适配器预算和 Orion 版本）。"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:60
msgid "The SQL checks create disposable scratch databases and verify shipped statements; they prove nothing about live scheduling or concurrency. The configuration checks can skip runtime parsing when the required image is missing. `tinybrains conform` keeps the CLI's match loop and Kalam's workflow in agreement, and it needs a replay to run against. Report what ran, including those limits."
msgstr "SQL 检查会创建一次性的临时数据库并验证随包发布的语句；它们对线上的调度或并发什么也证明不了。所需镜像缺失时，配置检查可能会跳过运行时解析。`tinybrains conform` 让 CLI 的对局循环与 Kalam 的工作流保持一致，它需要一个回放来运行。报告时写明跑了什么，包括这些局限。"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:65
msgid "Exercise an API contract change through the HTTP workflow. A game or adapter change needs behavioral examples. A replay change needs a reconstruction from a real stored envelope; an engine-internal fixture is not enough. Use a local stack for integration evidence where unit checks cannot establish the result."
msgstr "API 契约的改动要通过 HTTP 工作流实际演练。游戏或适配器的改动需要行为示例。回放的改动需要从真实存储的封包做一次重建；引擎内部的测试夹具不够。单元检查无法确定结果时，用本地栈来取得集成证据。"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:70
msgid "Writing documentation"
msgstr "撰写文档"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:72
msgid "Address competitors first: what they need to build, what the platform checks, what they can observe, and what to do next. Keep architecture in this platform section unless it explains a practical limitation, and keep it at the level of parts and contracts: the source is the specification. Label planned tools as planned, and never describe a design proposal as a working endpoint. Write what is true now, and leave out what used to be."
msgstr "先面向参赛者：他们需要构建什么、平台检查什么、他们能观察到什么，以及接下来做什么。架构内容留在这个平台章节里，除非它解释的是某个实际的限制；并且保持在部件与契约的层面：源码才是规范。规划中的工具要标明是规划中的，绝不要把设计提案写成可用的接口。写现在为真的事，略去曾经如何。"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:78
msgid "Use relative links within the book, and keep `src/SUMMARY.md` aligned with the pages. A replay placeholder states the behavior it will illustrate and keeps a text explanation. Record real replay and engine identities once you have the assets, and never invent a game result to fill an example slot."
msgstr "书内使用相对链接，并让 `src/SUMMARY.md` 与页面保持一致。回放占位要说明它将要展示的行为，并保留文字解释。拿到素材之后再记录真实的回放和引擎标识，绝不要编造对局结果来填充示例位置。"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:83
msgid "Opening a change"
msgstr "提交改动"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:85
msgid "Explain the concrete problem and the behavior after the change, list the contracts it touches, and give the checks that support it. Include generated or vendored output where the change needs it, and update the competitor-facing documentation in the same change. For a cross-repository change, name the companion revisions it needs and the deployment order, so reviewers can assess a consistent set of artifacts."
msgstr "说明具体的问题和改动后的行为，列出它触及的契约，并给出支持它的检查。改动需要时，附上生成或内置的输出，并在同一次改动里更新面向参赛者的文档。跨仓库的改动要写明它需要的配套修订和部署顺序，好让评审者能评估一组一致的产物。"

#: src/platform/contributing.md:91
msgid "A report gives the relevant version or match ID, the expected and the observed behavior, and steps to reproduce it. Leave out session cookies and deployment credentials. Keep the failing input or replay where you can, so whoever fixes it can verify the fix against the original problem."
msgstr "问题报告要给出相关的版本或对局 ID、预期与实际观察到的行为，以及复现步骤。不要附上会话 cookie 和部署凭据。尽可能保留导致失败的输入或回放，这样修复的人就能对照原始问题验证修复。"
